{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793872911773,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab285c47002qXGYgs3hDRZ5JV","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2856b40016qeCsuxxGczF1Z","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfd58435b67a0b6e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml","offset":190,"limit":420},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml, lines 190-609\n190:       immediately after artifact resolution and before fan-out so old packet files\n191:       cannot be merged with fresh lineage outputs. A restart request must never\n192:       fall back to auto-resume. In auto mode, the explicit restart flag is operator\n193:       authorization to archive the resolved review packet, so do not ask for a\n194:       second confirmation. Rollback is to move the timestamped archive back to\n195:       the packet directory.\n196:     command: \"if [ -d \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\" ]; then mkdir -p \\\"{state_paths.archive_root}\\\" && mv \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\" \\\"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\\\"; fi; mkdir -p \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\"\"\n197:     outputs:\n198:       - archived_path: \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug} when a prior packet existed, else null\"\n199:       - lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n200:     on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL; do not continue as resume or auto.\"\n201: \n202:   step_fanout_spawn:\n203:     description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n204:     skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n205:     instructions: |\n206:       Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own\n207:       isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n208:       This step runs before phase_init, so pass the raw review_focus. fanout-run.cjs\n209:       normalizes it and hands every lineage the same single-line text. Escape any double\n210:       quote, backslash, dollar sign or backtick in it for the shell, and pass an empty\n211:       string when no focus was given.\n212:       A cli-opencode lineage inside this fan-out is an explicit parallel-detached OpenCode\n213:       session with a separate lineage directory and session id; it is not the single-executor\n214:       self-invocation path. fanout-run.cjs owns the stack-only recursion guard for that\n215:       first-level detached lineage and still blocks recursive same-kind dispatch from inside it.\n216:       fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the\n217:       deep/review command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n218:       deep-review agent is used only for individual iterations, never as a full-loop\n219:       sub-agent or pasted phase-running prompt.\n220:       After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n221:       phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n222:       phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n223:     sub_steps:\n224:       step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n225:         description: \"Spawn all native and CLI lineages in capped worker pool\"\n226:         skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n227:         command: |\n228:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs \\\n229:             --spec-folder {spec_folder} \\\n230:             --loop-type review \\\n231:             --review-focus \"{review_focus}\" \\\n232:             --fanout-config-json '{config.fanout_json}' \\\n233:             --base-artifact-dir {artifact_dir} \\\n234:             --convergence-threshold {convergence_threshold} \\\n235:             --stop-policy {stop_policy} \\\n236:             --convergence-mode {convergence_mode}\n237:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n238:         wait_for_completion: true\n239: \n240:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n241:   # PHASE 1: INITIALIZATION\n242:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n243:   phase_init:\n244:     purpose: Create all state files for the review session and resolve review scope\n245:     steps:\n246: \n247:       step_preflight_contract:\n248:         action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n249:         verify:\n250:           - required_values_present: [review_target, review_target_type, review_dimensions, spec_folder, lineage_mode, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, stop_policy]\n251:           - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n252:           - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n253:           - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n254:         on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n255: \n256:       step_create_directories:\n257:         action: \"Create spec folder and canonical review packet directories if they don't exist\"\n258:         command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n259: \n260:       step_detect_resource_map:\n261:         action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist coverage-gate state\"\n262:         inspect:\n263:           - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n264:         classify:\n265:           present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n266:           absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n267:         outputs:\n268:           - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n269:           - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: concise resource-map snapshot for Known Context and charter framing. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n270: \n271:       step_migrate_legacy_review_state:\n272:         action: \"Rehome legacy review artifacts into review/iterations before session classification\"\n273:         detect:\n274:           canonical_review_state:\n275:             - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n276:             - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n277:             - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n278:             - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n279:           legacy_review_state:\n280:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json\"\n281:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n282:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n283:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n284:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md\"\n285:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause\"\n286:             - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n287:             - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report}\"\n288:           legacy_review_markers:\n289:             - \"scratch/deep-review-strategy.md exists\"\n290:             - \"scratch/deep-research-config.json declares mode == 'review' OR scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl contains mode == 'review'\"\n291:         migrate_only:\n292:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json -> {state_paths.config}\"\n293:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl -> {state_paths.state_log}\"\n294:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md -> {state_paths.strategy}\"\n295:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md -> {state_paths.dashboard}\"\n296:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n297:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause -> {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\"\n298:           - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n299:           - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report} -> {state_paths.review_output}\"\n300:         on_canonical_present: \"Leave canonical review/ state untouched and do not overwrite it with legacy scratch artifacts.\"\n301:         on_legacy_detected: \"Move only the review-specific whitelist, print LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED and leave unrelated scratch files untouched. Nothing is appended here: an append before session classification would create the state log and turn a fresh packet into a partial one, and the moved state log was written without the ledger, so the gateway refuses every append to it until step_classify_session.on_moved_legacy_state adopts it.\"\n302:         on_conflict: \"If canonical review/ state and legacy scratch review state both exist but disagree, halt for operator repair instead of merging contradictory state.\"\n303:         outputs:\n304:           - legacy_migration_detected: \"true when the command printed LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED, else false\"\n305:           - migration_recorded: \"false; step_record_artifact_migration sets it once the migration row is appended\"\n306:         command: |\n307:           mkdir -p {state_paths.iteration_dir}\n308:           if [ ! -e {state_paths.config} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.state_log} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.strategy} ] && [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && ( [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] || [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] ); then\n309:             [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json {state_paths.config}\n310:             [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl {state_paths.state_log}\n311:             [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md {state_paths.strategy}\n312:             [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md {state_paths.dashboard}\n313:             find {spec_folder}/scratch -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\;\n314:             [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\n315:             [ -e {state_paths.legacy_root_report} ] && mv {state_paths.legacy_root_report} {state_paths.review_output}\n316:             echo \"LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED\"\n317:           fi\n318:           find {state_paths.local_packet_dir} -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\; 2>/dev/null || true\n319: \n320:       step_acquire_lock:\n321:         action: \"Acquire the single-writer advisory lock before session classification\"\n322:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs acquire --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --packet-id {spec_folder} --ttl-ms 1800000\"\n323:         on_acquire: \"Capture lock.ownerPid as captured_owner_pid and lock.acquireNonce as captured_acquire_nonce from the JSON output, and reuse both for every release below. If acquired=false, fail closed — another deep-review run already holds this packet.\"\n324:         note: \"Uses the promoted runtime/ loop-lock CLI (single source of truth: stale-lock reclaim, clean owner-scoped release). macOS/BSD locking is advisory — best-effort single-writer, not a hard mutex across host calls. Acquire reclaims a stale lock itself and reports the old holder under `reclaimed`. A lock is stale when its heartbeat is older than twice its TTL, or when its owning process is known to be dead. No confirmation step exists in either mode: log a `reclaimed` holder and continue.\"\n325:         # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n326:         # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n327:         on_halt:\n328:           action: \"Release the lock before any terminal halt branch returns control\"\n329:           applies_to: [\"step_classify_session.on_invalid_state\", \"step_classify_session.on_completed_session\"]\n330:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; failures here are logged but do not block the halt\"\n331:         on_cancel:\n332:           action: \"Release the lock on user cancel or pause-sentinel detection before sentinel processing\"\n333:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; cancel completes regardless of cleanup result\"\n334:         on_workflow_exit:\n335:           action: \"Release the lock as the final step of any workflow exit path (success or failure)\"\n336:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; idempotent — safe to invoke when already released\"\n337: \n338:       step_classify_session:\n339:         action: \"Classify the session before writing files\"\n340:         inspect:\n341:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n342:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n343:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n344:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n345:         classify:\n346:           fresh: \"None of the three state artifacts exist\"\n347:           resume: \"Config, JSONL, and strategy all exist and config.mode == 'review' and agree on target/spec folder\"\n348:           completed-session: \"Resume artifacts exist and config.status == 'complete'\"\n349:           invalid-state: \"Any partial, missing, or contradictory combination\"\n350:         outputs:\n351:           - session_state: \"fresh | resume | completed-session | invalid-state\"\n352:           - prior_tail_digest: \"sha256 of the state log bytes when resuming or restarting an existing lineage\"\n353:         lifecycle_routing:\n354:           - \"If lineage_mode == restart and session_state is resume or completed-session, execute on_restart before on_resume or on_completed_session.\"\n355:           - \"If lineage_mode == auto or lineage_mode == resume, preserve the existing resume/completed/fresh behavior.\"\n356:         on_resume:\n357:           before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n358:           log: \"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent. Continue the same lineage (sessionId unchanged, generation unchanged, no archive).\"\n359:           append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n360:           skip_to: phase_loop\n361:         on_restart:\n362:           action: \"Archive the current review packet under the root-level review-archive/ tree and start a new lineage segment with a fresh sessionId and generation+1.\"\n363:           command: \"if [ -d {state_paths.packet_dir} ]; then mkdir -p {state_paths.archive_root} && mv {state_paths.packet_dir} {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}; fi\"\n364:           set:\n365:             lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n366:             parent_session_id: \"{prior_session_id}\"\n367:             generation: \"{prior_generation + 1}\"\n368:           skip_to: step_create_config\n369:         note_deferred_branches: \"fork and completed-continue are deferred and no longer runtime-supported in this release. The reducer still reads `lineageMode` from config for dashboards and analysis, but only `new`, `resume`, and `restart` are live. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n370:         on_moved_legacy_state:\n371:           applies_when: \"legacy_migration_detected == true and the branch taken resumes the session or goes to synthesis; never on restart or cancel\"\n372:           order: \"Runs after classification and before that branch appends anything, the resume event included.\"\n373:           note: |\n374:             The state log moved out of scratch/ was written by hand before the ledger existed, so the\n375:             gateway refuses every append to it. Set it aside unchanged as deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl,\n376:             open the run from the moved config, then replay its iteration rows through the gateway,\n377:             which carries each one whole. Rows the gateway cannot carry stay only in the set-aside file,\n378:             and the replay reports how many. Exit 2 from any of the three is a halt.\n379:           set_aside_command: |\n380:             STATE_LOG=\"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n381:             LEGACY_LOG=\"$(dirname \"$STATE_LOG\")/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\"\n382:             if [ -e \"$LEGACY_LOG\" ]; then\n383:               echo \"A set-aside legacy state log already exists at $LEGACY_LOG. Repair the packet by hand.\" >&2\n384:               exit 1\n385:             fi\n386:             mv \"$STATE_LOG\" \"$LEGACY_LOG\"\n387:           open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n388:           replay_command: |\n389:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n390:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n391:             RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n392:             node -e '\n393:               const fs = require(\"fs\"), os = require(\"os\"), path = require(\"path\");\n394:               const { spawnSync } = require(\"child_process\");\n395:               const [gateway, legacyLog, runDir] = process.argv.slice(1);\n396:               let replayedIterations = 0;\n397:               let keptOnlyInLegacyLog = 0;\n398:               for (const line of fs.readFileSync(legacyLog, \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\")) {\n399:                 if (line.trim() === \"\") continue;\n400:                 let row;\n401:                 try { row = JSON.parse(line); } catch { keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1; continue; }\n402:                 // The run open already replaced the config row.\n403:                 if (row && row.type === \"config\") continue;\n404:                 if (!row || row.type !== \"iteration\") { keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1; continue; }\n405:                 const tempDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"deep-review-replay-\"));\n406:                 const eventFile = path.join(tempDir, \"row.json\");\n407:                 fs.writeFileSync(eventFile, JSON.stringify(row));\n408:                 const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateway, \"--mode\", \"review\", \"--run-directory\", runDir, \"--event-json\", eventFile], { encoding: \"utf8\" });\n409:                 fs.rmSync(tempDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n410:                 if (result.status === 2) { process.stdout.write(result.stdout || \"\"); process.exit(2); }\n411:                 if (result.status === 0) replayedIterations += 1; else keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1;\n412:               }\n413:               process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ replayedIterations, keptOnlyInLegacyLog, legacyLog }) + \"\\n\");\n414:             ' \"$GATEWAY\" \"$RUN_DIR/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\" \"$RUN_DIR\"\n415:         on_completed_session:\n416:           before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n417:           log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n418:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n419:         on_invalid_state:\n420:           halt: true\n421:           message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n422:         on_fresh:\n423:           action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n424: \n425:       step_scope_discovery:\n426:         action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n427:         resolve:\n428:           spec-folder: |\n429:             1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n430:             2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n431:             3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n432:             4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n433:             5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n434:             6. Set scope = all discovered implementation and test files\n435:           skill: |\n436:             1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/\n437:             2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n438:             3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n439:             4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n440:             5. Set scope = all discovered files\n441:           agent: |\n442:             1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .skilled/agents/)\n443:             2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n444:             3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n445:           track: |\n446:             1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n447:             2. For each: read spec.md + acceptance-criteria.md\n448:             3. Set scope = all child spec artifacts\n449:           files: |\n450:             1. Expand glob patterns from review_target\n451:             2. Validate all files exist\n452:             3. Discover immediate cross-references (imports, links)\n453:             4. Set scope = expanded file list + cross-references\n454:         outputs:\n455:           - review_scope_files: \"List of all files in review scope\"\n456:           - cross_reference_targets: \"{ spec_paths: [...], code_paths: [...], test_paths: [...] }\"\n457: \n458:       step_order_dimensions:\n459:         action: \"Order review dimensions based on risk priority\"\n460:         algorithm: |\n461:           1. Iteration 0 (inventory pass): Build artifact map, identify file types, estimate complexity\n462:           2. Subsequent iterations follow risk-ordered deep passes:\n463:              correctness → security → traceability → maintainability\n464:           3. If review_dimensions != \"all\", filter to only requested dimensions\n465:           4. Derive traceability protocol plan:\n466:              - core: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n467:              - overlay: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n468:           5. If resource_map_present, reserve at least one traceability-oriented pass to cross-check target_files from applied/T-*.md against resource-map.md and classify touched / expected-by-scope / gap / absent-from-map outcomes\n469:           6. Store ordered list as dimension_queue\n470:         outputs:\n471:           - dimension_queue: \"Ordered list of dimensions to review\"\n472:           - inventory_pass: true\n473: \n474:       step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n475:         action: \"Normalize reviewDimensions once during init for config + JSONL reuse\"\n476:         outputs:\n477:           - review_dimensions_normalized: \"Canonical string[] for deep-review-config.json\"\n478:           - review_dimensions_json: \"JSON.stringify(review_dimensions_normalized) for JSONL config record\"\n479:         normalize: |\n480:           Accept {review_dimensions} in any of these shapes and convert once:\n481:             - \"all\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\",\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"]\n482:             - \"correctness,security\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\"]\n483:             - [\"correctness\"] → [\"correctness\"]\n484:           Every element MUST be one of the four canonical dimension names.\n485: \n486:       step_normalize_review_focus:\n487:         action: \"Normalize the optional operator review focus once during init\"\n488:         outputs:\n489:           - review_focus_normalized: \"Single-line focus text, or empty string when no focus was given\"\n490:         normalize: |\n491:           Collapse every control character (C0, C1, DEL, U+2028, U+2029) and whitespace run to one space, trim, treat an empty result as absent, and fail setup when more than 1000 characters remain.\n492:           fanout-run.cjs applies the same rule in code, so a fan-out lineage receives the same text.\n493: \n494:       step_resolve_session_id:\n495:         action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve timestamp fallback\"\n496:         branch_on: \"session_id\"\n497:         if_present:\n498:           bind:\n499:             session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n500:         if_absent:\n501:           bind:\n502:             session_id_init: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n503: \n504:       step_create_config:\n505:         action: \"Create deep-review-config.json from template with review-specific fields\"\n506:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n507:         populate:\n508:           topic: \"Review: {review_target}\"\n509:           mode: \"review\"\n510:           sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n511:           parentSessionId: null\n512:           lineageMode: \"new\"\n513:           generation: 1\n514:           continuedFromRun: null\n515:           reviewTarget: \"{review_target}\"\n516:           reviewTargetType: \"{review_target_type}\"\n517:           # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n518:           reviewDimensions: \"{review_dimensions_normalized}\"\n519:           # Null when review_focus_normalized is empty. The review report reads it back to show the focus.\n520:           reviewFocus: \"{review_focus_normalized}\"\n521:           resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n522:           reviewScopeFiles: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n523:           severityThreshold: \"P2\"\n524:           crossReference:\n525:             core: [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"]\n526:             overlay: [\"skill_agent\", \"agent_cross_runtime\", \"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n527:           maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n528:           # Semantic: weighted P0/P1/P2 severity ratio. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n529:           convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n530:           antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n531:           antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n532:           stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n533:           stuckThreshold: 2\n534:           maxDurationMinutes: 120\n535:           specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n536:           # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-review.md:71 (default true; false when flag is set).\n537:           # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n538:           resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n539:           createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n540:           status: \"initialized\"\n541:           releaseReadinessState: \"in-progress\"\n542:           executionMode: \"auto\"\n543:         output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n544: \n545:       step_create_state_log:\n546:         action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n547:         note: |\n548:           The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n549:           it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n550:           rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n551:           commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n552:           the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n553:           in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n554:         command: |\n555:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n556:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n557:           EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n558:           node -e '\n559:             const fs = require(\"fs\"), crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n560:             const [configPath, workflowPath] = process.argv.slice(1);\n561:             const sha = (bytes) => crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(bytes).digest(\"hex\");\n562:             const raw = fs.readFileSync(configPath);\n563:             const config = JSON.parse(raw);\n564:             const targetTypes = { files: \"file\", file: \"file\", directory: \"directory\", \"spec-folder\": \"directory\", track: \"directory\", repository: \"repository\" };\n565:             const lineageModes = { new: \"fresh\", fresh: \"fresh\", restart: \"restart\", resume: \"resume\" };\n566:             // The projected config row shows this topic; one the schema cannot hold is left out,\n567:             // and the row falls back to the run id rather than the run failing to open.\n568:             const topic = typeof config.topic === \"string\" && config.topic.trim() !== \"\" && config.topic.length <= 4096\n569:               ? config.topic\n570:               : null;\n571:             process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({\n572:               stem: \"deep_review.run_initialized\",\n573:               scope: { runId: config.sessionId, sessionId: config.sessionId, generation: Number(config.generation) || 1 },\n574:               data: {\n575:                 target: {\n576:                   targetId: \"review-target\",\n577:                   targetType: targetTypes[config.reviewTargetType] || \"artifact\",\n578:                   artifactRef: \"deep-review-config.json#reviewTarget\",\n579:                   sourceDigest: sha(String(config.reviewTarget)),\n580:                   contentDigest: sha(raw),\n581:                 },\n582:                 lineageMode: lineageModes[config.lineageMode] || \"fresh\",\n583:                 maxIterations: Number(config.maxIterations),\n584:                 convergencePolicyVersion: \"convergence-policy@\" + ((config.antiConvergence && config.antiConvergence.convergenceMode) || \"default\"),\n585:                 reviewModeContractDigest: sha(fs.readFileSync(workflowPath)),\n586:                 initialReleaseReadinessState: \"not-assessed\",\n587:                 ...(topic === null ? {} : { topic }),\n588:               },\n589:             }));\n590:           ' \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n591:           node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n592:           STATUS=$?\n593:           rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n594:           exit \"$STATUS\"\n595:         output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n596: \n597:       step_record_restarted_run:\n598:         skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n599:         action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n600:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n601: \n602:       step_create_findings_registry:\n603:         action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n604:         content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":1,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n605:         output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n606: \n607:       step_create_strategy:\n608:         action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n609:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 610]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml, lines 190-609\n190:       immediately after artifact resolution and before fan-out so old packet files\n191:       cannot be merged with fresh lineage outputs. A restart request must never\n192:       fall back to auto-resume. In auto mode, the explicit restart flag is operator\n193:       authorization to archive the resolved review packet, so do not ask for a\n194:       second confirmation. Rollback is to move the timestamped archive back to\n195:       the packet directory.\n196:     command: \"if [ -d \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\" ]; then mkdir -p \\\"{state_paths.archive_root}\\\" && mv \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\" \\\"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\\\"; fi; mkdir -p \\\"{state_paths.packet_dir}\\\"\"\n197:     outputs:\n198:       - archived_path: \"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug} when a prior packet existed, else null\"\n199:       - lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n200:     on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL; do not continue as resume or auto.\"\n201: \n202:   step_fanout_spawn:\n203:     description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n204:     skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n205:     instructions: |\n206:       Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own\n207:       isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n208:       This step runs before phase_init, so pass the raw review_focus. fanout-run.cjs\n209:       normalizes it and hands every lineage the same single-line text. Escape any double\n210:       quote, backslash, dollar sign or backtick in it for the shell, and pass an empty\n211:       string when no focus was given.\n212:       A cli-opencode lineage inside this fan-out is an explicit parallel-detached OpenCode\n213:       session with a separate lineage directory and session id; it is not the single-executor\n214:       self-invocation path. fanout-run.cjs owns the stack-only recursion guard for that\n215:       first-level detached lineage and still blocks recursive same-kind dispatch from inside it.\n216:       fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the\n217:       deep/review command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n218:       deep-review agent is used only for individual iterations, never as a full-loop\n219:       sub-agent or pasted phase-running prompt.\n220:       After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n221:       phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n222:       phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n223:     sub_steps:\n224:       step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n225:         description: \"Spawn all native and CLI lineages in capped worker pool\"\n226:         skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n227:         command: |\n228:           node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs \\\n229:             --spec-folder {spec_folder} \\\n230:             --loop-type review \\\n231:             --review-focus \"{review_focus}\" \\\n232:             --fanout-config-json '{config.fanout_json}' \\\n233:             --base-artifact-dir {artifact_dir} \\\n234:             --convergence-threshold {convergence_threshold} \\\n235:             --stop-policy {stop_policy} \\\n236:             --convergence-mode {convergence_mode}\n237:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n238:         wait_for_completion: true\n239: \n240:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n241:   # PHASE 1: INITIALIZATION\n242:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n243:   phase_init:\n244:     purpose: Create all state files for the review session and resolve review scope\n245:     steps:\n246: \n247:       step_preflight_contract:\n248:         action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n249:         verify:\n250:           - required_values_present: [review_target, review_target_type, review_dimensions, spec_folder, lineage_mode, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, stop_policy]\n251:           - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n252:           - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n253:           - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n254:         on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n255: \n256:       step_create_directories:\n257:         action: \"Create spec folder and canonical review packet directories if they don't exist\"\n258:         command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n259: \n260:       step_detect_resource_map:\n261:         action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist coverage-gate state\"\n262:         inspect:\n263:           - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n264:         classify:\n265:           present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n266:           absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n267:         outputs:\n268:           - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n269:           - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: concise resource-map snapshot for Known Context and charter framing. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n270: \n271:       step_migrate_legacy_review_state:\n272:         action: \"Rehome legacy review artifacts into review/iterations before session classification\"\n273:         detect:\n274:           canonical_review_state:\n275:             - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n276:             - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n277:             - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n278:             - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n279:           legacy_review_state:\n280:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json\"\n281:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n282:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md\"\n283:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md\"\n284:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md\"\n285:             - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause\"\n286:             - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n287:             - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report}\"\n288:           legacy_review_markers:\n289:             - \"scratch/deep-review-strategy.md exists\"\n290:             - \"scratch/deep-research-config.json declares mode == 'review' OR scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl contains mode == 'review'\"\n291:         migrate_only:\n292:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json -> {state_paths.config}\"\n293:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl -> {state_paths.state_log}\"\n294:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md -> {state_paths.strategy}\"\n295:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md -> {state_paths.dashboard}\"\n296:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n297:           - \"{spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause -> {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\"\n298:           - \"{state_paths.local_packet_dir}/iteration-*.md -> {state_paths.iteration_dir}/\"\n299:           - \"{state_paths.legacy_root_report} -> {state_paths.review_output}\"\n300:         on_canonical_present: \"Leave canonical review/ state untouched and do not overwrite it with legacy scratch artifacts.\"\n301:         on_legacy_detected: \"Move only the review-specific whitelist, print LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED and leave unrelated scratch files untouched. Nothing is appended here: an append before session classification would create the state log and turn a fresh packet into a partial one, and the moved state log was written without the ledger, so the gateway refuses every append to it until step_classify_session.on_moved_legacy_state adopts it.\"\n302:         on_conflict: \"If canonical review/ state and legacy scratch review state both exist but disagree, halt for operator repair instead of merging contradictory state.\"\n303:         outputs:\n304:           - legacy_migration_detected: \"true when the command printed LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED, else false\"\n305:           - migration_recorded: \"false; step_record_artifact_migration sets it once the migration row is appended\"\n306:         command: |\n307:           mkdir -p {state_paths.iteration_dir}\n308:           if [ ! -e {state_paths.config} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.state_log} ] && [ ! -e {state_paths.strategy} ] && [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && ( [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] || [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] ); then\n309:             [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-config.json {state_paths.config}\n310:             [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-research-state.jsonl {state_paths.state_log}\n311:             [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-strategy.md {state_paths.strategy}\n312:             [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/deep-review-dashboard.md {state_paths.dashboard}\n313:             find {spec_folder}/scratch -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\;\n314:             [ -e {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause ] && mv {spec_folder}/scratch/.deep-research-pause {state_paths.pause_sentinel}\n315:             [ -e {state_paths.legacy_root_report} ] && mv {state_paths.legacy_root_report} {state_paths.review_output}\n316:             echo \"LEGACY_REVIEW_STATE_MOVED\"\n317:           fi\n318:           find {state_paths.local_packet_dir} -maxdepth 1 -name 'iteration-*.md' -exec mv {} {state_paths.iteration_dir}/ \\; 2>/dev/null || true\n319: \n320:       step_acquire_lock:\n321:         action: \"Acquire the single-writer advisory lock before session classification\"\n322:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs acquire --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --packet-id {spec_folder} --ttl-ms 1800000\"\n323:         on_acquire: \"Capture lock.ownerPid as captured_owner_pid and lock.acquireNonce as captured_acquire_nonce from the JSON output, and reuse both for every release below. If acquired=false, fail closed — another deep-review run already holds this packet.\"\n324:         note: \"Uses the promoted runtime/ loop-lock CLI (single source of truth: stale-lock reclaim, clean owner-scoped release). macOS/BSD locking is advisory — best-effort single-writer, not a hard mutex across host calls. Acquire reclaims a stale lock itself and reports the old holder under `reclaimed`. A lock is stale when its heartbeat is older than twice its TTL, or when its owning process is known to be dead. No confirmation step exists in either mode: log a `reclaimed` holder and continue.\"\n325:         # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n326:         # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n327:         on_halt:\n328:           action: \"Release the lock before any terminal halt branch returns control\"\n329:           applies_to: [\"step_classify_session.on_invalid_state\", \"step_classify_session.on_completed_session\"]\n330:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; failures here are logged but do not block the halt\"\n331:         on_cancel:\n332:           action: \"Release the lock on user cancel or pause-sentinel detection before sentinel processing\"\n333:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; cancel completes regardless of cleanup result\"\n334:         on_workflow_exit:\n335:           action: \"Release the lock as the final step of any workflow exit path (success or failure)\"\n336:           command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}; idempotent — safe to invoke when already released\"\n337: \n338:       step_classify_session:\n339:         action: \"Classify the session before writing files\"\n340:         inspect:\n341:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n342:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n343:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n344:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n345:         classify:\n346:           fresh: \"None of the three state artifacts exist\"\n347:           resume: \"Config, JSONL, and strategy all exist and config.mode == 'review' and agree on target/spec folder\"\n348:           completed-session: \"Resume artifacts exist and config.status == 'complete'\"\n349:           invalid-state: \"Any partial, missing, or contradictory combination\"\n350:         outputs:\n351:           - session_state: \"fresh | resume | completed-session | invalid-state\"\n352:           - prior_tail_digest: \"sha256 of the state log bytes when resuming or restarting an existing lineage\"\n353:         lifecycle_routing:\n354:           - \"If lineage_mode == restart and session_state is resume or completed-session, execute on_restart before on_resume or on_completed_session.\"\n355:           - \"If lineage_mode == auto or lineage_mode == resume, preserve the existing resume/completed/fresh behavior.\"\n356:         on_resume:\n357:           before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n358:           log: \"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent. Continue the same lineage (sessionId unchanged, generation unchanged, no archive).\"\n359:           append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_resumed\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"sourceSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"resumeReason\":\"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent; continue the same lineage.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n360:           skip_to: phase_loop\n361:         on_restart:\n362:           action: \"Archive the current review packet under the root-level review-archive/ tree and start a new lineage segment with a fresh sessionId and generation+1.\"\n363:           command: \"if [ -d {state_paths.packet_dir} ]; then mkdir -p {state_paths.archive_root} && mv {state_paths.packet_dir} {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}; fi\"\n364:           set:\n365:             lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n366:             parent_session_id: \"{prior_session_id}\"\n367:             generation: \"{prior_generation + 1}\"\n368:           skip_to: step_create_config\n369:         note_deferred_branches: \"fork and completed-continue are deferred and no longer runtime-supported in this release. The reducer still reads `lineageMode` from config for dashboards and analysis, but only `new`, `resume`, and `restart` are live. See deep-review/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branches for the one-session contract.\"\n370:         on_moved_legacy_state:\n371:           applies_when: \"legacy_migration_detected == true and the branch taken resumes the session or goes to synthesis; never on restart or cancel\"\n372:           order: \"Runs after classification and before that branch appends anything, the resume event included.\"\n373:           note: |\n374:             The state log moved out of scratch/ was written by hand before the ledger existed, so the\n375:             gateway refuses every append to it. Set it aside unchanged as deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl,\n376:             open the run from the moved config, then replay its iteration rows through the gateway,\n377:             which carries each one whole. Rows the gateway cannot carry stay only in the set-aside file,\n378:             and the replay reports how many. Exit 2 from any of the three is a halt.\n379:           set_aside_command: |\n380:             STATE_LOG=\"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n381:             LEGACY_LOG=\"$(dirname \"$STATE_LOG\")/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\"\n382:             if [ -e \"$LEGACY_LOG\" ]; then\n383:               echo \"A set-aside legacy state log already exists at $LEGACY_LOG. Repair the packet by hand.\" >&2\n384:               exit 1\n385:             fi\n386:             mv \"$STATE_LOG\" \"$LEGACY_LOG\"\n387:           open_run: \"Run step_create_state_log.command unchanged. With the hand-written log set aside, it opens the run from the moved config.\"\n388:           replay_command: |\n389:             GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n390:             [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n391:             RUN_DIR=\"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\"\n392:             node -e '\n393:               const fs = require(\"fs\"), os = require(\"os\"), path = require(\"path\");\n394:               const { spawnSync } = require(\"child_process\");\n395:               const [gateway, legacyLog, runDir] = process.argv.slice(1);\n396:               let replayedIterations = 0;\n397:               let keptOnlyInLegacyLog = 0;\n398:               for (const line of fs.readFileSync(legacyLog, \"utf8\").split(\"\\n\")) {\n399:                 if (line.trim() === \"\") continue;\n400:                 let row;\n401:                 try { row = JSON.parse(line); } catch { keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1; continue; }\n402:                 // The run open already replaced the config row.\n403:                 if (row && row.type === \"config\") continue;\n404:                 if (!row || row.type !== \"iteration\") { keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1; continue; }\n405:                 const tempDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"deep-review-replay-\"));\n406:                 const eventFile = path.join(tempDir, \"row.json\");\n407:                 fs.writeFileSync(eventFile, JSON.stringify(row));\n408:                 const result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateway, \"--mode\", \"review\", \"--run-directory\", runDir, \"--event-json\", eventFile], { encoding: \"utf8\" });\n409:                 fs.rmSync(tempDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n410:                 if (result.status === 2) { process.stdout.write(result.stdout || \"\"); process.exit(2); }\n411:                 if (result.status === 0) replayedIterations += 1; else keptOnlyInLegacyLog += 1;\n412:               }\n413:               process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ replayedIterations, keptOnlyInLegacyLog, legacyLog }) + \"\\n\");\n414:             ' \"$GATEWAY\" \"$RUN_DIR/deep-review-state.legacy.jsonl\" \"$RUN_DIR\"\n415:         on_completed_session:\n416:           before_append: \"Run on_moved_legacy_state first when it applies.\"\n417:           log: \"Prior session already completed. Either archive the completed review/ tree and start a fresh session, or jump straight to synthesis with the existing artifacts.\"\n418:           skip_to: phase_synthesis\n419:         on_invalid_state:\n420:           halt: true\n421:           message: \"Existing deep-review state in review/ is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid review packet before continuing.\"\n422:         on_fresh:\n423:           action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n424: \n425:       step_scope_discovery:\n426:         action: \"Resolve review target to a concrete file list based on target type\"\n427:         resolve:\n428:           spec-folder: |\n429:             1. Inspect spec.md, plan.md, tasks.md, acceptance-criteria.md, implementation-summary.md, and goal-file-manifest.txt when present\n430:             2. If goal-file-manifest.txt exists, parse one repo-relative path per non-empty, non-comment line; reject absolute paths, traversal outside repo_root, duplicates, missing paths, and non-file entries\n431:             3. Fail before dispatch with line-numbered validation errors when any manifest entry is invalid; otherwise set scope = the validated manifest paths in declared order\n432:             4. When no manifest exists, discover implementation files referenced in the canonical spec artifacts\n433:             5. Discover test files associated with the implementation files\n434:             6. Set scope = all discovered implementation and test files\n435:           skill: |\n436:             1. Read SKILL.md from .skilled/skills/{skill_name}/\n437:             2. Discover references/, assets/, scripts/ contents\n438:             3. Find agent definitions referencing this skill across runtimes\n439:             4. Find command entry points referencing this skill\n440:             5. Set scope = all discovered files\n441:           agent: |\n442:             1. Find agent definition across repo-managed runtimes (.claude/agents/, .skilled/agents/)\n443:             2. Compare agent definitions for consistency\n444:             3. Set scope = all discovered agent files\n445:           track: |\n446:             1. List all child spec folders under specs/{track}/ or .opencode/specs/{track}/\n447:             2. For each: read spec.md + acceptance-criteria.md\n448:             3. Set scope = all child spec artifacts\n449:           files: |\n450:             1. Expand glob patterns from review_target\n451:             2. Validate all files exist\n452:             3. Discover immediate cross-references (imports, links)\n453:             4. Set scope = expanded file list + cross-references\n454:         outputs:\n455:           - review_scope_files: \"List of all files in review scope\"\n456:           - cross_reference_targets: \"{ spec_paths: [...], code_paths: [...], test_paths: [...] }\"\n457: \n458:       step_order_dimensions:\n459:         action: \"Order review dimensions based on risk priority\"\n460:         algorithm: |\n461:           1. Iteration 0 (inventory pass): Build artifact map, identify file types, estimate complexity\n462:           2. Subsequent iterations follow risk-ordered deep passes:\n463:              correctness → security → traceability → maintainability\n464:           3. If review_dimensions != \"all\", filter to only requested dimensions\n465:           4. Derive traceability protocol plan:\n466:              - core: spec_code, checklist_evidence\n467:              - overlay: skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability\n468:           5. If resource_map_present, reserve at least one traceability-oriented pass to cross-check target_files from applied/T-*.md against resource-map.md and classify touched / expected-by-scope / gap / absent-from-map outcomes\n469:           6. Store ordered list as dimension_queue\n470:         outputs:\n471:           - dimension_queue: \"Ordered list of dimensions to review\"\n472:           - inventory_pass: true\n473: \n474:       step_normalize_review_dimensions:\n475:         action: \"Normalize reviewDimensions once during init for config + JSONL reuse\"\n476:         outputs:\n477:           - review_dimensions_normalized: \"Canonical string[] for deep-review-config.json\"\n478:           - review_dimensions_json: \"JSON.stringify(review_dimensions_normalized) for JSONL config record\"\n479:         normalize: |\n480:           Accept {review_dimensions} in any of these shapes and convert once:\n481:             - \"all\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\",\"traceability\",\"maintainability\"]\n482:             - \"correctness,security\" → [\"correctness\",\"security\"]\n483:             - [\"correctness\"] → [\"correctness\"]\n484:           Every element MUST be one of the four canonical dimension names.\n485: \n486:       step_normalize_review_focus:\n487:         action: \"Normalize the optional operator review focus once during init\"\n488:         outputs:\n489:           - review_focus_normalized: \"Single-line focus text, or empty string when no focus was given\"\n490:         normalize: |\n491:           Collapse every control character (C0, C1, DEL, U+2028, U+2029) and whitespace run to one space, trim, treat an empty result as absent, and fail setup when more than 1000 characters remain.\n492:           fanout-run.cjs applies the same rule in code, so a fan-out lineage receives the same text.\n493: \n494:       step_resolve_session_id:\n495:         action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve timestamp fallback\"\n496:         branch_on: \"session_id\"\n497:         if_present:\n498:           bind:\n499:             session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n500:         if_absent:\n501:           bind:\n502:             session_id_init: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n503: \n504:       step_create_config:\n505:         action: \"Create deep-review-config.json from template with review-specific fields\"\n506:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-config.json\n507:         populate:\n508:           topic: \"Review: {review_target}\"\n509:           mode: \"review\"\n510:           sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n511:           parentSessionId: null\n512:           lineageMode: \"new\"\n513:           generation: 1\n514:           continuedFromRun: null\n515:           reviewTarget: \"{review_target}\"\n516:           reviewTargetType: \"{review_target_type}\"\n517:           # Reuse the single normalized init-time value from step_normalize_review_dimensions.\n518:           reviewDimensions: \"{review_dimensions_normalized}\"\n519:           # Null when review_focus_normalized is empty. The review report reads it back to show the focus.\n520:           reviewFocus: \"{review_focus_normalized}\"\n521:           resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n522:           reviewScopeFiles: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n523:           severityThreshold: \"P2\"\n524:           crossReference:\n525:             core: [\"spec_code\", \"checklist_evidence\"]\n526:             overlay: [\"skill_agent\", \"agent_cross_runtime\", \"feature_catalog_code\", \"playbook_capability\"]\n527:           maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n528:           # Semantic: weighted P0/P1/P2 severity ratio. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n529:           convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n530:           antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n531:           antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n532:           stopPolicy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n533:           stuckThreshold: 2\n534:           maxDurationMinutes: 120\n535:           specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n536:           # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-review.md:71 (default true; false when flag is set).\n537:           # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n538:           resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n539:           createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n540:           status: \"initialized\"\n541:           releaseReadinessState: \"in-progress\"\n542:           executionMode: \"auto\"\n543:         output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n544: \n545:       step_create_state_log:\n546:         action: \"Open the run in the ledger: record deep_review.run_initialized through the append gateway, which writes the state log's first row\"\n547:         note: |\n548:           The state log is a projection the gateway rebuilds from the ledger, so this step never writes\n549:           it directly. A config row written beside the ledger carries keys the projection cannot\n550:           rebuild, and the projection refuses to drop them, so every later append in the run would\n551:           commit to the ledger and then exit 2. Recording the run's opening as a ledger event makes\n552:           the projected config row the state log's first row from the start. The full config stays\n553:           in deep-review-config.json, which is what the reducer reads.\n554:         command: |\n555:           GATEWAY=\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n556:           [ -f \"$GATEWAY\" ] || GATEWAY=\"scripts/append-mode-event.cjs\"\n557:           EVENT_FILE=\"$(mktemp \"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-review-run-open.XXXXXX\")\"\n558:           node -e '\n559:             const fs = require(\"fs\"), crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n560:             const [configPath, workflowPath] = process.argv.slice(1);\n561:             const sha = (bytes) => crypto.createHash(\"sha256\").update(bytes).digest(\"hex\");\n562:             const raw = fs.readFileSync(configPath);\n563:             const config = JSON.parse(raw);\n564:             const targetTypes = { files: \"file\", file: \"file\", directory: \"directory\", \"spec-folder\": \"directory\", track: \"directory\", repository: \"repository\" };\n565:             const lineageModes = { new: \"fresh\", fresh: \"fresh\", restart: \"restart\", resume: \"resume\" };\n566:             // The projected config row shows this topic; one the schema cannot hold is left out,\n567:             // and the row falls back to the run id rather than the run failing to open.\n568:             const topic = typeof config.topic === \"string\" && config.topic.trim() !== \"\" && config.topic.length <= 4096\n569:               ? config.topic\n570:               : null;\n571:             process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({\n572:               stem: \"deep_review.run_initialized\",\n573:               scope: { runId: config.sessionId, sessionId: config.sessionId, generation: Number(config.generation) || 1 },\n574:               data: {\n575:                 target: {\n576:                   targetId: \"review-target\",\n577:                   targetType: targetTypes[config.reviewTargetType] || \"artifact\",\n578:                   artifactRef: \"deep-review-config.json#reviewTarget\",\n579:                   sourceDigest: sha(String(config.reviewTarget)),\n580:                   contentDigest: sha(raw),\n581:                 },\n582:                 lineageMode: lineageModes[config.lineageMode] || \"fresh\",\n583:                 maxIterations: Number(config.maxIterations),\n584:                 convergencePolicyVersion: \"convergence-policy@\" + ((config.antiConvergence && config.antiConvergence.convergenceMode) || \"default\"),\n585:                 reviewModeContractDigest: sha(fs.readFileSync(workflowPath)),\n586:                 initialReleaseReadinessState: \"not-assessed\",\n587:                 ...(topic === null ? {} : { topic }),\n588:               },\n589:             }));\n590:           ' \"{state_paths.config}\" \".skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\" > \"$EVENT_FILE\" || { rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"; exit 1; }\n591:           node \"$GATEWAY\" --mode review --run-directory \"$(dirname \"{state_paths.state_log}\")\" --event-json \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n592:           STATUS=$?\n593:           rm -f \"$EVENT_FILE\"\n594:           exit \"$STATUS\"\n595:         output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n596: \n597:       step_record_restarted_run:\n598:         skip_when: \"lineage_mode != 'restart'\"\n599:         action: \"Record the restarted lineage after the run-open row so the restart marker never precedes deep_review.run_initialized\"\n600:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.run_restarted\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}},\"data\":{\"priorTailDigest\":\"{prior_tail_digest}\",\"archivedLineageId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"restartReason\":\"Restart requested: the prior review packet was archived and a new lineage segment opened.\",\"continuedFromRunId\":\"{prior_session_id}-i{iteration_count}\",\"compatibilityDecision\":\"exact\",\"recoveryReceiptRef\":\"none\"}}'\n601: \n602:       step_create_findings_registry:\n603:         action: \"Initialize reducer-owned review findings registry\"\n604:         content: '{\"sessionId\":\"{session_id_init}\",\"generation\":1,\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"openFindings\":[],\"resolvedFindings\":[],\"repeatedFindings\":[],\"dimensionCoverage\":{\"correctness\":false,\"security\":false,\"traceability\":false,\"maintainability\":false},\"findingsBySeverity\":{\"P0\":0,\"P1\":0,\"P2\":0},\"openFindingsCount\":0,\"resolvedFindingsCount\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0.0}'\n605:         output: \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n606: \n607:       step_create_strategy:\n608:         action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n609:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 610]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\", \"offset\": 190, \"limit\": 420}"},"time":{"start":1793872911431,"end":1793872911773}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1793872912657,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"id":"prt_1ab286111001oNpzszH1eOle6n","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2856b40016qeCsuxxGczF1Z","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"a746fe1f8e328782bcd6c869ebf5d8725a1a031e","cost":0.000425184,"tokens":{"input":1172,"output":103,"reasoning":72,"cache":{"read":48128,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793872913873,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"id":"prt_1ab2865d1001p68zBV99foGsQp","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab286115001X1dUnmgHYyMMgq","type":"step-start","snapshot":"a746fe1f8e328782bcd6c869ebf5d8725a1a031e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793872914727,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab286687002somPPCScoNqrRE","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab286115001X1dUnmgHYyMMgq","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-934600e8774a5be7","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":200,"offset":607,"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml, lines 607-806\n607:       step_create_strategy:\n608:         action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n609:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n610:         populate:\n611:           review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n612:           review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n613:           dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n614:           scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n615:           cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n616:           max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n617:           convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n618:           stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n619:         output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n620: \n621:       step_seed_coverage_graph:\n622:         action: \"Seed the review coverage graph before the first convergence check\"\n623:         transform: |\n624:           1. Convert review_scope_files into FILE nodes.\n625:           2. Convert review target groupings into coarse SLICE nodes only; do not expand SYMBOL\n626:              or DEPENDENCY nodes in review mode.\n627:           3. Emit COVERS edges from SLICE nodes to FILE nodes when the grouping is known.\n628:           4. Bind coverage_seed_source to \"scope_discovery\" and coverage_seed_confidence to 0.50.\n629:           5. When scope discovery yields no files, emit [] for both arrays; the upsert script\n630:              returns a warning and review continues with an empty graph.\n631:         bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{config.sessionId}\\\" --nodes '{coverage_seed_nodes_json}' --edges '{coverage_seed_edges_json}' --seed-source \\\"{coverage_seed_source}\\\" --seed-confidence \\\"{coverage_seed_confidence}\\\"\"\n632:         outputs:\n633:           - coverage_seed_nodes_json: \"Seed nodes for review SLICE and FILE kinds only\"\n634:           - coverage_seed_edges_json: \"Seed COVERS edges where review target groupings resolved\"\n635:           - coverage_seed_warning: \"Warning emitted when the seed batch inserts zero nodes, else empty\"\n636:         on_warning:\n637:           log: \"Coverage graph seed inserted zero nodes; continuing with an empty graph.\"\n638:           proceed: true\n639: \n640:       step_enrich_strategy_context:\n641:         action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n642:         condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n643:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n644:         note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n645: \n646:       step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n647:         action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n648:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n649:         note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot and add Resource Map Coverage to the Review Charter. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n650: \n651:       step_init_complete:\n652:         log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created. Review scope: {review_scope_files_count} files, {dimension_queue_count} dimensions.\"\n653:         set: { current_iteration: 1, stuck_count: 0, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }\n654: \n655:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n656:   # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n657:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n658:   phase_loop:\n659:     purpose: Dispatch review agent iterations until convergence\n660:     repeat: true\n661:     max_repeats: \"{max_iterations}\"\n662:     steps:\n663: \n664:       step_refresh_lock:\n665:         action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat before the iteration begins\"\n666:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n667:         on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet and must stop rather than iterate without it.\"\n668: \n669:       step_record_artifact_migration:\n670:         action: \"Record the legacy review state move once per session, after the run is open\"\n671:         skip_when: \"legacy_migration_detected != true or migration_recorded == true\"\n672:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.migration\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"legacyArtifacts\":[\"deep-research-config.json\",\"deep-research-state.jsonl\",\".deep-research-pause\"],\"canonicalArtifacts\":[\"deep-review-config.json\",\"deep-review-state.jsonl\",\".deep-review-pause\"]}}'\n673:         set: { migration_recorded: true }\n674: \n675:       step_read_state:\n676:         action: \"Read current state from JSONL, strategy, and config\"\n677:         read:\n678:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n679:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n680:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n681:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n682:         extract:\n683:           - iteration_count: \"Count lines where type === 'iteration'\"\n684:           - current_iteration: \"iteration_count + 1\"\n685:           - last_newFindingsRatio: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from last iteration record\"\n686:           - last_focus: \"Extract focus/dimension from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n687:           - ratio_prev: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from second-latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n688:           - ratio_latest: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n689:           - next_dimension: \"Next uncovered dimension from dimension_queue in strategy.md\"\n690:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of dimensions already reviewed\"\n691:           - dimensions_remaining: \"List of dimensions not yet reviewed\"\n692:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total dimensions\"\n693:           - coverage_age: \"Iterations since dimension coverage last changed; require >= 1 before STOP\"\n694:           - p0_count: \"Count P0 findings across all iterations\"\n695:           - p1_count: \"Count P1 findings across all iterations\"\n696:           - p2_count: \"Count P2 findings across all iterations\"\n697:           - resource_map_present: \"Extract boolean from deep-review-config.json, default false\"\n698:           - resource_map_prompt_line: \"If resource_map_present is true, return 'Resource Map Coverage: cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md and classify only missed coverage as gaps.' Else return 'Resource Map Coverage: resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate.'\"\n699:           - session_id: \"Extract sessionId from deep-review-config.json\"\n700:           - generation: \"Extract generation from deep-review-config.json, else 1\"\n701:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records as 'run N: dimension (ratio, P0/P1/P2)'\"\n702:           - latest_status: \"Extract status from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n703:           - last_claim_adjudication_passed: \"Scan state.jsonl for the most recent `claim_adjudication` event; use its `passed` boolean. Default true when no event exists or when activeP0 + activeP1 == 0 (gate is vacuous without adjudicable findings).\"\n704:           - claim_adjudication_active_count: \"Count of active P0/P1 findings at the time of the last claim_adjudication event; 0 when none exist\"\n705:           - security_sensitive_fix_scope: \"Boolean true when the current review is a rerun after fixes involving security, path disclosure, auth/authz, sandboxing, env precedence, public schemas, persistence, or user-visible error payloads; derive from the latest review report, remediation notes, or planning packet when present, else false.\"\n706:           - fix_completeness_replay_required_rows: \"Count prior active or remediated P0/P1 findings, plus any prior security/path P2 findings, that require closed-gate replay before STOP.\"\n707:           - fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows: \"Count required replay rows marked PASS with file:line or command evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage.\"\n708:           - stop_policy: \"Extract stopPolicy from deep-review-config.json, default 'convergence'. Valid values: convergence, max-iterations.\"\n709:           - convergence_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.convergenceMode when it is one of 'default', 'off', 'sliding-window', or 'divergent'; default to 'default'\"\n710:           - convergence_mode_warning: \"Boolean true when antiConvergence.convergenceMode is present with an unsupported value; use 'default'\"\n711:           - pivot_lineage: \"Summarize registry.divergence.completed and registry.divergence.overrides with pivot ids, source iterations, and selected review direction; else 'none yet'\"\n712:           - saturated_directions: \"List registry.divergence.saturatedDirections; else 'none yet'\"\n713:           - review_focus_block: \"When deep-review-config.json reviewFocus is a non-empty string, return 'Operator review focus (cover it in addition to the dimension of this iteration, and say in the narrative how you addressed it): <reviewFocus>'. Else return an empty string.\"\n714: \n715:       step_check_pause_sentinel:\n716:         action: \"Check for pause sentinel file\"\n717:         check: \"Does {state_paths.pause_sentinel} exist?\"\n718:         if_exists:\n719:           set:\n720:             pending_stop_event: \"paused\"\n721:             pending_stop_reason: \"userPaused\"\n722:             pending_stop_detail: \"sentinel file detected\"\n723:           skip_to: step_normalize_pause_events\n724:         if_not_exists:\n725:           proceed: true\n726: \n727:       step_validate_convergence_config:\n728:         action: \"Validate convergence mode when loading config\"\n729:         if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n730:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"field\":\"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n731:           log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n732: \n733:       step_graph_convergence:\n734:         action: \"Evaluate coverage-graph convergence before the inline review convergence vote\"\n735:         inspect:\n736:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n737:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n738:         transform: |\n739:           1. Call graph convergence on the current review lineage before the inline 3-signal vote.\n740:           2. Record the decision as one of CONTINUE, STOP_ALLOWED, STOP_BLOCKED.\n741:           3. Preserve raw graph signals and blockers for reducer rollup and blocked-stop evidence.\n742:           4. Normalize blockers to both JSON array and CSV forms for downstream stop handling.\n743:           5. Set graph_stop_blocked = true only when graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\".\n744:         bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"review\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\"'\n745:         note: \"Invoke the runtime script directly. Review-side graph convergence must run before the inline review stop vote.\"\n746:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.graph_convergence_evaluated\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"rawSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"weightedSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"dimensionCoverageDigest\":\"{dimension_coverage_digest}\",\"protocolCoverageDigest\":\"{protocol_coverage_digest}\",\"findingStability\":\"{finding_stability}\",\"p0p1ResolutionState\":\"{p0p1_resolution_state}\",\"evidenceDensity\":{evidence_density},\"hotspotSaturation\":{hotspot_saturation},\"decision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"policyFingerprint\":\"{policy_fingerprint}\",\"blockerIds\":{graph_blocker_ids_json},\"stopCandidate\":{stop_candidate},\"graphDecision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"graphDigest\":\"{graph_digest}\",\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json}},\"eventId\":\"graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}\"}'\n747:         outputs:\n748:           - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED\"\n749:           - graph_decision_code: \"CONTINUE maps to continue, STOP_ALLOWED to converged, STOP_BLOCKED to blocked\"\n750:           - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by convergence.cjs\"\n751:           - graph_raw_signals_json: \"Exact-field convergence-signals JSON built from the convergence.cjs signals; observationDigest is the sha256 of graph_signals_json\"\n752:           - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers when present, else []\"\n753:           - graph_blocker_ids_json: \"JSON array of blocker type values; use [\\\"graph_blocker\\\"] when the decision is blocked and the list is empty\"\n754:           - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated blocker summary when graph blocks STOP, else empty string\"\n755:           - graph_stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n756:           - dimension_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the registry dimensionCoverage map\"\n757:           - protocol_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the protocol coverage object in graph_signals_json, or of {} when absent\"\n758:           - finding_stability: \"stable when findingStabilityRatio >= convergenceThreshold, unstable when below, unknown when the signal is missing\"\n759:           - p0p1_resolution_state: \"resolved when active P0 + P1 findings are 0, blocked when above 0, unknown when counts are unavailable\"\n760:           - evidence_density: \"evidenceDensityRatio from graph_signals_json, capped at 1\"\n761:           - hotspot_saturation: \"hotspotSaturationRatio from graph_signals_json, between 0 and 1\"\n762:           - policy_fingerprint: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON {convergenceThreshold, stopPolicy, convergenceMode} from the review config\"\n763:           - stop_candidate: \"true when graph_decision == STOP_ALLOWED, else false\"\n764:           - graph_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of graph_signals_json\"\n765: \n766:       step_check_convergence:\n767:         action: \"Evaluate graph-assisted review stop conditions and the legal-stop decision tree\"\n768:         algorithm: |\n769:           0. CLAIM-ADJUDICATION PRE-CHECK (universal STOP veto; runs before hard stops and composite convergence):\n770:              claim_adjudication_gate_pass = (last_claim_adjudication_passed != false) OR (p0_count + p1_count == 0)\n771:              If claim_adjudication_gate_pass == false:\n772:                candidate_decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n773:                stop_blocked = true\n774:                stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n775:                blocked_gates = [\"claimAdjudicationGate\"]\n776:                recovery_strategy = \"Reviewer must add typed claim-adjudication packets (claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger) for every active P0/P1 finding before STOP is allowed.\"\n777:                Skip hard stops (1) and composite convergence (4); proceed directly to step 5 legal-stop decision-tree assembly so blocked_by_json, gate outputs, and the blocked_stop event still populate consistently.\n778:           1. HARD STOPS:\n779:              a) if iteration_count >= max_iterations: set decision = \"STOP\", stopReason = \"maxIterationsReached\", hard_stop_reason = \"max_iterations_reached\", preserve any failed legal-stop gates as terminal evidence, and proceed to synthesis without legal-stop veto\n780:              b) if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: do not allow all-dimensions-clean or composite convergence to stop; treat convergence signals as telemetry, set decision = \"CONTINUE\", and broaden the next review angle.\n781:              c) if all dimensions clean AND required traceability protocols are covered AND p0_count == 0 AND p1_count == 0 AND coverage_age >= 1 AND all quality gates pass (evidence: every P0/P1 has file:line; scope: all findings within target; coverage: all dimensions reviewed): mark hard_stop_reason = \"all_dimensions_clean\" and promote to STOP candidate\n782:              Operator stop reasons (`maxIterationsReached`, `manualStop`, `userPaused`, unrecoverable `error`) are terminal ceilings. They do not hide failed gates; they record them in synthesis and stop dispatch.\n783:           2. STUCK DETECTION (threshold 2):\n784:              if stuck_count >= 2: STUCK_RECOVERY\n785:           3. GRAPH CONVERGENCE PREREQUISITE:\n786:                graph_decision, graph_signals_json, and graph_blockers_json are already populated by step_graph_convergence.\n787:                Final STOP is never legal unless the inline review vote says STOP AND graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\".\n788:                If graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\", set stop_blocked = true and route through blocked_stop emission instead of stopping.\n789:           4. COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE (3-signal weighted vote with split thresholds):\n790:                signals = []\n791:                a) Rolling average (w=0.30, window=2, needs 2+ iterations):\n792:                   avg = mean(last 2 newFindingsRatios)\n793:                   stop if avg <= 0.08\n794:                b) MAD noise floor (w=0.25, needs 3+ iterations):\n795:                   noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n796:                   stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n797:                c) Dimension coverage (w=0.45):\n798:                   coverage = dimensions_covered / total_dimensions\n799:                   stop if coverage >= 1.0 AND required traceability protocols are covered AND coverage_age >= 1\n800:                Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n801:                if latest ratio <= 0.05: mark no_progress_threshold_reached\n802:                if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: convergence votes are telemetry only; set weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\", and choose a broader next focus.\n803:                else if weighted_stop_score >= 0.60: inline STOP becomes a candidate and binary gates must run\n804:           5. LEGAL-STOP DECISION TREE (review-specific gates; runs whenever step 0, all-dimensions-clean, or the composite vote promotes STOP to a candidate; terminal max-iteration/manual/error stops bypass veto and record failed gates as evidence):\n805:                a) convergenceGate: pass when a hard-stop condition is met OR weighted_stop_score >= 0.60; record score\n806:                b) dimensionCoverageGate: pass when configured dimensions and required traceability coverage are complete and coverage_age >= 1; record covered and missing dimensions\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 807]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml, lines 607-806\n607:       step_create_strategy:\n608:         action: \"Create review strategy file from deep-review-strategy.md template\"\n609:         template: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/assets/deep-review-strategy.md\n610:         populate:\n611:           review_target: \"{review_target}\"\n612:           review_target_type: \"{review_target_type}\"\n613:           dimensions: \"{dimension_queue}\"\n614:           scope_files: \"{review_scope_files}\"\n615:           cross_reference_targets: \"{cross_reference_targets}\"\n616:           max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n617:           convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n618:           stop_policy: \"{stop_policy}\"\n619:         output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n620: \n621:       step_seed_coverage_graph:\n622:         action: \"Seed the review coverage graph before the first convergence check\"\n623:         transform: |\n624:           1. Convert review_scope_files into FILE nodes.\n625:           2. Convert review target groupings into coarse SLICE nodes only; do not expand SYMBOL\n626:              or DEPENDENCY nodes in review mode.\n627:           3. Emit COVERS edges from SLICE nodes to FILE nodes when the grouping is known.\n628:           4. Bind coverage_seed_source to \"scope_discovery\" and coverage_seed_confidence to 0.50.\n629:           5. When scope discovery yields no files, emit [] for both arrays; the upsert script\n630:              returns a warning and review continues with an empty graph.\n631:         bash: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/upsert.cjs --spec-folder \\\"{spec_folder}\\\" --loop-type \\\"review\\\" --session-id \\\"{config.sessionId}\\\" --nodes '{coverage_seed_nodes_json}' --edges '{coverage_seed_edges_json}' --seed-source \\\"{coverage_seed_source}\\\" --seed-confidence \\\"{coverage_seed_confidence}\\\"\"\n632:         outputs:\n633:           - coverage_seed_nodes_json: \"Seed nodes for review SLICE and FILE kinds only\"\n634:           - coverage_seed_edges_json: \"Seed COVERS edges where review target groupings resolved\"\n635:           - coverage_seed_warning: \"Warning emitted when the seed batch inserts zero nodes, else empty\"\n636:         on_warning:\n637:           log: \"Coverage graph seed inserted zero nodes; continuing with an empty graph.\"\n638:           proceed: true\n639: \n640:       step_enrich_strategy_context:\n641:         action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n642:         condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n643:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n644:         note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n645: \n646:       step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n647:         action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n648:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n649:         note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot and add Resource Map Coverage to the Review Charter. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n650: \n651:       step_init_complete:\n652:         log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created. Review scope: {review_scope_files_count} files, {dimension_queue_count} dimensions.\"\n653:         set: { current_iteration: 1, stuck_count: 0, p0_count: 0, p1_count: 0, p2_count: 0 }\n654: \n655:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n656:   # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n657:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n658:   phase_loop:\n659:     purpose: Dispatch review agent iterations until convergence\n660:     repeat: true\n661:     max_repeats: \"{max_iterations}\"\n662:     steps:\n663: \n664:       step_refresh_lock:\n665:         action: \"Refresh the packet lock heartbeat before the iteration begins\"\n666:         command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs refresh --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid} --nonce {captured_acquire_nonce}\"\n667:         on_refresh: \"If the refresh output has refreshed:false, fail closed: lost the packet lock. This run no longer holds the packet and must stop rather than iterate without it.\"\n668: \n669:       step_record_artifact_migration:\n670:         action: \"Record the legacy review state move once per session, after the run is open\"\n671:         skip_when: \"legacy_migration_detected != true or migration_recorded == true\"\n672:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.migration\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\"},\"data\":{\"mode\":\"review\",\"legacyArtifacts\":[\"deep-research-config.json\",\"deep-research-state.jsonl\",\".deep-research-pause\"],\"canonicalArtifacts\":[\"deep-review-config.json\",\"deep-review-state.jsonl\",\".deep-review-pause\"]}}'\n673:         set: { migration_recorded: true }\n674: \n675:       step_read_state:\n676:         action: \"Read current state from JSONL, strategy, and config\"\n677:         read:\n678:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n679:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n680:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n681:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n682:         extract:\n683:           - iteration_count: \"Count lines where type === 'iteration'\"\n684:           - current_iteration: \"iteration_count + 1\"\n685:           - last_newFindingsRatio: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from last iteration record\"\n686:           - last_focus: \"Extract focus/dimension from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n687:           - ratio_prev: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from second-latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n688:           - ratio_latest: \"Extract newFindingsRatio from latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n689:           - next_dimension: \"Next uncovered dimension from dimension_queue in strategy.md\"\n690:           - dimensions_covered: \"List of dimensions already reviewed\"\n691:           - dimensions_remaining: \"List of dimensions not yet reviewed\"\n692:           - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total dimensions\"\n693:           - coverage_age: \"Iterations since dimension coverage last changed; require >= 1 before STOP\"\n694:           - p0_count: \"Count P0 findings across all iterations\"\n695:           - p1_count: \"Count P1 findings across all iterations\"\n696:           - p2_count: \"Count P2 findings across all iterations\"\n697:           - resource_map_present: \"Extract boolean from deep-review-config.json, default false\"\n698:           - resource_map_prompt_line: \"If resource_map_present is true, return 'Resource Map Coverage: cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md and classify only missed coverage as gaps.' Else return 'Resource Map Coverage: resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate.'\"\n699:           - session_id: \"Extract sessionId from deep-review-config.json\"\n700:           - generation: \"Extract generation from deep-review-config.json, else 1\"\n701:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records as 'run N: dimension (ratio, P0/P1/P2)'\"\n702:           - latest_status: \"Extract status from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n703:           - last_claim_adjudication_passed: \"Scan state.jsonl for the most recent `claim_adjudication` event; use its `passed` boolean. Default true when no event exists or when activeP0 + activeP1 == 0 (gate is vacuous without adjudicable findings).\"\n704:           - claim_adjudication_active_count: \"Count of active P0/P1 findings at the time of the last claim_adjudication event; 0 when none exist\"\n705:           - security_sensitive_fix_scope: \"Boolean true when the current review is a rerun after fixes involving security, path disclosure, auth/authz, sandboxing, env precedence, public schemas, persistence, or user-visible error payloads; derive from the latest review report, remediation notes, or planning packet when present, else false.\"\n706:           - fix_completeness_replay_required_rows: \"Count prior active or remediated P0/P1 findings, plus any prior security/path P2 findings, that require closed-gate replay before STOP.\"\n707:           - fix_completeness_replay_passing_rows: \"Count required replay rows marked PASS with file:line or command evidence and producer/consumer/matrix coverage.\"\n708:           - stop_policy: \"Extract stopPolicy from deep-review-config.json, default 'convergence'. Valid values: convergence, max-iterations.\"\n709:           - convergence_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.convergenceMode when it is one of 'default', 'off', 'sliding-window', or 'divergent'; default to 'default'\"\n710:           - convergence_mode_warning: \"Boolean true when antiConvergence.convergenceMode is present with an unsupported value; use 'default'\"\n711:           - pivot_lineage: \"Summarize registry.divergence.completed and registry.divergence.overrides with pivot ids, source iterations, and selected review direction; else 'none yet'\"\n712:           - saturated_directions: \"List registry.divergence.saturatedDirections; else 'none yet'\"\n713:           - review_focus_block: \"When deep-review-config.json reviewFocus is a non-empty string, return 'Operator review focus (cover it in addition to the dimension of this iteration, and say in the narrative how you addressed it): <reviewFocus>'. Else return an empty string.\"\n714: \n715:       step_check_pause_sentinel:\n716:         action: \"Check for pause sentinel file\"\n717:         check: \"Does {state_paths.pause_sentinel} exist?\"\n718:         if_exists:\n719:           set:\n720:             pending_stop_event: \"paused\"\n721:             pending_stop_reason: \"userPaused\"\n722:             pending_stop_detail: \"sentinel file detected\"\n723:           skip_to: step_normalize_pause_events\n724:         if_not_exists:\n725:           proceed: true\n726: \n727:       step_validate_convergence_config:\n728:         action: \"Validate convergence mode when loading config\"\n729:         if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n730:           bookkeeping_log: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"review\",\"field\":\"antiConvergence.convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation}}'\n731:           log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n732: \n733:       step_graph_convergence:\n734:         action: \"Evaluate coverage-graph convergence before the inline review convergence vote\"\n735:         inspect:\n736:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n737:           - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n738:         transform: |\n739:           1. Call graph convergence on the current review lineage before the inline 3-signal vote.\n740:           2. Record the decision as one of CONTINUE, STOP_ALLOWED, STOP_BLOCKED.\n741:           3. Preserve raw graph signals and blockers for reducer rollup and blocked-stop evidence.\n742:           4. Normalize blockers to both JSON array and CSV forms for downstream stop handling.\n743:           5. Set graph_stop_blocked = true only when graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\".\n744:         bash: 'node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"review\" --session-id \"{session_id}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\"'\n745:         note: \"Invoke the runtime script directly. Review-side graph convergence must run before the inline review stop vote.\"\n746:         append_jsonl: '{\"stem\":\"deep_review.graph_convergence_evaluated\",\"scope\":{\"runId\":\"{session_id}\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"generation\":{generation},\"iterationId\":\"iteration-{current_iteration}\"},\"data\":{\"rawSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"weightedSignals\":{graph_raw_signals_json},\"dimensionCoverageDigest\":\"{dimension_coverage_digest}\",\"protocolCoverageDigest\":\"{protocol_coverage_digest}\",\"findingStability\":\"{finding_stability}\",\"p0p1ResolutionState\":\"{p0p1_resolution_state}\",\"evidenceDensity\":{evidence_density},\"hotspotSaturation\":{hotspot_saturation},\"decision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"policyFingerprint\":\"{policy_fingerprint}\",\"blockerIds\":{graph_blocker_ids_json},\"stopCandidate\":{stop_candidate},\"graphDecision\":\"{graph_decision_code}\",\"graphDigest\":\"{graph_digest}\",\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json}},\"eventId\":\"graph-{session_id}-g{generation}-i{current_iteration}\"}'\n747:         outputs:\n748:           - graph_decision: \"CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED\"\n749:           - graph_decision_code: \"CONTINUE maps to continue, STOP_ALLOWED to converged, STOP_BLOCKED to blocked\"\n750:           - graph_signals_json: \"JSON object returned by convergence.cjs\"\n751:           - graph_raw_signals_json: \"Exact-field convergence-signals JSON built from the convergence.cjs signals; observationDigest is the sha256 of graph_signals_json\"\n752:           - graph_blockers_json: \"JSON array of graph blockers when present, else []\"\n753:           - graph_blocker_ids_json: \"JSON array of blocker type values; use [\\\"graph_blocker\\\"] when the decision is blocked and the list is empty\"\n754:           - graph_blockers_csv: \"Comma-separated blocker summary when graph blocks STOP, else empty string\"\n755:           - graph_stop_blocked: \"Boolean true when graph_decision == STOP_BLOCKED\"\n756:           - dimension_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the registry dimensionCoverage map\"\n757:           - protocol_coverage_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON of the protocol coverage object in graph_signals_json, or of {} when absent\"\n758:           - finding_stability: \"stable when findingStabilityRatio >= convergenceThreshold, unstable when below, unknown when the signal is missing\"\n759:           - p0p1_resolution_state: \"resolved when active P0 + P1 findings are 0, blocked when above 0, unknown when counts are unavailable\"\n760:           - evidence_density: \"evidenceDensityRatio from graph_signals_json, capped at 1\"\n761:           - hotspot_saturation: \"hotspotSaturationRatio from graph_signals_json, between 0 and 1\"\n762:           - policy_fingerprint: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of the canonical JSON {convergenceThreshold, stopPolicy, convergenceMode} from the review config\"\n763:           - stop_candidate: \"true when graph_decision == STOP_ALLOWED, else false\"\n764:           - graph_digest: \"sha256 (64 lowercase hex) of graph_signals_json\"\n765: \n766:       step_check_convergence:\n767:         action: \"Evaluate graph-assisted review stop conditions and the legal-stop decision tree\"\n768:         algorithm: |\n769:           0. CLAIM-ADJUDICATION PRE-CHECK (universal STOP veto; runs before hard stops and composite convergence):\n770:              claim_adjudication_gate_pass = (last_claim_adjudication_passed != false) OR (p0_count + p1_count == 0)\n771:              If claim_adjudication_gate_pass == false:\n772:                candidate_decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n773:                stop_blocked = true\n774:                stopReason = \"blockedStop\"\n775:                blocked_gates = [\"claimAdjudicationGate\"]\n776:                recovery_strategy = \"Reviewer must add typed claim-adjudication packets (claim, evidenceRefs, counterevidenceSought, alternativeExplanation, finalSeverity, confidence, downgradeTrigger) for every active P0/P1 finding before STOP is allowed.\"\n777:                Skip hard stops (1) and composite convergence (4); proceed directly to step 5 legal-stop decision-tree assembly so blocked_by_json, gate outputs, and the blocked_stop event still populate consistently.\n778:           1. HARD STOPS:\n779:              a) if iteration_count >= max_iterations: set decision = \"STOP\", stopReason = \"maxIterationsReached\", hard_stop_reason = \"max_iterations_reached\", preserve any failed legal-stop gates as terminal evidence, and proceed to synthesis without legal-stop veto\n780:              b) if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: do not allow all-dimensions-clean or composite convergence to stop; treat convergence signals as telemetry, set decision = \"CONTINUE\", and broaden the next review angle.\n781:              c) if all dimensions clean AND required traceability protocols are covered AND p0_count == 0 AND p1_count == 0 AND coverage_age >= 1 AND all quality gates pass (evidence: every P0/P1 has file:line; scope: all findings within target; coverage: all dimensions reviewed): mark hard_stop_reason = \"all_dimensions_clean\" and promote to STOP candidate\n782:              Operator stop reasons (`maxIterationsReached`, `manualStop`, `userPaused`, unrecoverable `error`) are terminal ceilings. They do not hide failed gates; they record them in synthesis and stop dispatch.\n783:           2. STUCK DETECTION (threshold 2):\n784:              if stuck_count >= 2: STUCK_RECOVERY\n785:           3. GRAPH CONVERGENCE PREREQUISITE:\n786:                graph_decision, graph_signals_json, and graph_blockers_json are already populated by step_graph_convergence.\n787:                Final STOP is never legal unless the inline review vote says STOP AND graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\".\n788:                If graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\", set stop_blocked = true and route through blocked_stop emission instead of stopping.\n789:           4. COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE (3-signal weighted vote with split thresholds):\n790:                signals = []\n791:                a) Rolling average (w=0.30, window=2, needs 2+ iterations):\n792:                   avg = mean(last 2 newFindingsRatios)\n793:                   stop if avg <= 0.08\n794:                b) MAD noise floor (w=0.25, needs 3+ iterations):\n795:                   noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n796:                   stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n797:                c) Dimension coverage (w=0.45):\n798:                   coverage = dimensions_covered / total_dimensions\n799:                   stop if coverage >= 1.0 AND required traceability protocols are covered AND coverage_age >= 1\n800:                Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n801:                if latest ratio <= 0.05: mark no_progress_threshold_reached\n802:                if stop_policy == \"max-iterations\" AND iteration_count < max_iterations: convergence votes are telemetry only; set weighted_stop_score for diagnostics, keep decision = \"CONTINUE\", and choose a broader next focus.\n803:                else if weighted_stop_score >= 0.60: inline STOP becomes a candidate and binary gates must run\n804:           5. LEGAL-STOP DECISION TREE (review-specific gates; runs whenever step 0, all-dimensions-clean, or the composite vote promotes STOP to a candidate; terminal max-iteration/manual/error stops bypass veto and record failed gates as evidence):\n805:                a) convergenceGate: pass when a hard-stop condition is met OR weighted_stop_score >= 0.60; record score\n806:                b) dimensionCoverageGate: pass when configured dimensions and required traceability coverage are complete and coverage_age >= 1; record covered and missing dimensions\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 807]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 200, \"offset\": 607, \"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1793872914055,"end":1793872914727}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793872914734,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2867cf0015TL2RjjhRusRYv","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab286115001X1dUnmgHYyMMgq","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-87fed4440220d77d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && sed -n '2290,2420p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml"},"output":"  phase_synthesis:\n    purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n    steps:\n\n      step_fanout_merge:\n        description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n        command: |\n          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n            --loop-type review \\\n            --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        wait_for_completion: true\n        bind_from_output:\n          p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n          p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n          p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n\n      step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n        action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        read_patterns:\n          - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n        extract:\n          - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count type === 'iteration' across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n          - p0_count: \"Total P0 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - p1_count: \"Total P1 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - p2_count: \"Total P2 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n          - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n          - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n          - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n          - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present, else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused.)\"\n\n      # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n      # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n      # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 findings (no P0)\n      # - FAIL: any P0 findings\n      # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n      step_derive_verdict:\n        action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n        algorithm: |\n          if p0_count > 0:\n            verdict = \"FAIL\"\n          elif p1_count > 0:\n            verdict = \"CONDITIONAL\"\n          else:\n            verdict = \"PASS\"\n          has_advisories = (verdict == \"PASS\" and p2_count > 0)\n          ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\n        outputs:\n          - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n          - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n          - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n        contract: |\n          Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n          Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n\n      step_read_all_iterations:\n        action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n        read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n        read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n\n      step_build_finding_registry:\n        action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n        algorithm: |\n          1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n          2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n             content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n             Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n          3. Two-tier dedup:\n             PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n               - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n               - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n             FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n               - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n               - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n          4. Track finding lifecycle:\n             - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n             - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n             - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n          5. Resolve contradictions:\n             - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n             - Determine final severity and status\n          6. Count only 'active' findings for totals\n        outputs:\n          - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n          - active_p0: \"Count of active P0 findings\"\n          - active_p1: \"Count of active P1 findings\"\n          - active_p2: \"Count of active P2 findings\"\n\n      step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n        action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n        algorithm: |\n          For each active P0/P1 finding:\n            1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n            2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n            3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n          Update finding_registry with adjudicated results.\n\n      step_emit_resource_map:\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n        action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n        write:\n          - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n        guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n        note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n\n      step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n        action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n        note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n\n      step_compile_review_report:\n        action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n        instructions: |\n          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n          1. **Executive Summary**\n             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n             - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n             - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n             - Review scope summary\n             - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"  phase_synthesis:\n    purpose: Compile all iteration findings into review/review-report.md\n    steps:\n\n      step_fanout_merge:\n        description: \"Merge N lineage registries with strongest-restriction; bind p0/p1/p2 counts for step_derive_verdict; skip when single-executor\"\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n        command: |\n          node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-merge.cjs \\\n            --loop-type review \\\n            --artifact-dir {artifact_dir}\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        wait_for_completion: true\n        bind_from_output:\n          p0_count: \"active_p0\"\n          p1_count: \"active_p1\"\n          p2_count: \"active_p2\"\n\n      step_hydrate_summary_metrics:\n        action: \"Hydrate summary metrics before synthesis\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.findings_registry}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        read_patterns:\n          - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/lineages/*/deep-review-state.jsonl\"\n        extract:\n          - iteration_count: \"When direct lineage state logs exist, count type === 'iteration' across those logs in stable lineage order; otherwise count the root state log. Never add root compatibility records to lineage records.\"\n          - p0_count: \"Total P0 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - p1_count: \"Total P1 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - p2_count: \"Total P2 findings across all iterations (deduped)\"\n          - dimensions_covered: \"List of reviewed dimensions\"\n          - dimension_coverage: \"covered / total\"\n          - ac_coverage_signal: \"For spec-folder targets only: if level is 2+ and acceptance-criteria.md exists and implementation-summary.md is in-progress or later, surface the AC_COVERAGE advisory status; otherwise mark exempt.\"\n          - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records\"\n          - reason: \"Use the latest stop reason if present, else the frozen default 'converged'. (Must be a member of the STOP_REASONS enum: converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused.)\"\n\n      # H-1 verdict derivation: parse findings JSONL, map highest severity to verdict\n      # - PASS: no P0 or P1 findings (P2-only or clean)\n      # - CONDITIONAL: any P1 findings (no P0)\n      # - FAIL: any P0 findings\n      # Final line of iteration-NNN.md MUST be exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" / \"Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\" / \"Review verdict: FAIL\"\n      step_derive_verdict:\n        action: \"Derive review verdict from accumulated findings\"\n        algorithm: |\n          if p0_count > 0:\n            verdict = \"FAIL\"\n          elif p1_count > 0:\n            verdict = \"CONDITIONAL\"\n          else:\n            verdict = \"PASS\"\n          has_advisories = (verdict == \"PASS\" and p2_count > 0)\n          ac_coverage_signal is advisory while the validation rule is INFO/default-off; include it in synthesis traceability, but do not change the exact verdict enum from this signal alone.\n        outputs:\n          - verdict: \"PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\"\n          - has_advisories: \"Boolean true when verdict is PASS and any active P2 findings exist\"\n          - ac_coverage_signal: \"exempt | disabled | pass | advisory-shortfall\"\n        contract: |\n          Every iteration-NNN.md must end with exactly: \"Review verdict: PASS\" (or CONDITIONAL or FAIL).\n          Downstream automation parses this final line via exact string match — do not vary the format.\n\n      step_read_all_iterations:\n        action: \"Read all iteration files and strategy\"\n        read_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_dir}/iteration-*.md\"\n        read_also: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n\n      step_build_finding_registry:\n        action: \"Build deduplicated finding registry from all iterations\"\n        algorithm: |\n          1. Extract all findings from iteration JSONL delta files\n          2. Compute content_hash for each finding (emission requirement):\n             content_hash = sha256(file_path + \"\\u001f\" + line_range + \"\\u001f\" + finding_type + \"\\u001f\" + normalized_description_80chars)\n             Normalized description = whitespace-collapsed, lowercased, first 80 chars of the finding description.\n          3. Two-tier dedup:\n             PRIMARY: group by content_hash field\n               - Same content_hash, multiple dimensions → single finding, merged `dimensions: [<all>]` array\n               - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n             FALLBACK (legacy records lacking content_hash): file:line + normalized_title\n               - Same file:line, multiple dimensions → single finding, multiple dimension tags\n               - Keep highest severity on duplicates\n          4. Track finding lifecycle:\n             - status: active | duplicate | upgraded | downgraded | contested | resolved_false_positive\n             - Record first_seen, upgraded_in, previous_severity for severity changes\n             - Record dimensions array reflecting all dimensions that emitted this finding\n          5. Resolve contradictions:\n             - Findings marked contested across iterations → referee pass\n             - Determine final severity and status\n          6. Count only 'active' findings for totals\n        outputs:\n          - finding_registry: \"Deduplicated list of all findings with metadata\"\n          - active_p0: \"Count of active P0 findings\"\n          - active_p1: \"Count of active P1 findings\"\n          - active_p2: \"Count of active P2 findings\"\n\n      step_adversarial_selfcheck:\n        action: \"Final adversarial self-check on all P0 and P1 findings\"\n        algorithm: |\n          For each active P0/P1 finding:\n            1. Hunter: Re-verify finding against source code (re-read file:line)\n            2. Skeptic: Challenge severity — is this really P0/P1? Could it be P2?\n            3. Referee: Final call — confirm, downgrade, or mark false_positive\n          Update finding_registry with adjudicated results.\n\n      step_emit_resource_map:\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n        action: \"Emit {state_paths.resource_map_output} from converged review deltas unless config.resource_map.emit is false\"\n        command: \"node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder} {reducer_artifact_arg} --create-missing-anchors --emit-resource-map\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.delta_dir}/iter-*.jsonl\"\n        write:\n          - \"{state_paths.resource_map_output}\"\n        guarantee: \"Reducer skips cleanly when config.resource_map.emit == false and writes a deterministic resource-map when enabled.\"\n        note: \"A fan-out root has no root state log before closeout, so the root reducer would fail on the missing file. Each lineage emits its own map, so the report names the ones that exist at {artifact_dir}/lineages/*/resource-map.md.\"\n\n      step_resource_map_coverage_gate:\n        action: \"If resource_map_present, compute the Resource Map Coverage Gate synthesis inputs; otherwise preserve the skip note\"\n        note: \"Cross-check target_files from {spec_folder}/applied/T-*.md against {spec_folder}/resource-map.md. Report touched entries, untouched entries split into expected-by-scope vs gap, and implementation paths absent from the map. Findings raised here use category resource-map-coverage with severity calibrated to the gate outcome.\"\n\n      step_compile_review_report:\n        action: \"Compile review/review-report.md with 9 core sections, a conditional Resource Map Coverage Gate section, and an embedded Planning Packet\"\n        instructions: |\n          Create review/review-report.md with the following sections:\n\n          1. **Executive Summary**\n             - Overall verdict: PASS | CONDITIONAL | FAIL\n             - hasAdvisories: true when PASS carries active P2 items\n             - P0/P1/P2 counts (active only)\n             - Review scope summary\n             - Operator review focus: config.reviewFocus verbatim, or omit this line when it is null\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && sed -n '2290,2420p' .skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-review-auto.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1793872914383,"end":1793872914734}}}}
