{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793872945933,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab28e181001c8IgAkAOnMH2l2","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab28d787001ebZ20NxxgFG0Ib","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8129cd7bd9991a89","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && git diff 10474a9567 -- .skilled/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md | head -260"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md\nindex ccf7d62624..6e2a9bc370 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"design intent routing\"\n importance_tier: important\n contextType: implementation\n-version: 2.0.9.0\n+version: 3.0.0.0\n router_state: active\n skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n ---\n@@ -29,21 +29,16 @@ An intent that matches nothing here is a gap to report, not a reason to load eve\n \n ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n \n-Five intents across four modes. The split is real rather than decorative: deciding a value, judging\n-a surface against values, authoring a chart canvas, authoring a diagram canvas, and reading values\n-back off a surface that already exists all load different things.\n+Three intents across three modes. The split is real rather than decorative: authoring a chart\n+canvas, authoring a diagram canvas, and reading values back off a surface that already exists all\n+load different things.\n \n | Intent | Mode | What the request is asking for |\n |--------|------|-------------------------------|\n-| `VALUES` | `sk-design-fundamentals` | Decide a value for something that does not exist yet |\n-| `REVIEW` | `sk-design-fundamentals` | Judge a surface that does exist against those values |\n | `CHART` | `sk-design-chart` | Author a data canvas: one file, one question a reader answers by looking |\n | `FLOWCHART` | `sk-design-diagram` | Author a process canvas, in markup or in text characters |\n | `EXTRACT` | `sk-design-md-generator` | Read values back off a surface that already exists |\n \n-`VALUES` and `REVIEW` share a mode because they share its references; they stay separate intents\n-because they load different ones.\n-\n ---\n \n ## 3. MACHINE-READABLE ROUTER (replay / benchmark source)\n@@ -59,28 +54,16 @@ The single machine-readable projection of the intent model above.\n ```python\n # No always-loaded preamble: a design request loads only the selected mode's\n # leaves, so the hub default route stays minimal and a no-match disambiguates\n-# rather than pulling four modes' references into context.\n+# rather than pulling three modes' references into context.\n DEFAULT_RESOURCE = []\n \n INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n-    \"VALUES\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"padding\", \"spacing\", \"margin\", \"gutter\", \"type scale\", \"typography\", \"font size\", \"colour\", \"color\", \"contrast\", \"contrast ratio\", \"radius\", \"corner radius\", \"elevation\", \"shadow\", \"hierarchy\", \"visual hierarchy\", \"what should this look like\", \"slide deck design\", \"slide layout\", \"presentation design\", \"deck spacing\", \"how should this slide be laid out\", \"print layout\", \"printed page design\", \"margins for a print layout\", \"type scale for a printed report\", \"document layout\", \"document layout hierarchy\", \"report layout\", \"long-form layout\", \"poster layout\", \"design fundamentals\", \"what padding should this have\", \"spacing scale\", \"colour decision\", \"color decision\"]},\n-    \"REVIEW\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"design review\", \"does this look right\", \"critique this\", \"visual audit\", \"ux laws\", \"accessibility contrast\", \"review this screen\", \"why does this look wrong\", \"design review of this slide deck\", \"review this deck\", \"review this layout\", \"critique\"]},\n     \"CHART\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a chart\", \"make a chart\", \"chart this data\", \"chart the data\", \"plot the data\", \"plot this data\", \"standalone html chart\", \"chart catalog\", \"which chart type\", \"chart template\", \"chart color system\", \"chart colour system\", \"data visualization\", \"data visualisation\", \"data viz\", \"bar chart of\", \"line chart of\", \"scatter plot of\", \"treemap\", \"waterfall chart\", \"heat matrix\", \"heatmap\", \"heat map\", \"calendar heatmap\", \"box plot\", \"candlestick chart\", \"stacked area chart\", \"stacked bar chart\", \"grouped bar chart\", \"donut chart\", \"waffle chart\", \"histogram\", \"parallel coordinates\", \"measured site's look\", \"theme a chart\", \"theme this chart\", \"theme the chart\"]},\n     \"FLOWCHART\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"flowchart\", \"ascii\", \"text diagram\", \"text characters\", \"decision tree\", \"process diagram\", \"flow diagram\", \"diagram the\", \"as a diagram\", \"create diagram\", \"diagram\", \"architecture diagram\", \"sequence diagram\", \"er diagram\", \"entity relationship diagram\", \"data model diagram\", \"state machine diagram\", \"swimlane diagram\", \"swimlane\", \"venn diagram\", \"org chart\", \"quadrant diagram\", \"gantt chart\", \"radar chart\", \"high-level diagram\", \"medallion diagram\", \"data flow diagram\", \"draw.io\", \"drawio\", \"mermaid diagram\", \"redraw diagram\", \"self-contained html diagram\", \"editorial diagram\", \"create flowchart\", \"ascii flowchart\", \"workflow diagram\", \"decision branch\", \"parallel execution diagram\", \"approval loop diagram\", \"export diagram\", \"create:diagram\", \"/design:diagram\", \"theme diagram\", \"repaint diagram\", \"brand the diagram\", \"venn\", \"mermaid\"]},\n     \"EXTRACT\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"extract\", \"design.md\", \"style reference\", \"design tokens\", \"measure this surface\", \"from a url\", \"from a site\", \"css extraction\", \"validate design.md\", \"style guide from\", \"measure\", \"extract design tokens\", \"measure a surface\", \"extract css\", \"design tokens from a site\", \"style guide from a url\"]},\n }\n \n RESOURCE_MAP = {\n-    \"VALUES\": [\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/references/hierarchy.md\",\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/references/color-system.md\",\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/assets/token-starter-set.md\",\n-    ],\n-    \"REVIEW\": [\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/references/review-checklist.md\",\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/references/ux-laws.md\",\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/references/diagnosis-table.md\",\n-    ],\n     \"CHART\": [\n         \"sk-design-chart/references/catalog.md\",\n         \"sk-design-chart/references/color-system.md\",\n@@ -107,8 +90,6 @@ RESOURCE_MAP = {\n - Two near-tied intents (within the ambiguity delta) route to both leaf sets; the union is deduped by\n   canonical pair and capped at the selected-map union limit. `CHART` and `FLOWCHART` are the pair most\n   likely to tie, because a request to visualise something rarely says which canvas it wants.\n-- `VALUES` and `REVIEW` resolve to the same mode. A tie between them is not ambiguity to escalate; it\n-  is one mode loading both leaf sets.\n - This map lists leaves, which is why no `SKILL.md` appears in it. A mode entry is loaded because the\n   registry named the mode, not from here.\n - Load what a row resolves and nothing more; a resource already in context is not re-read.\n@@ -131,8 +112,8 @@ no map of its own: the `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` block in section 3 st\n \n ### Surface Router, per-intent leaf sets\n \n-Stage 2 lives in section 3 of this file. It defines the five-intent leaf\n-model (VALUES, REVIEW, CHART, FLOWCHART, EXTRACT), the machine-readable `INTENT_SIGNALS` and\n+Stage 2 lives in section 3 of this file. It defines the three-intent leaf\n+model (CHART, FLOWCHART, EXTRACT), the machine-readable `INTENT_SIGNALS` and\n `RESOURCE_MAP` block the deterministic router-replay parses, and the how-to-read rules: a dominant\n intent takes one leaf set, near-tied intents take a deduped union, and no keyword match is the hub's\n UNKNOWN fallback rather than a silent default. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and\n@@ -142,11 +123,11 @@ This router stays a separate document from `SKILL.md` on purpose; [the parent-sk\n \n ### The discriminator\n \n-- **`workflowMode`** — the public mode key: `sk-design-fundamentals`, `sk-design-md-generator`,\n-  `sk-design-chart`, `sk-design-diagram`.\n-- **`packetKind`** — `workflow` for all four. There is no surface axis on this hub.\n-- **`backendKind`** — `surface-router` for fundamentals and the generator, which resolve leaves from\n-  a reference set; `template-scaffold` for chart and diagram, which build an artifact from a form.\n+- **`workflowMode`** — the public mode key: `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart`,\n+  `sk-design-diagram`.\n+- **`packetKind`** — `workflow` for all three. There is no surface axis on this hub.\n+- **`backendKind`** — `surface-router` for the generator, which resolves leaves from a reference\n+  set. `template-scaffold` for chart and diagram, which build an artifact from a form.\n \n ### Routing rule\n \n@@ -156,8 +137,8 @@ REGISTRY    = SKILL_ROOT / \"mode-registry.json\"\n HUB_ROUTER  = SKILL_ROOT / \"hub-router.json\"\n \n UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n-    \"Confirm whether this decides a value, reviews a surface, measures an existing surface, or builds a chart or diagram\",\n-    \"Confirm the surface: screen UI, slide deck, printed page, document layout, or a chart or diagram canvas\",\n+    \"Confirm whether this measures an existing surface or builds a chart or diagram\",\n+    \"A request to decide a value or review a screen belongs to sk-code, not this hub\",\n     \"For a measure request, provide the live URL or path; there is nothing to read without one\",\n     \"For a canvas request, state the question the artifact must answer, not the form you want\",\n ]\n@@ -187,7 +168,6 @@ classify the request to one or more workflowMode values using hub-router.json\n \n if two intents tie within routerPolicy.ambiguityDelta:\n   apply routerPolicy.tieBreak, then take the deduped union of their leaf sets\n-  VALUES and REVIEW resolving together is not ambiguity: they are one mode loading both sets\n \n if confidence is low or the intent is contradictory:\n   return UNKNOWN_FALLBACK with disambiguation_checklist = UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST\n@@ -202,6 +182,5 @@ for each resolved workflowMode:\n return single or ambiguous according to hub-router.json routerPolicy.outcomes\n ```\n \n-`routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `sk-design-fundamentals`: a design question with no clearer owner is a\n-values question. That differs from `sk-doc`, whose default is `null` because an unclear documentation\n-intent has no safe default. The outcomes `routerPolicy.outcomes` defines are `single`, `orderedBundle`, `defer` and `none`.\n+`routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`: a design request with no clearer owner has no safe default\n+among the three artifacts, so it defers and asks which one is wanted. The outcomes `routerPolicy.outcomes` defines are `single`, `orderedBundle`, `defer` and `none`.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md\nindex 6647d3a6a9..4f12d86645 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md\n@@ -1,13 +1,13 @@\n ---\n name: sk-design\n-description: \"Design parent hub. Routes one design identity to the mode that owns the decision, starting with sk-design-fundamentals.\"\n+description: \"Design parent hub. Routes one design identity to the mode that owns the artifact: a measured Style Reference, a chart or a diagram.\"\n allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n-version: 2.0.11.0\n+version: 3.0.0.0\n metadata:\n   family: sk-design\n ---\n \n-<!-- Keywords: design, spacing, padding, typography, colour, contrast, hierarchy, design review, ux laws, design fundamentals -->\n+<!-- Keywords: design, style reference, design.md, extract design tokens, chart, diagram, flowchart -->\n \n # Design (parent hub)\n \n@@ -18,31 +18,25 @@ decision in front of you and hands over. The work lives in the modes.\n \n ## 1. WHEN TO USE\n \n-Use this hub when the question is what a surface should look like, why it looks wrong, or what\n-visual artifact answers it: spacing, type, colour, contrast, hierarchy, a review of an existing\n-surface against design criteria, a data chart, or a process diagram. The surface can be screen UI, a\n-slide deck, a printed page or a document layout.\n+Use this hub when the answer is a design artifact: a measured Style Reference of an existing\n+surface, a data chart, or a process diagram.\n \n | Mode | Command | Owns | Reach it by asking about |\n |------|---------|------|--------------------------|\n-| `sk-design-fundamentals` | routes via aliases | The values a surface is built from, and reviewing a surface against them | spacing, padding, type scale, colour, contrast, hierarchy, design review |\n | `sk-design-md-generator` | `/design:extract` | Measuring an existing surface into a Style Reference, and validating one | extract, design.md, design tokens, from a url |\n | `sk-design-chart` | `/design:chart` | Chart forms: which one answers the question, and building it as a self-contained file | chart, plot, heatmap, bar chart, chart catalog |\n | `sk-design-diagram` | `/design:diagram` | Flowcharts and text diagrams | diagram, flowchart, ascii diagram, mermaid, drawio |\n \n-Four modes. Fundamentals and the generator are complements rather than alternatives: one decides values, the other reads values back\n-off something that already exists. A request that names an existing surface belongs to the\n-generator; a request that asks what a value should be belongs to fundamentals.\n+Three modes. The generator reads values back off something that already exists. Chart and diagram\n+each build one self-contained canvas.\n \n ### When NOT to Use\n \n-- **Measuring a surface that already exists into a written specification.** That is this hub's\n-  EXTRACT mode, reached by naming the source; it is not the values path.\n+- **Deciding a value or reviewing a screen.** Spacing, type, colour, contrast, hierarchy, motion\n+  and visual review belong to `sk-code`, whose frontend surface carries the value scales and the\n+  review pass.\n - **Authoring documentation prose.** `sk-doc` owns that, including READMEs, changelogs and playbooks.\n-- **Implementing the values once decided.** `sk-code` owns the code that renders them; this hub\n-  decides what they should be and never writes the component.\n-- **A canvas question that names its own form.** A chart or diagram request goes to its mode\n-  directly rather than through the values mode.\n+- **Implementing a component.** `sk-code` owns the code that renders it.\n \n ---\n \n@@ -52,14 +46,14 @@ Routing runs in two stages.\n Stage one picks a mode from this hub.\n `hub-router.json` is its one authored vocabulary.\n `vocabularyClasses` holds the terms, and `routerSignals` maps each mode to the classes it scores.\n-The four modes are `sk-design-fundamentals`, `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart` and `sk-design-diagram`.\n+The three modes are `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart` and `sk-design-diagram`.\n Stage two maps the chosen mode to its leaves in the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md).\n The two layers stay separate: the hub never emits leaf paths, and the surface router never re-decides the mode.\n The advisor routes every design query to the single identity `sk-design`.\n Run the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-design --prompt \"<task>\"`.\n Act on the decision: `route` loads its targets, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\n-With no signal at all, `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `sk-design-fundamentals`, so the request lands on the values mode rather than asking.\n+With no signal at all, `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`, so the request defers and asks which artifact is wanted.\n \n ---\n \n@@ -67,17 +61,17 @@ With no signal at all, `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `sk-design-fundamentals`, s\n \n ### Terms\n \n-- **`workflowMode`**: the public mode key, one of `sk-design-fundamentals`, `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart` or `sk-design-diagram`.\n-- **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for all four modes, because this hub has no surface axis.\n-- **`backendKind`**: `surface-router` for fundamentals and the generator, which resolve leaves from a reference set, while `template-scaffold` for chart and diagram builds an artifact from a form.\n+- **`workflowMode`**: the public mode key, one of `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart` or `sk-design-diagram`.\n+- **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for all three modes, because this hub has no surface axis.\n+- **`backendKind`**: `surface-router` for the generator, which resolves leaves from a reference set, while `template-scaffold` for chart and diagram builds an artifact from a form.\n - **`routingClass`**: `metadata` on every nested mode, so the advisor resolves this hub by membership and holds no entry of its own per mode.\n - **`mode-registry.json`**: what modes exist and what each may touch.\n - **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's signals, vocabulary classes, tie-break and default mode.\n - **`vocabularyClasses`**: the terms stage one matches, with `routerSignals` naming the classes each mode scores.\n-- **`tieBreak`**: the `routerPolicy` order that ranks the four modes when scores are close.\n-- **`routerPolicy.defaultMode`**: `sk-design-fundamentals`, the mode a request with no signal at all lands on.\n+- **`tieBreak`**: the `routerPolicy` order that ranks the three modes when scores are close.\n+- **`routerPolicy.defaultMode`**: `null`, so a request with no signal at all defers instead of landing on a mode.\n - **leaf**: a resource a chosen mode loads, counted as a canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair through `leaf-manifest.json`.\n-- **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` over the five leaf intents, VALUES, REVIEW, CHART, FLOWCHART and EXTRACT.\n+- **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` over the three leaf intents, CHART, FLOWCHART and EXTRACT.\n - **`intent_signals`**: the `graph-metadata.json` field that carries this hub's vocabulary to the advisor, since a `description.json` keyword is documentation and not scored.\n \n ### Layout\n@@ -91,7 +85,6 @@ sk-design/\n ├── graph-metadata.json      the only vocabulary the advisor scores\n ├── command-metadata.json    the commands this hub owns, and which mode owns each\n ├── shared/scripts/          tooling both canvas modes use\n-├── sk-design-fundamentals/  the values mode, and everything it owns\n ├── sk-design-md-generator/  the extraction mode, its engine and style corpus\n ├── sk-design-chart/         the chart corpus, its checker, gallery and screenshots\n └── sk-design-diagram/       the diagram forms, their validator and screenshots\n@@ -143,7 +136,6 @@ green gate all leave a request unable to arrive. Only replaying the request prov\n | `mode-registry.json` | What modes exist, and what each may touch |\n | `hub-router.json` | Signals, vocabulary classes, tie-break |\n | `ROUTER.md` | Stage two: which resources a chosen mode loads |\n-| `sk-design-fundamentals/` | The values mode, and everything it owns |\n | `sk-design-md-generator/` | The extraction mode, its engine and its style corpus |\n | `sk-design-chart/` | The chart corpus and its checker |\n | `sk-design-diagram/` | The diagram forms and their validator |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md\nindex ccf7d62624..6e2a9bc370 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"design intent routing\"\n importance_tier: important\n contextType: implementation\n-version: 2.0.9.0\n+version: 3.0.0.0\n router_state: active\n skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n ---\n@@ -29,21 +29,16 @@ An intent that matches nothing here is a gap to report, not a reason to load eve\n \n ## 2. INTENT MODEL\n \n-Five intents across four modes. The split is real rather than decorative: deciding a value, judging\n-a surface against values, authoring a chart canvas, authoring a diagram canvas, and reading values\n-back off a surface that already exists all load different things.\n+Three intents across three modes. The split is real rather than decorative: authoring a chart\n+canvas, authoring a diagram canvas, and reading values back off a surface that already exists all\n+load different things.\n \n | Intent | Mode | What the request is asking for |\n |--------|------|-------------------------------|\n-| `VALUES` | `sk-design-fundamentals` | Decide a value for something that does not exist yet |\n-| `REVIEW` | `sk-design-fundamentals` | Judge a surface that does exist against those values |\n | `CHART` | `sk-design-chart` | Author a data canvas: one file, one question a reader answers by looking |\n | `FLOWCHART` | `sk-design-diagram` | Author a process canvas, in markup or in text characters |\n | `EXTRACT` | `sk-design-md-generator` | Read values back off a surface that already exists |\n \n-`VALUES` and `REVIEW` share a mode because they share its references; they stay separate intents\n-because they load different ones.\n-\n ---\n \n ## 3. MACHINE-READABLE ROUTER (replay / benchmark source)\n@@ -59,28 +54,16 @@ The single machine-readable projection of the intent model above.\n ```python\n # No always-loaded preamble: a design request loads only the selected mode's\n # leaves, so the hub default route stays minimal and a no-match disambiguates\n-# rather than pulling four modes' references into context.\n+# rather than pulling three modes' references into context.\n DEFAULT_RESOURCE = []\n \n INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n-    \"VALUES\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"padding\", \"spacing\", \"margin\", \"gutter\", \"type scale\", \"typography\", \"font size\", \"colour\", \"color\", \"contrast\", \"contrast ratio\", \"radius\", \"corner radius\", \"elevation\", \"shadow\", \"hierarchy\", \"visual hierarchy\", \"what should this look like\", \"slide deck design\", \"slide layout\", \"presentation design\", \"deck spacing\", \"how should this slide be laid out\", \"print layout\", \"printed page design\", \"margins for a print layout\", \"type scale for a printed report\", \"document layout\", \"document layout hierarchy\", \"report layout\", \"long-form layout\", \"poster layout\", \"design fundamentals\", \"what padding should this have\", \"spacing scale\", \"colour decision\", \"color decision\"]},\n-    \"REVIEW\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"design review\", \"does this look right\", \"critique this\", \"visual audit\", \"ux laws\", \"accessibility contrast\", \"review this screen\", \"why does this look wrong\", \"design review of this slide deck\", \"review this deck\", \"review this layout\", \"critique\"]},\n     \"CHART\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"create a chart\", \"make a chart\", \"chart this data\", \"chart the data\", \"plot the data\", \"plot this data\", \"standalone html chart\", \"chart catalog\", \"which chart type\", \"chart template\", \"chart color system\", \"chart colour system\", \"data visualization\", \"data visualisation\", \"data viz\", \"bar chart of\", \"line chart of\", \"scatter plot of\", \"treemap\", \"waterfall chart\", \"heat matrix\", \"heatmap\", \"heat map\", \"calendar heatmap\", \"box plot\", \"candlestick chart\", \"stacked area chart\", \"stacked bar chart\", \"grouped bar chart\", \"donut chart\", \"waffle chart\", \"histogram\", \"parallel coordinates\", \"measured site's look\", \"theme a chart\", \"theme this chart\", \"theme the chart\"]},\n     \"FLOWCHART\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"flowchart\", \"ascii\", \"text diagram\", \"text characters\", \"decision tree\", \"process diagram\", \"flow diagram\", \"diagram the\", \"as a diagram\", \"create diagram\", \"diagram\", \"architecture diagram\", \"sequence diagram\", \"er diagram\", \"entity relationship diagram\", \"data model diagram\", \"state machine diagram\", \"swimlane diagram\", \"swimlane\", \"venn diagram\", \"org chart\", \"quadrant diagram\", \"gantt chart\", \"radar chart\", \"high-level diagram\", \"medallion diagram\", \"data flow diagram\", \"draw.io\", \"drawio\", \"mermaid diagram\", \"redraw diagram\", \"self-contained html diagram\", \"editorial diagram\", \"create flowchart\", \"ascii flowchart\", \"workflow diagram\", \"decision branch\", \"parallel execution diagram\", \"approval loop diagram\", \"export diagram\", \"create:diagram\", \"/design:diagram\", \"theme diagram\", \"repaint diagram\", \"brand the diagram\", \"venn\", \"mermaid\"]},\n     \"EXTRACT\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"extract\", \"design.md\", \"style reference\", \"design tokens\", \"measure this surface\", \"from a url\", \"from a site\", \"css extraction\", \"validate design.md\", \"style guide from\", \"measure\", \"extract design tokens\", \"measure a surface\", \"extract css\", \"design tokens from a site\", \"style guide from a url\"]},\n }\n \n RESOURCE_MAP = {\n-    \"VALUES\": [\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/references/hierarchy.md\",\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/references/color-system.md\",\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/assets/token-starter-set.md\",\n-    ],\n-    \"REVIEW\": [\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/references/review-checklist.md\",\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/references/ux-laws.md\",\n-        \"sk-design-fundamentals/references/diagnosis-table.md\",\n-    ],\n     \"CHART\": [\n         \"sk-design-chart/references/catalog.md\",\n         \"sk-design-chart/references/color-system.md\",\n@@ -107,8 +90,6 @@ RESOURCE_MAP = {\n - Two near-tied intents (within the ambiguity delta) route to both leaf sets; the union is deduped by\n   canonical pair and capped at the selected-map union limit. `CHART` and `FLOWCHART` are the pair most\n   likely to tie, because a request to visualise something rarely says which canvas it wants.\n-- `VALUES` and `REVIEW` resolve to the same mode. A tie between them is not ambiguity to escalate; it\n-  is one mode loading both leaf sets.\n - This map lists leaves, which is why no `SKILL.md` appears in it. A mode entry is loaded because the\n   registry named the mode, not from here.\n - Load what a row resolves and nothing more; a resource already in context is not re-read.\n@@ -131,8 +112,8 @@ no map of its own: the `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` block in section 3 st\n \n ### Surface Router, per-intent leaf sets\n \n-Stage 2 lives in section 3 of this file. It defines the five-intent leaf\n-model (VALUES, REVIEW, CHART, FLOWCHART, EXTRACT), the machine-readable `INTENT_SIGNALS` and\n+Stage 2 lives in section 3 of this file. It defines the three-intent leaf\n+model (CHART, FLOWCHART, EXTRACT), the machine-readable `INTENT_SIGNALS` and\n `RESOURCE_MAP` block the deterministic router-replay parses, and the how-to-read rules: a dominant\n intent takes one leaf set, near-tied intents take a deduped union, and no keyword match is the hub's\n UNKNOWN fallback rather than a silent default. Every `RESOURCE_MAP` path resolves on disk and\n@@ -142,11 +123,11 @@ This router stays a separate document from `SKILL.md` on purpose; [the parent-sk\n \n ### The discriminator\n \n-- **`workflowMode`** — the public mode key: `sk-design-fundamentals`, `sk-design-md-generator`,\n-  `sk-design-chart`, `sk-design-diagram`.\n-- **`packetKind`** — `workflow` for all four. There is no surface axis on this hub.\n-- **`backendKind`** — `surface-router` for fundamentals and the generator, which resolve leaves from\n-  a reference set; `template-scaffold` for chart and diagram, which build an artifact from a form.\n+- **`workflowMode`** — the public mode key: `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart`,\n+  `sk-design-diagram`.\n+- **`packetKind`** — `workflow` for all three. There is no surface axis on this hub.\n+- **`backendKind`** — `surface-router` for the generator, which resolves leaves from a reference\n+  set. `template-scaffold` for chart and diagram, which build an artifact from a form.\n \n ### Routing rule\n \n@@ -156,8 +137,8 @@ REGISTRY    = SKILL_ROOT / \"mode-registry.json\"\n HUB_ROUTER  = SKILL_ROOT / \"hub-router.json\"\n \n UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [\n-    \"Confirm whether this decides a value, reviews a surface, measures an existing surface, or builds a chart or diagram\",\n-    \"Confirm the surface: screen UI, slide deck, printed page, document layout, or a chart or diagram canvas\",\n+    \"Confirm whether this measures an existing surface or builds a chart or diagram\",\n+    \"A request to decide a value or review a screen belongs to sk-code, not this hub\",\n     \"For a measure request, provide the live URL or path; there is nothing to read without one\",\n     \"For a canvas request, state the question the artifact must answer, not the form you want\",\n ]\n@@ -187,7 +168,6 @@ classify the request to one or more workflowMode values using hub-router.json\n \n if two intents tie within routerPolicy.ambiguityDelta:\n   apply routerPolicy.tieBreak, then take the deduped union of their leaf sets\n-  VALUES and REVIEW resolving together is not ambiguity: they are one mode loading both sets\n \n if confidence is low or the intent is contradictory:\n   return UNKNOWN_FALLBACK with disambiguation_checklist = UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST\n@@ -202,6 +182,5 @@ for each resolved workflowMode:\n return single or ambiguous according to hub-router.json routerPolicy.outcomes\n ```\n \n-`routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `sk-design-fundamentals`: a design question with no clearer owner is a\n-values question. That differs from `sk-doc`, whose default is `null` because an unclear documentation\n-intent has no safe default. The outcomes `routerPolicy.outcomes` defines are `single`, `orderedBundle`, `defer` and `none`.\n+`routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`: a design request with no clearer owner has no safe default\n+among the three artifacts, so it defers and asks which one is wanted. The outcomes `routerPolicy.outcomes` defines are `single`, `orderedBundle`, `defer` and `none`.\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md\nindex 6647d3a6a9..4f12d86645 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md\n@@ -1,13 +1,13 @@\n ---\n name: sk-design\n-description: \"Design parent hub. Routes one design identity to the mode that owns the decision, starting with sk-design-fundamentals.\"\n+description: \"Design parent hub. Routes one design identity to the mode that owns the artifact: a measured Style Reference, a chart or a diagram.\"\n allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n-version: 2.0.11.0\n+version: 3.0.0.0\n metadata:\n   family: sk-design\n ---\n \n-<!-- Keywords: design, spacing, padding, typography, colour, contrast, hierarchy, design review, ux laws, design fundamentals -->\n+<!-- Keywords: design, style reference, design.md, extract design tokens, chart, diagram, flowchart -->\n \n # Design (parent hub)\n \n@@ -18,31 +18,25 @@ decision in front of you and hands over. The work lives in the modes.\n \n ## 1. WHEN TO USE\n \n-Use this hub when the question is what a surface should look like, why it looks wrong, or what\n-visual artifact answers it: spacing, type, colour, contrast, hierarchy, a review of an existing\n-surface against design criteria, a data chart, or a process diagram. The surface can be screen UI, a\n-slide deck, a printed page or a document layout.\n+Use this hub when the answer is a design artifact: a measured Style Reference of an existing\n+surface, a data chart, or a process diagram.\n \n | Mode | Command | Owns | Reach it by asking about |\n |------|---------|------|--------------------------|\n-| `sk-design-fundamentals` | routes via aliases | The values a surface is built from, and reviewing a surface against them | spacing, padding, type scale, colour, contrast, hierarchy, design review |\n | `sk-design-md-generator` | `/design:extract` | Measuring an existing surface into a Style Reference, and validating one | extract, design.md, design tokens, from a url |\n | `sk-design-chart` | `/design:chart` | Chart forms: which one answers the question, and building it as a self-contained file | chart, plot, heatmap, bar chart, chart catalog |\n | `sk-design-diagram` | `/design:diagram` | Flowcharts and text diagrams | diagram, flowchart, ascii diagram, mermaid, drawio |\n \n-Four modes. Fundamentals and the generator are complements rather than alternatives: one decides values, the other reads values back\n-off something that already exists. A request that names an existing surface belongs to the\n-generator; a request that asks what a value should be belongs to fundamentals.\n+Three modes. The generator reads values back off something that already exists. Chart and diagram\n+each build one self-contained canvas.\n \n ### When NOT to Use\n \n-- **Measuring a surface that already exists into a written specification.** That is this hub's\n-  EXTRACT mode, reached by naming the source; it is not the values path.\n+- **Deciding a value or reviewing a screen.** Spacing, type, colour, contrast, hierarchy, motion\n+  and visual review belong to `sk-code`, whose frontend surface carries the value scales and the\n+  review pass.\n - **Authoring documentation prose.** `sk-doc` owns that, including READMEs, changelogs and playbooks.\n-- **Implementing the values once decided.** `sk-code` owns the code that renders them; this hub\n-  decides what they should be and never writes the component.\n-- **A canvas question that names its own form.** A chart or diagram request goes to its mode\n-  directly rather than through the values mode.\n+- **Implementing a component.** `sk-code` owns the code that renders it.\n \n ---\n \n@@ -52,14 +46,14 @@ Routing runs in two stages.\n Stage one picks a mode from this hub.\n `hub-router.json` is its one authored vocabulary.\n `vocabularyClasses` holds the terms, and `routerSignals` maps each mode to the classes it scores.\n-The four modes are `sk-design-fundamentals`, `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart` and `sk-design-diagram`.\n+The three modes are `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart` and `sk-design-diagram`.\n Stage two maps the chosen mode to its leaves in the root [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md).\n The two layers stay separate: the hub never emits leaf paths, and the surface router never re-decides the mode.\n The advisor routes every design query to the single identity `sk-design`.\n Run the compiled-routing directive in [`ROUTER.md`](./ROUTER.md) before selecting hub resources.\n Resolve the mode with `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-design --prompt \"<task>\"`.\n Act on the decision: `route` loads its targets, `clarify` and `defer` ask, `reject` refuses.\n-With no signal at all, `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `sk-design-fundamentals`, so the request lands on the values mode rather than asking.\n+With no signal at all, `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `null`, so the request defers and asks which artifact is wanted.\n \n ---\n \n@@ -67,17 +61,17 @@ With no signal at all, `routerPolicy.defaultMode` is `sk-design-fundamentals`, s\n \n ### Terms\n \n-- **`workflowMode`**: the public mode key, one of `sk-design-fundamentals`, `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart` or `sk-design-diagram`.\n-- **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for all four modes, because this hub has no surface axis.\n-- **`backendKind`**: `surface-router` for fundamentals and the generator, which resolve leaves from a reference set, while `template-scaffold` for chart and diagram builds an artifact from a form.\n+- **`workflowMode`**: the public mode key, one of `sk-design-md-generator`, `sk-design-chart` or `sk-design-diagram`.\n+- **`packetKind`**: `workflow` for all three modes, because this hub has no surface axis.\n+- **`backendKind`**: `surface-router` for the generator, which resolves leaves from a reference set, while `template-scaffold` for chart and diagram builds an artifact from a form.\n - **`routingClass`**: `metadata` on every nested mode, so the advisor resolves this hub by membership and holds no entry of its own per mode.\n - **`mode-registry.json`**: what modes exist and what each may touch.\n - **`hub-router.json`**: stage one's signals, vocabulary classes, tie-break and default mode.\n - **`vocabularyClasses`**: the terms stage one matches, with `routerSignals` naming the classes each mode scores.\n-- **`tieBreak`**: the `routerPolicy` order that ranks the four modes when scores are close.\n-- **`routerPolicy.defaultMode`**: `sk-design-fundamentals`, the mode a request with no signal at all lands on.\n+- **`tieBreak`**: the `routerPolicy` order that ranks the three modes when scores are close.\n+- **`routerPolicy.defaultMode`**: `null`, so a request with no signal at all defers instead of landing on a mode.\n - **leaf**: a resource a chosen mode loads, counted as a canonical `(workflowMode, leafResourceId)` pair through `leaf-manifest.json`.\n-- **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` over the five leaf intents, VALUES, REVIEW, CHART, FLOWCHART and EXTRACT.\n+- **`ROUTER.md`**: stage two's `INTENT_SIGNALS` and `RESOURCE_MAP` over the three leaf intents, CHART, FLOWCHART and EXTRACT.\n - **`intent_signals`**: the `graph-metadata.json` field that carries this hub's vocabulary to the advisor, since a `description.json` keyword is documentation and not scored.\n \n ### Layout\n@@ -91,7 +85,6 @@ sk-design/\n ├── graph-metadata.json      the only vocabulary the advisor scores\n ├── command-metadata.json    the commands this hub owns, and which mode owns each\n ├── shared/scripts/          tooling both canvas modes use\n-├── sk-design-fundamentals/  the values mode, and everything it owns\n ├── sk-design-md-generator/  the extraction mode, its engine and style corpus\n ├── sk-design-chart/         the chart corpus, its checker, gallery and screenshots\n └── sk-design-diagram/       the diagram forms, their validator and screenshots\n@@ -143,7 +136,6 @@ green gate all leave a request unable to arrive. Only replaying the request prov\n | `mode-registry.json` | What modes exist, and what each may touch |\n | `hub-router.json` | Signals, vocabulary classes, tie-break |\n | `ROUTER.md` | Stage two: which resources a chosen mode loads |\n-| `sk-design-fundamentals/` | The values mode, and everything it owns |\n | `sk-design-md-generator/` | The extraction mode, its engine and its style corpus |\n | `sk-design-chart/` | The chart corpus and its checker |\n | `sk-design-diagram/` | The diagram forms and their validator |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && git diff 10474a9567 -- .skilled/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/sk-design/ROUTER.md | head -260\"}"},"time":{"start":1793872945537,"end":1793872945933}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793872950138,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab28e047002aFcM3b6lh6gHtZ","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab28d787001ebZ20NxxgFG0Ib","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3e576437a2e4085","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \"sk-design-fundamentals\" --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=specs . 2>/dev/null | grep -v \"^./.skilled/changelog/\" | head -60"},"output":"./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/phrase-variants.json:90925:      \"retire sk-design-fundamentals\"\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/corpus-manifest.json:15026:    \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/goal.md\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/corpus-manifest.json:15027:    \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/implementation-summary.md\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/corpus-manifest.json:15028:    \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/plan.md\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/corpus-manifest.json:15029:    \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/spec.md\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/corpus-manifest.json:15030:    \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/tasks.md\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/corpus-manifest.json:32371:      \"path\": \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/scratch\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/fixtures/generation-diagnostics.json:73135:      \"path\": \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/scratch\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json:8283:    \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/goal.md\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json:8284:    \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/implementation-summary.md\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json:8285:    \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/plan.md\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json:8286:    \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/spec.md\",\n./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/data/trigger-index.json:8287:    \"specs/sk-doc/066-skill-readability-refinement/007-sk-design/004-sk-design-fundamentals/tasks.md\",\n./.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:3:description: \"Three playbook scenarios cover a Figma read feeding code, and open visual values now go to sk-design-fundamentals.\"\n./.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/changelog/v1.2.0.0.md:24:- **Open values have an owner.** When a request or a frame leaves a visual value open, or a value sits off every token and scale, `sk-design-fundamentals` decides it.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/skill-benchmark-report.md:60:The load-bearing finding differs from the headline: **the default mode hides vocabulary gaps.** A prompt that hits no keyword in any mode goes to `sk-design-fundamentals` (`hub-router.json:5`, `canary-router.cjs:301-307`). Seven of the eleven fundamentals matches reached their gold that way, with zero keyword hits. Nine of the twelve misses reached `sk-design-fundamentals` the same way. The fundamentals row therefore measures the default setting, not the fundamentals vocabulary. That vocabulary hit only 3 of its own 12 prompts.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/skill-benchmark-report.md:74:| `SKD-030` | `stage: negative` (`sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/boundary/extraction-defers-to-md-generator.md:4`). Expects `sk-design-md-generator` ranked first (`:33`, `:35`) | `sk-design-md-generator` | The expected target is a mode of this hub, so the scenario's own answer is scoreable at the hub front door. The admission script's negative rule (pass only on no route, `compiled-route-admission.cjs:276`, `:288-292`) was not used: it treats \"negative\" as \"not this hub\", and this target is inside the hub |\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/skill-benchmark-report.md:160:`CHT-001`, `CHT-002`, `CHT-003`, `CHT-004`, `CHT-006`, `CHT-007`, `CHT-009`, `A11Y-001` and `PROVENANCE-001` score zero in every mode and land on `sk-design-fundamentals`.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/skill-benchmark-report.md:241:Not applicable to this run. Reason: this is the first hub-level routing run archived for sk-design. `benchmark/README.md` section 1 records that no Lane C hub run was archived before that runner was retired. The per-mode baselines under `sk-design-fundamentals/benchmark/` and `sk-design-diagram/benchmark/` measure a mode, not the hub route, so they are not a before-number for this run.\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:37:probe 'SKD-030 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/boundary/extraction-defers-to-md-generator.md' 'Extract the design system from stripe.com.'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:38:probe 'SKD-031 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/boundary/implementation-defers-to-sk-code.md' 'Write the API client for this form.'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:39:probe 'SKD-021 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/conflict-handling/contrast-escape-hatches.md' 'Our brand green fails contrast on white, what do we do?'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:40:probe 'SKD-020 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/conflict-handling/project-system-precedence.md' 'Our design system says 24px spacing here, but you suggested 32px.'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:41:probe 'SKD-022 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/conflict-handling/shadow-system-consistency.md' 'Add a drop shadow to this card.'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:42:probe 'SKD-001 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/routing/diagnose-entry.md' 'This dashboard looks amateur, can you make it better?'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:43:probe 'SKD-003 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/routing/motion-entry.md' 'How long should this dropdown animation be?'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:44:probe 'SKD-004 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/routing/procedure-entry.md' 'I need to design a new settings screen, where do I start?'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:45:probe 'SKD-002 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/routing/review-entry.md' 'Can you review this component for accessibility problems?'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:46:probe 'SKD-011 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/value-discipline/no-runtime-shades.md' 'I need a slightly darker blue for the hover state, can you just darken it 10%?'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:47:probe 'SKD-010 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/value-discipline/on-scale-values.md' 'How much padding should this card have?'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-run.sh:48:probe 'SKD-012 | sk-design-fundamentals | sk-design-fundamentals/manual-testing-playbook/value-discipline/unit-discipline.md' 'Set the headline to 2.5em'\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-after-fix.txt:4:ROUTE: {\"hubId\":\"sk-design\",\"action\":\"route\",\"selectionKind\":\"single\",\"targets\":[{\"backendKind\":\"surface-router\",\"packetId\":\"sk-design-fundamentals\",\"packetKind\":\"workflow\",\"skillId\":\"sk-design\",\"workflowMode\":\"sk-design-fundamentals\"}],\"effectivePolicyHash\":\"cdc874749f2cf8babb969500f411045747280859667e3adaff6797017817d581\",\"generation\":1}\n./.skilled/skills/sk-design/benchmark/reports/2026-09-27--manual-testing-playbook--hub-routing-replay/raw/mode-routing-after-fix.tx