{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793872958992,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab29141c001IclaCvETCWLOU7","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab290946001frjgCT0FJtyU1g","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f390845a046d26c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && git diff 10474a9567 -- .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md\nindex bff0fc1044..14e72e903f 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md\n@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ Frontend work needs shared rules that hold across frameworks, with a web layer f\n \n ### What It Holds\n \n-[`references/frontend-practice.md`](references/frontend-practice.md) is the core page for shared principles, token guidance, Figma as reference, and overrides. The web layer is [`references/web-markup-and-css.md`](references/web-markup-and-css.md). Six web topic files provide focused guidance, and [`references/figma-to-code.md`](references/figma-to-code.md) defines the five-pass check and its verdicts.\n+[`references/frontend-practice.md`](references/frontend-practice.md) is the core page for shared principles, token guidance, Figma as reference, and overrides. The web layer is [`references/web-markup-and-css.md`](references/web-markup-and-css.md). Six web topic files provide focused guidance, three visual topic files decide values, hierarchy and motion, and [`references/figma-to-code.md`](references/figma-to-code.md) defines the five-pass check and its verdicts.\n \n The packet is read-only. The paired workflow mode applies its evidence to the requested work.\n \n@@ -48,8 +48,10 @@ The packet is read-only. The paired workflow mode applies its evidence to the re\n | `references/frontend-practice.md` | Shared principles, token precedence, the Figma boundary, and the Frontend overrides contract |\n | `references/web-markup-and-css.md` | Semantic web markup, forms, layout, responsive behavior, media, CSS architecture, and framework examples |\n | Six web topic files | [Elements and attributes](references/web-elements-and-attributes.md), [cascade and selectors](references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md), [layout and sizing](references/web-layout-and-sizing.md), [accessibility patterns](references/web-accessibility-patterns.md), [performance and loading](references/web-performance-and-loading.md) and [internationalization](references/web-internationalization.md) |\n+| Three visual topic files | [Visual values](references/web-visual-values.md), [visual hierarchy and review](references/web-visual-hierarchy.md) and [motion and interaction](references/web-motion-and-interaction.md) |\n+| `assets/tokens.css` | A contrast-verified starter token file for a project with no token layer |\n | `references/figma-to-code.md` | Read-only inputs, five passes, the verdict and report, and the Figma-side tool ladder |\n-| `manual-testing-playbook/` | The routing scenarios the hub's router-sync guard replays: one web and one Figma check |\n+| `manual-testing-playbook/` | The routing scenarios the hub's router-sync guard replays: one web, one Figma check and one visual-values scenario |\n | `references/workflow-*.md` | Shared [implement](references/workflow-implement.md), [debug](references/workflow-debug.md) and [verify](references/workflow-verify.md) workflow doctrine |\n | `changelog/` | Release history for this surface |\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md\nindex a1bf03145f..0d8ae7cab5 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"figma to code routing\"\n importance_tier: normal\n contextType: general\n-version: 1.0.3.0\n+version: 1.1.0.0\n router_state: active\n skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n ---\n@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ The machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). The core reference is the defau\n \n ## 1. OVERVIEW\n \n-This surface holds the core in `references/frontend-practice.md`, the web layer in `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, six web topic files, and the five-pass Figma check in `references/figma-to-code.md`. Every intent loads the core and the matching web or Figma-to-code layer. Topic files load when the request touches their listed concern.\n+This surface holds the core in `references/frontend-practice.md`, the web layer in `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, nine web topic files, the starter token file `assets/tokens.css`, and the five-pass Figma check in `references/figma-to-code.md`. Every intent loads the core and the matching web or Figma-to-code layer. Topic files load when the request touches their listed concern.\n \n ### Web Topic Files\n \n@@ -29,6 +29,9 @@ This surface holds the core in `references/frontend-practice.md`, the web layer\n | Accessibility patterns | [web-accessibility-patterns.md](references/web-accessibility-patterns.md) | Changing a widget pattern, accessible name, focus behavior, live region, browser preference, or form validation and error messaging |\n | Performance and loading | [web-performance-and-loading.md](references/web-performance-and-loading.md) | Changing vitals, resource loading, image delivery, fonts, or main-thread work |\n | Internationalization | [web-internationalization.md](references/web-internationalization.md) | Changing locale, direction, bidirectional text, formatting, or translation tolerance |\n+| Visual values | [web-visual-values.md](references/web-visual-values.md) | Choosing a spacing, type, weight, colour, shadow, radius or opacity value, or building a palette or token set |\n+| Visual hierarchy and review | [web-visual-hierarchy.md](references/web-visual-hierarchy.md) | Fixing a screen that looks wrong, starting a new screen, applying UX laws, or reviewing a screen's visual quality |\n+| Motion and interaction | [web-motion-and-interaction.md](references/web-motion-and-interaction.md) | Adding or tuning animation, or deciding input, touch, state and feedback behavior |\n \n ---\n \n@@ -38,9 +41,12 @@ This surface holds the core in `references/frontend-practice.md`, the web layer\n - **`WEB_ELEMENTS`** fires on `html form autocomplete`, `dialog element`, or `popover attribute`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-elements-and-attributes.md`.\n - **`WEB_CASCADE`** fires on `css cascade layers` or `css specificity conflict`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md`.\n - **`WEB_LAYOUT`** fires on `container query layout` or `css stacking context`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-layout-and-sizing.md`.\n-- **`WEB_A11Y`** fires on `web accessibility pattern`, `focus visible styling`, `keyboard focus`, `broken tab order`, `accessible name`, or `aria live region`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-accessibility-patterns.md`.\n+- **`WEB_A11Y`** fires on `web accessibility pattern`, `focus visible styling`, `keyboard focus`, `broken tab order`, `accessible name`, `aria live region`, `focus ring accessibility`, `focus outline removed`, `screen reader support`, `aria label missing`, `alt text missing`, or `wcag audit`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-accessibility-patterns.md`.\n - **`WEB_PERF`** fires on `web font loading` or `largest contentful paint`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-performance-and-loading.md`.\n - **`WEB_I18N`** fires on `right to left layout` or `bidirectional text`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-internationalization.md`.\n+- **`WEB_VISUAL_VALUES`** fires on `what padding should this have`, `how much padding`, `what font size should this be`, `spacing between elements`, `spacing scale`, `type scale`, `build a color palette`, `shade ramp`, `box shadow elevation`, `border radius consistency`, `contrast ratio failure`, `grey text on colored background`, `dark mode palette`, `concentric border radius`, `layered shadows`, `shadow color on dark surface`, `tabular numbers`, `what should this button look like`, `colour decision`, `color decision`, `padding`, `type scale for`, `font size`, `colour palette`, `color palette`, `contrast ratio`, `corner radius`, `box shadow`, or `spacing between`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md` and `references/web-visual-values.md`.\n+- **`WEB_VISUAL_HIERARCHY`** fires on `ui looks off`, `looks amateur`, `feels cluttered`, `make this look better`, `make this ui look designed`, `visual hierarchy`, `no visual hierarchy`, `nothing draws the eye`, `everything competes for attention`, `everything looks the same`, `emphasize by de-emphasizing`, `how to style a destructive button`, `this page feels overwhelming`, `where do i start designing`, `design a new screen from scratch`, `how much white space`, `why does this look wrong`, `does this look right`, `critique this design`, `design critique`, `visual audit`, `design review findings`, `review this screen`, `ux laws`, `cognitive load`, `progressive disclosure`, `empty state design`, `look wrong`, `looks wrong`, `looks off`, or `visual review`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-visual-hierarchy.md`, and `references/web-visual-values.md`.\n+- **`WEB_MOTION`** fires on `animation duration`, `transition duration`, `easing curve`, `spring versus easing`, `twelve principles of animation`, `when not to animate`, `response time budget`, `touch target size`, `hover state`, `active pressed state`, `disabled state styling`, `button states`, `animation`, `transition timing`, or `easing`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md` and `references/web-motion-and-interaction.md`.\n - **`FIGMA_TO_CODE`** fires on `figma to code`, `check built screen against figma`, `compare build with figma frame`, `figma frame`, `figma frame check`, or `implement a figma design`. It loads `references/figma-to-code.md` and `references/frontend-practice.md`.\n \n ---\n@@ -55,9 +61,12 @@ INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n     \"WEB_ELEMENTS\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"html form autocomplete\", \"dialog element\", \"popover attribute\"]},\n     \"WEB_CASCADE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"css cascade layers\", \"css specificity conflict\"]},\n     \"WEB_LAYOUT\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"container query layout\", \"css stacking context\"]},\n-    \"WEB_A11Y\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"web accessibility pattern\", \"focus visible styling\", \"keyboard focus\", \"broken tab order\", \"accessible name\", \"aria live region\"]},\n+    \"WEB_A11Y\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"web accessibility pattern\", \"focus visible styling\", \"keyboard focus\", \"broken tab order\", \"accessible name\", \"aria live region\", \"focus ring accessibility\", \"focus outline removed\", \"screen reader support\", \"aria label missing\", \"alt text missing\", \"wcag audit\"]},\n     \"WEB_PERF\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"web font loading\", \"largest contentful paint\"]},\n     \"WEB_I18N\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"right to left layout\", \"bidirectional text\"]},\n+    \"WEB_VISUAL_VALUES\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"what padding should this have\", \"how much padding\", \"what font size should this be\", \"spacing between elements\", \"spacing scale\", \"type scale\", \"build a color palette\", \"shade ramp\", \"box shadow elevation\", \"border radius consistency\", \"contrast ratio failure\", \"grey text on colored background\", \"dark mode palette\", \"concentric border radius\", \"layered shadows\", \"shadow color on dark surface\", \"tabular numbers\", \"what should this button look like\", \"colour decision\", \"color decision\", \"padding\", \"type scale for\", \"font size\", \"colour palette\", \"color palette\", \"contrast ratio\", \"corner radius\", \"box shadow\", \"spacing between\"]},\n+    \"WEB_VISUAL_HIERARCHY\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"ui looks off\", \"looks amateur\", \"feels cluttered\", \"make this look better\", \"make this ui look designed\", \"visual hierarchy\", \"no visual hierarchy\", \"nothing draws the eye\", \"everything competes for attention\", \"everything looks the same\", \"emphasize by de-emphasizing\", \"how to style a destructive button\", \"this page feels overwhelming\", \"where do i start designing\", \"design a new screen from scratch\", \"how much white space\", \"why does this look wrong\", \"does this look right\", \"critique this design\", \"design critique\", \"visual audit\", \"design review findings\", \"review this screen\", \"ux laws\", \"cognitive load\", \"progressive disclosure\", \"empty state design\", \"look wrong\", \"looks wrong\", \"looks off\", \"visual review\"]},\n+    \"WEB_MOTION\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"animation duration\", \"transition duration\", \"easing curve\", \"spring versus easing\", \"twelve principles of animation\", \"when not to animate\", \"response time budget\", \"touch target size\", \"hover state\", \"active pressed state\", \"disabled state styling\", \"button states\", \"animation\", \"transition timing\", \"easing\"]},\n     \"FIGMA_TO_CODE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"figma to code\", \"check built screen against figma\", \"compare build with figma frame\", \"figma frame\", \"figma frame check\", \"implement a figma design\"]},\n }\n \n@@ -96,6 +105,19 @@ RESOURCE_MAP = {\n         \"references/web-markup-and-css.md\",\n         \"references/web-internationalization.md\",\n     ],\n+    \"WEB_VISUAL_VALUES\": [\n+        \"references/frontend-practice.md\",\n+        \"references/web-visual-values.md\",\n+    ],\n+    \"WEB_VISUAL_HIERARCHY\": [\n+        \"references/frontend-practice.md\",\n+        \"references/web-visual-hierarchy.md\",\n+        \"references/web-visual-values.md\",\n+    ],\n+    \"WEB_MOTION\": [\n+        \"references/frontend-practice.md\",\n+        \"references/web-motion-and-interaction.md\",\n+    ],\n     \"FIGMA_TO_CODE\": [\n         \"references/figma-to-code.md\",\n         \"references/frontend-practice.md\",\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md\nindex 3a1905e43d..887bf70317 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md\n@@ -1,8 +1,8 @@\n ---\n name: sk-code-frontend\n-description: Read-only frontend evidence for stack-agnostic web practice, topic references, and Figma checks.\n+description: Read-only frontend evidence for stack-agnostic web practice, visual values, topic references, and Figma checks.\n allowed-tools: [Read, Bash, Grep, Glob]\n-version: 1.0.4.0\n+version: 1.1.0.0\n metadata:\n   family: sk-code\n   packetKind: surface\n@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ Read-only frontend evidence for web work across project stacks.\n \n ## 1. WHEN THE HUB BUNDLES THIS\n \n-The sk-code hub bundles this surface beside `sk-code-quality` for authoring or `sk-code-review` for review when a request needs shared web frontend practice, or a Figma-to-code check, and it routes this surface alone when no workflow mode scores.\n+The sk-code hub bundles this surface beside `sk-code-quality` for authoring or `sk-code-review` for review when a request needs shared web frontend practice, a visual value or visual review, or a Figma-to-code check, and it routes this surface alone when no workflow mode scores.\n \n This packet writes nothing. When the hub bundles it beside a workflow mode, that mode applies the guidance it loads. When no workflow mode scores, the hub routes this packet alone, and the acting agent applies the guidance and hands the author gates to `sk-code-quality` before it claims completion.\n \n@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@ This packet writes nothing. When the hub bundles it beside a workflow mode, that\n - [`references/frontend-practice.md`](references/frontend-practice.md) holds the shared principles and the Frontend overrides contract.\n - [`references/web-markup-and-css.md`](references/web-markup-and-css.md) is the web layer.\n - The six web topic files cover focused implementation details for web work: [`references/web-elements-and-attributes.md`](references/web-elements-and-attributes.md), [`references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md`](references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md), [`references/web-layout-and-sizing.md`](references/web-layout-and-sizing.md), [`references/web-accessibility-patterns.md`](references/web-accessibility-patterns.md), [`references/web-performance-and-loading.md`](references/web-performance-and-loading.md) and [`references/web-internationalization.md`](references/web-internationalization.md).\n+- Three visual topic files decide what a surface looks like and how it behaves: [`references/web-visual-values.md`](references/web-visual-values.md) holds the value scales, colour ramps, elevation, tokens and hard rules, [`references/web-visual-hierarchy.md`](references/web-visual-hierarchy.md) holds the build procedure, symptom-to-fix tables, hierarchy method, UX laws and visual review pass, and [`references/web-motion-and-interaction.md`](references/web-motion-and-interaction.md) holds motion, input, touch, focus, performance and feedback rules.\n+- [`assets/tokens.css`](assets/tokens.css) is a contrast-verified starter token file for a project with no token layer.\n - [`references/figma-to-code.md`](references/figma-to-code.md) holds the five-pass check for comparing a built screen with its Figma frame.\n - [`references/workflow-implement.md`](references/workflow-implement.md), [`references/workflow-debug.md`](references/workflow-debug.md), and [`references/workflow-verify.md`](references/workflow-verify.md) provide the shared workflow doctrine.\n \n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md\nindex bff0fc1044..14e72e903f 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md\n@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ Frontend work needs shared rules that hold across frameworks, with a web layer f\n \n ### What It Holds\n \n-[`references/frontend-practice.md`](references/frontend-practice.md) is the core page for shared principles, token guidance, Figma as reference, and overrides. The web layer is [`references/web-markup-and-css.md`](references/web-markup-and-css.md). Six web topic files provide focused guidance, and [`references/figma-to-code.md`](references/figma-to-code.md) defines the five-pass check and its verdicts.\n+[`references/frontend-practice.md`](references/frontend-practice.md) is the core page for shared principles, token guidance, Figma as reference, and overrides. The web layer is [`references/web-markup-and-css.md`](references/web-markup-and-css.md). Six web topic files provide focused guidance, three visual topic files decide values, hierarchy and motion, and [`references/figma-to-code.md`](references/figma-to-code.md) defines the five-pass check and its verdicts.\n \n The packet is read-only. The paired workflow mode applies its evidence to the requested work.\n \n@@ -48,8 +48,10 @@ The packet is read-only. The paired workflow mode applies its evidence to the re\n | `references/frontend-practice.md` | Shared principles, token precedence, the Figma boundary, and the Frontend overrides contract |\n | `references/web-markup-and-css.md` | Semantic web markup, forms, layout, responsive behavior, media, CSS architecture, and framework examples |\n | Six web topic files | [Elements and attributes](references/web-elements-and-attributes.md), [cascade and selectors](references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md), [layout and sizing](references/web-layout-and-sizing.md), [accessibility patterns](references/web-accessibility-patterns.md), [performance and loading](references/web-performance-and-loading.md) and [internationalization](references/web-internationalization.md) |\n+| Three visual topic files | [Visual values](references/web-visual-values.md), [visual hierarchy and review](references/web-visual-hierarchy.md) and [motion and interaction](references/web-motion-and-interaction.md) |\n+| `assets/tokens.css` | A contrast-verified starter token file for a project with no token layer |\n | `references/figma-to-code.md` | Read-only inputs, five passes, the verdict and report, and the Figma-side tool ladder |\n-| `manual-testing-playbook/` | The routing scenarios the hub's router-sync guard replays: one web and one Figma check |\n+| `manual-testing-playbook/` | The routing scenarios the hub's router-sync guard replays: one web, one Figma check and one visual-values scenario |\n | `references/workflow-*.md` | Shared [implement](references/workflow-implement.md), [debug](references/workflow-debug.md) and [verify](references/workflow-verify.md) workflow doctrine |\n | `changelog/` | Release history for this surface |\n \ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md\nindex a1bf03145f..0d8ae7cab5 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md\n@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ trigger_phrases:\n   - \"figma to code routing\"\n importance_tier: normal\n contextType: general\n-version: 1.0.3.0\n+version: 1.1.0.0\n router_state: active\n skill_pointer: SKILL.md\n ---\n@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ The machine router for [`SKILL.md`](./SKILL.md). The core reference is the defau\n \n ## 1. OVERVIEW\n \n-This surface holds the core in `references/frontend-practice.md`, the web layer in `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, six web topic files, and the five-pass Figma check in `references/figma-to-code.md`. Every intent loads the core and the matching web or Figma-to-code layer. Topic files load when the request touches their listed concern.\n+This surface holds the core in `references/frontend-practice.md`, the web layer in `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, nine web topic files, the starter token file `assets/tokens.css`, and the five-pass Figma check in `references/figma-to-code.md`. Every intent loads the core and the matching web or Figma-to-code layer. Topic files load when the request touches their listed concern.\n \n ### Web Topic Files\n \n@@ -29,6 +29,9 @@ This surface holds the core in `references/frontend-practice.md`, the web layer\n | Accessibility patterns | [web-accessibility-patterns.md](references/web-accessibility-patterns.md) | Changing a widget pattern, accessible name, focus behavior, live region, browser preference, or form validation and error messaging |\n | Performance and loading | [web-performance-and-loading.md](references/web-performance-and-loading.md) | Changing vitals, resource loading, image delivery, fonts, or main-thread work |\n | Internationalization | [web-internationalization.md](references/web-internationalization.md) | Changing locale, direction, bidirectional text, formatting, or translation tolerance |\n+| Visual values | [web-visual-values.md](references/web-visual-values.md) | Choosing a spacing, type, weight, colour, shadow, radius or opacity value, or building a palette or token set |\n+| Visual hierarchy and review | [web-visual-hierarchy.md](references/web-visual-hierarchy.md) | Fixing a screen that looks wrong, starting a new screen, applying UX laws, or reviewing a screen's visual quality |\n+| Motion and interaction | [web-motion-and-interaction.md](references/web-motion-and-interaction.md) | Adding or tuning animation, or deciding input, touch, state and feedback behavior |\n \n ---\n \n@@ -38,9 +41,12 @@ This surface holds the core in `references/frontend-practice.md`, the web layer\n - **`WEB_ELEMENTS`** fires on `html form autocomplete`, `dialog element`, or `popover attribute`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-elements-and-attributes.md`.\n - **`WEB_CASCADE`** fires on `css cascade layers` or `css specificity conflict`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-cascade-and-selectors.md`.\n - **`WEB_LAYOUT`** fires on `container query layout` or `css stacking context`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-layout-and-sizing.md`.\n-- **`WEB_A11Y`** fires on `web accessibility pattern`, `focus visible styling`, `keyboard focus`, `broken tab order`, `accessible name`, or `aria live region`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-accessibility-patterns.md`.\n+- **`WEB_A11Y`** fires on `web accessibility pattern`, `focus visible styling`, `keyboard focus`, `broken tab order`, `accessible name`, `aria live region`, `focus ring accessibility`, `focus outline removed`, `screen reader support`, `aria label missing`, `alt text missing`, or `wcag audit`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-accessibility-patterns.md`.\n - **`WEB_PERF`** fires on `web font loading` or `largest contentful paint`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-performance-and-loading.md`.\n - **`WEB_I18N`** fires on `right to left layout` or `bidirectional text`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-markup-and-css.md`, and `references/web-internationalization.md`.\n+- **`WEB_VISUAL_VALUES`** fires on `what padding should this have`, `how much padding`, `what font size should this be`, `spacing between elements`, `spacing scale`, `type scale`, `build a color palette`, `shade ramp`, `box shadow elevation`, `border radius consistency`, `contrast ratio failure`, `grey text on colored background`, `dark mode palette`, `concentric border radius`, `layered shadows`, `shadow color on dark surface`, `tabular numbers`, `what should this button look like`, `colour decision`, `color decision`, `padding`, `type scale for`, `font size`, `colour palette`, `color palette`, `contrast ratio`, `corner radius`, `box shadow`, or `spacing between`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md` and `references/web-visual-values.md`.\n+- **`WEB_VISUAL_HIERARCHY`** fires on `ui looks off`, `looks amateur`, `feels cluttered`, `make this look better`, `make this ui look designed`, `visual hierarchy`, `no visual hierarchy`, `nothing draws the eye`, `everything competes for attention`, `everything looks the same`, `emphasize by de-emphasizing`, `how to style a destructive button`, `this page feels overwhelming`, `where do i start designing`, `design a new screen from scratch`, `how much white space`, `why does this look wrong`, `does this look right`, `critique this design`, `design critique`, `visual audit`, `design review findings`, `review this screen`, `ux laws`, `cognitive load`, `progressive disclosure`, `empty state design`, `look wrong`, `looks wrong`, `looks off`, or `visual review`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-visual-hierarchy.md`, and `references/web-visual-values.md`.\n+- **`WEB_MOTION`** fires on `animation duration`, `transition duration`, `easing curve`, `spring versus easing`, `twelve principles of animation`, `when not to animate`, `response time budget`, `touch target size`, `hover state`, `active pressed state`, `disabled state styling`, `button states`, `animation`, `transition timing`, or `easing`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md` and `references/web-motion-and-interaction.md`.\n - **`FIGMA_TO_CODE`** fires on `figma to code`, `check built screen against figma`, `compare build with figma frame`, `figma frame`, `figma frame check`, or `implement a figma design`. It loads `references/figma-to-code.md` and `references/frontend-practice.md`.\n \n ---\n@@ -55,9 +61,12 @@ INTENT_SIGNALS = {\n     \"WEB_ELEMENTS\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"html form autocomplete\", \"dialog element\", \"popover attribute\"]},\n     \"WEB_CASCADE\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"css cascade layers\", \"css specificity conflict\"]},\n     \"WEB_LAYOUT\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"container query layout\", \"css stacking context\"]},\n-    \"WEB_A11Y\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"web accessibility pattern\", \"focus visible styling\", \"keyboard focus\", \"broken tab order\", \"accessible name\", \"aria live region\"]},\n+    \"WEB_A11Y\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"web accessibility pattern\", \"focus visible styling\", \"keyboard focus\", \"broken tab order\", \"accessible name\", \"aria live region\", \"focus ring accessibility\", \"focus outline removed\", \"screen reader support\", \"aria label missing\", \"alt text missing\", \"wcag audit\"]},\n     \"WEB_PERF\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"web font loading\", \"largest contentful paint\"]},\n     \"WEB_I18N\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"right to left layout\", \"bidirectional text\"]},\n+    \"WEB_VISUAL_VALUES\": {\"weight\": 4, \"keywords\": [\"what padding should this have\", \"how much padding\", \"what font size should this be\", \"spacing between elements\", \"spacing scale\", \"type scale\", \"build a color palette\", \"shade ramp\", \"box shadow elevat