e/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:45:| 3 | frontend-surface-visual-values | WEB_VISUAL_VALUES | [visual-values.md](frontend-surface/visual-values.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:150:| 1 | Frontend Surface | `frontend-surface-web`, `frontend-surface-figma-check`, `frontend-surface-visual-values` | All three read one router and one replay command, with no fixture to schedule. Run them serially in one session. |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:166:| `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs` (check `4`) | Replays every packet-level routing scenario against its `expected_resources` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check, frontend-surface-visual-values |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:167:| `.skilled/bin/tests/compiled-route-surface-hint.test.cjs` | Asserts a frontend review prompt bundles `[sk-code-review, sk-code-frontend]` and that near-miss prompts never bundle the surface | frontend-surface-web (the same web surface family, with a different prompt) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:168:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs` | The `12a-router-contract` and `12b-routing-shape` checks on this packet's `ROUTER.md` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check, frontend-surface-visual-values (the machine router all three read) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:176:| frontend-surface-web | Web markup and CSS routing | Frontend Surface | [frontend-web](frontend-surface/frontend-web.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:177:| frontend-surface-figma-check | Figma frame check routing | Frontend Surface | [figma-check](frontend-surface/figma-check.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:178:| frontend-surface-visual-values | Visual values routing | Frontend Surface | [visual-values](frontend-surface/visual-values.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:32:| Visual values | [web-visual-values.md](references/web-visual-values.md) | Choosing a spacing, type, weight, colour, shadow, radius or opacity value, or building a palette or token set |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:47:- **`WEB_VISUAL_VALUES`** fires on `what padding should this have`, `how much padding`, `what font size should this be`, `spacing between elements`, `spacing scale`, `type scale`, `build a color palette`, `shade ramp`, `box shadow elevation`, `border radius consistency`, `contrast ratio failure`, `grey text on colored background`, `dark mode palette`, `concentric border radius`, `layered shadows`, `shadow color on dark surface`, `tabular numbers`, `what should this button look like`, `colour decision`, `color decision`, `padding`, `type scale for`, `font size`, `colour palette`, `color palette`, `contrast ratio`, `corner radius`, `box shadow`, or `spacing between`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md` and `references/web-visual-values.md`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:48:- **`WEB_VISUAL_HIERARCHY`** fires on `ui looks off`, `looks amateur`, `feels cluttered`, `make this look better`, `make this ui look designed`, `visual hierarchy`, `no visual hierarchy`, `nothing draws the eye`, `everything competes for attention`, `everything looks the same`, `emphasize by de-emphasizing`, `how to style a destructive button`, `this page feels overwhelming`, `where do i start designing`, `design a new screen from scratch`, `how much white space`, `why does this look wrong`, `does this look right`, `critique this design`, `design critique`, `visual audit`, `design review findings`, `review this screen`, `ux laws`, `cognitive load`, `progressive disclosure`, `empty state design`, `look wrong`, `looks wrong`, `looks off`, or `visual review`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-visual-hierarchy.md`, and `references/web-visual-values.md`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:110:        \"references/web-visual-values.md\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:115:        \"references/web-visual-values.md\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md:30:- Three visual topic files decide what a surface looks like and how it behaves: [`references/web-visual-values.md`](references/web-visual-values.md) holds the value scales, colour ramps, elevation, tokens and hard rules, [`references/web-visual-hierarchy.md`](references/web-visual-hierarchy.md) holds the build procedure, symptom-to-fix tables, hierarchy method, UX laws and visual review pass, and [`references/web-motion-and-interaction.md`](references/web-motion-and-interaction.md) holds motion, input, touch, focus, performance and feedback rules.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md:37:Manual testing scenarios for this surface live in [`manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`](manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md), the root index, plus one file per intent family under `manual-testing-playbook/frontend-surface/<scenario>.md`. The category folder and each scenario file use bare descriptive slugs, with no numeric prefix.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md:51:| Three visual topic files | [Visual values](references/web-visual-values.md), [visual hierarchy and review](references/web-visual-hierarchy.md) and [motion and interaction](references/web-motion-and-interaction.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md:54:| `manual-testing-playbook/` | The routing scenarios the hub's router-sync guard replays: one web, one Figma check and one visual-values scenario |\n=== diff playbook ===\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\nindex c40685582e..8a66ad063c 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\n@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ The hub's router-sync guard replays every scenario here that declares `expected_\n \n | # | Category | Folder | Scenario IDs |\n |---|---|---|---|\n-| 1 | Frontend Surface | `frontend-surface/` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check |\n+| 1 | Frontend Surface | `frontend-surface/` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check, frontend-surface-visual-values |\n \n ### Scenarios\n \n@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ The hub's router-sync guard replays every scenario here that declares `expected_\n | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n | 1 | frontend-surface-web | FRONTEND_WEB | [frontend-web.md](frontend-surface/frontend-web.md) |\n | 2 | frontend-surface-figma-check | FIGMA_TO_CODE | [figma-check.md](frontend-surface/figma-check.md) |\n+| 3 | frontend-surface-visual-values | WEB_VISUAL_VALUES | [visual-values.md](frontend-surface/visual-values.md) |\n \n A **routing** scenario, meaning one that declares `expected_intent` and `expected_resources`, is `PASS` when every path in its `expected_resources` resolves under the packet root, the replayed router selects that intent, and the router emits that path set for the exact prompt. It is `FAIL` when its checks do not hold, and `SKIP` only when a specific sandbox or runtime blocker prevented the run.\n \n@@ -146,7 +147,7 @@ Global verdict logic lives here. The prompt, the expected signals, the commands\n \n | Wave | Category | Scenarios | Rationale |\n |---|---|---|---|\n-| 1 | Frontend Surface | `frontend-surface-web`, `frontend-surface-figma-check` | Both read one router and one replay command, with no fixture to schedule. Run them serially in one session. |\n+| 1 | Frontend Surface | `frontend-surface-web`, `frontend-surface-figma-check`, `frontend-surface-visual-values` | All three read one router and one replay command, with no fixture to schedule. Run them serially in one session. |\n \n ### What Belongs In Per-Feature Files\n \n@@ -162,9 +163,9 @@ Global verdict logic lives here. The prompt, the expected signals, the commands\n \n | Test Module | Coverage | Playbook Overlap |\n |---|---|---|\n-| `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs` (check `4`) | Replays every packet-level routing scenario against its `expected_resources` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check |\n+| `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs` (check `4`) | Replays every packet-level routing scenario against its `expected_resources` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check, frontend-surface-visual-values |\n | `.skilled/bin/tests/compiled-route-surface-hint.test.cjs` | Asserts a frontend review prompt bundles `[sk-code-review, sk-code-frontend]` and that near-miss prompts never bundle the surface | frontend-surface-web (the same web surface family, with a different prompt) |\n-| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs` | The `12a-router-contract` and `12b-routing-shape` checks on this packet's `ROUTER.md` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check (the machine router both read) |\n+| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs` | The `12a-router-contract` and `12b-routing-shape` checks on this packet's `ROUTER.md` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check, frontend-surface-visual-values (the machine router all three read) |\n \n ---\n \n@@ -174,5 +175,6 @@ Global verdict logic lives here. The prompt, the expected signals, the commands\n |---|---|---|---|\n | frontend-surface-web | Web markup and CSS routing | Frontend Surface | [frontend-web](frontend-surface/frontend-web.md) |\n | frontend-surface-figma-check | Figma frame check routing | Frontend Surface | [figma-check](frontend-surface/figma-check.md) |\n+| frontend-surface-visual-values | Visual values routing | Frontend Surface | [visual-values](frontend-surface/visual-values.md) |\n \n The routing rows above belong to the entry `feature-catalog/two-axis-registry-driven-routing/two-axis-registry-driven-routing.md`, which records the surface axis and the advisor-invisible surfaces. The reference families behind the scenarios, which are the core, the web layer and the Figma check, have no separate catalog entry, and each scenario's Playbook Sources section says so.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/:\nfrontend-surface\nmanual-testing-playbook.md\n\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/frontend-surface/:\nfigma-check.md\nfrontend-web.md\nvisual-values.md\n=== index refs ===\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:37:| 1 | Frontend Surface | `frontend-surface/` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check, frontend-surface-visual-values |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:43:| 1 | frontend-surface-web | FRONTEND_WEB | [frontend-web.md](frontend-surface/frontend-web.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:44:| 2 | frontend-surface-figma-check | FIGMA_TO_CODE | [figma-check.md](frontend-surface/figma-check.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:45:| 3 | frontend-surface-visual-values | WEB_VISUAL_VALUES | [visual-values.md](frontend-surface/visual-values.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:150:| 1 | Frontend Surface | `frontend-surface-web`, `frontend-surface-figma-check`, `frontend-surface-visual-values` | All three read one router and one replay command, with no fixture to schedule. Run them serially in one session. |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:166:| `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs` (check `4`) | Replays every packet-level routing scenario against its `expected_resources` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check, frontend-surface-visual-values |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:167:| `.skilled/bin/tests/compiled-route-surface-hint.test.cjs` | Asserts a frontend review prompt bundles `[sk-code-review, sk-code-frontend]` and that near-miss prompts never bundle the surface | frontend-surface-web (the same web surface family, with a different prompt) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:168:| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs` | The `12a-router-contract` and `12b-routing-shape` checks on this packet's `ROUTER.md` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check, frontend-surface-visual-values (the machine router all three read) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:176:| frontend-surface-web | Web markup and CSS routing | Frontend Surface | [frontend-web](frontend-surface/frontend-web.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:177:| frontend-surface-figma-check | Figma frame check routing | Frontend Surface | [figma-check](frontend-surface/figma-check.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md:178:| frontend-surface-visual-values | Visual values routing | Frontend Surface | [visual-values](frontend-surface/visual-values.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:32:| Visual values | [web-visual-values.md](references/web-visual-values.md) | Choosing a spacing, type, weight, colour, shadow, radius or opacity value, or building a palette or token set |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:47:- **`WEB_VISUAL_VALUES`** fires on `what padding should this have`, `how much padding`, `what font size should this be`, `spacing between elements`, `spacing scale`, `type scale`, `build a color palette`, `shade ramp`, `box shadow elevation`, `border radius consistency`, `contrast ratio failure`, `grey text on colored background`, `dark mode palette`, `concentric border radius`, `layered shadows`, `shadow color on dark surface`, `tabular numbers`, `what should this button look like`, `colour decision`, `color decision`, `padding`, `type scale for`, `font size`, `colour palette`, `color palette`, `contrast ratio`, `corner radius`, `box shadow`, or `spacing between`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md` and `references/web-visual-values.md`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:48:- **`WEB_VISUAL_HIERARCHY`** fires on `ui looks off`, `looks amateur`, `feels cluttered`, `make this look better`, `make this ui look designed`, `visual hierarchy`, `no visual hierarchy`, `nothing draws the eye`, `everything competes for attention`, `everything looks the same`, `emphasize by de-emphasizing`, `how to style a destructive button`, `this page feels overwhelming`, `where do i start designing`, `design a new screen from scratch`, `how much white space`, `why does this look wrong`, `does this look right`, `critique this design`, `design critique`, `visual audit`, `design review findings`, `review this screen`, `ux laws`, `cognitive load`, `progressive disclosure`, `empty state design`, `look wrong`, `looks wrong`, `looks off`, or `visual review`. It loads `references/frontend-practice.md`, `references/web-visual-hierarchy.md`, and `references/web-visual-values.md`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:110:        \"references/web-visual-values.md\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md:115:        \"references/web-visual-values.md\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md:30:- Three visual topic files decide what a surface looks like and how it behaves: [`references/web-visual-values.md`](references/web-visual-values.md) holds the value scales, colour ramps, elevation, tokens and hard rules, [`references/web-visual-hierarchy.md`](references/web-visual-hierarchy.md) holds the build procedure, symptom-to-fix tables, hierarchy method, UX laws and visual review pass, and [`references/web-motion-and-interaction.md`](references/web-motion-and-interaction.md) holds motion, input, touch, focus, performance and feedback rules.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md:37:Manual testing scenarios for this surface live in [`manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md`](manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md), the root index, plus one file per intent family under `manual-testing-playbook/frontend-surface/<scenario>.md`. The category folder and each scenario file use bare descriptive slugs, with no numeric prefix.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md:51:| Three visual topic files | [Visual values](references/web-visual-values.md), [visual hierarchy and review](references/web-visual-hierarchy.md) and [motion and interaction](references/web-motion-and-interaction.md) |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md:54:| `manual-testing-playbook/` | The routing scenarios the hub's router-sync guard replays: one web, one Figma check and one visual-values scenario |\n=== diff playbook ===\ndiff --git a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\nindex c40685582e..8a66ad063c 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md\n@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ The hub's router-sync guard replays every scenario here that declares `expected_\n \n | # | Category | Folder | Scenario IDs |\n |---|---|---|---|\n-| 1 | Frontend Surface | `frontend-surface/` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check |\n+| 1 | Frontend Surface | `frontend-surface/` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check, frontend-surface-visual-values |\n \n ### Scenarios\n \n@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@ The hub's router-sync guard replays every scenario here that declares `expected_\n | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n | 1 | frontend-surface-web | FRONTEND_WEB | [frontend-web.md](frontend-surface/frontend-web.md) |\n | 2 | frontend-surface-figma-check | FIGMA_TO_CODE | [figma-check.md](frontend-surface/figma-check.md) |\n+| 3 | frontend-surface-visual-values | WEB_VISUAL_VALUES | [visual-values.md](frontend-surface/visual-values.md) |\n \n A **routing** scenario, meaning one that declares `expected_intent` and `expected_resources`, is `PASS` when every path in its `expected_resources` resolves under the packet root, the replayed router selects that intent, and the router emits that path set for the exact prompt. It is `FAIL` when its checks do not hold, and `SKIP` only when a specific sandbox or runtime blocker prevented the run.\n \n@@ -146,7 +147,7 @@ Global verdict logic lives here. The prompt, the expected signals, the commands\n \n | Wave | Category | Scenarios | Rationale |\n |---|---|---|---|\n-| 1 | Frontend Surface | `frontend-surface-web`, `frontend-surface-figma-check` | Both read one router and one replay command, with no fixture to schedule. Run them serially in one session. |\n+| 1 | Frontend Surface | `frontend-surface-web`, `frontend-surface-figma-check`, `frontend-surface-visual-values` | All three read one router and one replay command, with no fixture to schedule. Run them serially in one session. |\n \n ### What Belongs In Per-Feature Files\n \n@@ -162,9 +163,9 @@ Global verdict logic lives here. The prompt, the expected signals, the commands\n \n | Test Module | Coverage | Playbook Overlap |\n |---|---|---|\n-| `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs` (check `4`) | Replays every packet-level routing scenario against its `expected_resources` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check |\n+| `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs` (check `4`) | Replays every packet-level routing scenario against its `expected_resources` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check, frontend-surface-visual-values |\n | `.skilled/bin/tests/compiled-route-surface-hint.test.cjs` | Asserts a frontend review prompt bundles `[sk-code-review, sk-code-frontend]` and that near-miss prompts never bundle the surface | frontend-surface-web (the same web surface family, with a different prompt) |\n-| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs` | The `12a-router-contract` and `12b-routing-shape` checks on this packet's `ROUTER.md` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check (the machine router both read) |\n+| `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs` | The `12a-router-contract` and `12b-routing-shape` checks on this packet's `ROUTER.md` | frontend-surface-web, frontend-surface-figma-check, frontend-surface-visual-values (the machine router all three read) |\n \n ---\n \n@@ -174,5 +175,6 @@ Global verdict logic lives here. The prompt, the expected signals, the commands\n |---|---|---|---|\n | frontend-surface-web | Web markup and CSS routing | Frontend Surface | [frontend-web](frontend-surface/frontend-web.md) |\n | frontend-surface-figma-check | Figma frame check routing | Frontend Surface | [figma-check](frontend-surface/figma-check.md) |\n+| frontend-surface-visual-values | Visual values routing | Frontend Surface | [visual-values](frontend-surface/visual-values.md) |\n \n The routing rows above belong to the entry `feature-catalog/two-axis-registry-driven-routing/two-axis-registry-driven-routing.md`, which records the surface axis and the advisor-invisible surfaces. The reference families behind the scenarios, which are the core, the web layer and the Figma check, have no separate catalog entry, and each scenario's Playbook Sources section says so.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && ls .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/ .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/frontend-surface/; echo \\\"=== index refs ===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"visual-values\\\\|frontend-surface\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/README.md | head -20; echo \\\"=== diff playbook ===\\\"; git diff 10474a9567 -- .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md | head -60\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873066573,"end":1793873067645}}}}
