{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793873113696,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"id":"prt_1ab2b7260001IrdJet3hA0xH0U","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2b6c8d001GUVXW3TRODhsbP","type":"step-start","snapshot":"95e5f715ae3eace8ec8e1d53214acaf40a3cc127"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873115479,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2b782e0018sK1i6AAlRgUqg","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2b6c8d001GUVXW3TRODhsbP","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0126b4377f9027c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && head -25 .skilled/skills/sk-design/changelog/v3.0.0.0.md; echo \"=== frontend ===\"; head -20 .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md; echo \"=== chart ===\"; head -15 .skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.23.7.0.md"},"output":"---\ntitle: \"sk-design v3.0.0.0, three modes and no values mode\"\ndescription: \"v3.0.0.0 retires the sk-design-fundamentals mode. Value scales, hierarchy, motion and visual review now live in sk-code-frontend. The hub routes to the generator, chart and diagram modes, and a request with no signal defers.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-design v3.0.0.0\"\n  - \"sk-design 3.0.0.0\"\n  - \"fundamentals mode retired\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\nversion: 3.0.0.0\n---\n\n# v3.0.0.0, Three Modes and No Values Mode\n\nThe hub drops its values mode. Deciding a spacing, type, colour or motion value and reviewing a screen now belong to `sk-code`, whose frontend surface carries the same scales and review pass. The hub keeps the three modes that build a design artifact.\n\n> Spec folder: `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals` (Level 2)\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## Why This Release\n\nTwo skills answered the same question. `sk-code-frontend` already sent every open value to `sk-design-fundamentals`, so a frontend request crossed two hubs to pick a padding. The value guidance now sits where the code that uses it is written.\n\n&nbsp;\n=== frontend ===\n---\ntitle: \"sk-code-frontend v1.1.0.0, the surface decides visual values\"\ndescription: \"v1.1.0.0 adds three visual references and a starter token file, so the surface decides spacing, type, colour, elevation, hierarchy and motion values instead of sending them to another skill.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-code-frontend v1.1.0.0\"\n  - \"sk-code-frontend 1.1.0.0\"\n  - \"visual value references\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n\n# v1.1.0.0, The Surface Decides Visual Values\n\nThe frontend surface now carries the value scales and visual review it used to borrow. An open value is decided here, from a scale, rather than handed to the design hub.\n\n> Spec folder: `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals` (Level 2)\n\n&nbsp;\n\n=== chart ===\n---\ntitle: \"sk-design-chart v0.23.7.0, the references describe only the chart work\"\ndescription: \"v0.23.7.0 removes research citations and phase history from the chart references. Each rule they backed stays, stated on its own.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-design-chart v0.23.7.0\"\n  - \"sk-design-chart 0.23.7.0\"\n  - \"research citations removed\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\nversion: 0.23.7.0\n---\n\n# v0.23.7.0, The References Describe Only the Chart Work\n\nThe catalog, colour system, template contract and the evilcharts origin note no longer cite research files or name the phase that made a decision. The decisions stay.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"sk-design v3.0.0.0, three modes and no values mode\"\ndescription: \"v3.0.0.0 retires the sk-design-fundamentals mode. Value scales, hierarchy, motion and visual review now live in sk-code-frontend. The hub routes to the generator, chart and diagram modes, and a request with no signal defers.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-design v3.0.0.0\"\n  - \"sk-design 3.0.0.0\"\n  - \"fundamentals mode retired\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\nversion: 3.0.0.0\n---\n\n# v3.0.0.0, Three Modes and No Values Mode\n\nThe hub drops its values mode. Deciding a spacing, type, colour or motion value and reviewing a screen now belong to `sk-code`, whose frontend surface carries the same scales and review pass. The hub keeps the three modes that build a design artifact.\n\n> Spec folder: `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals` (Level 2)\n\n&nbsp;\n\n## Why This Release\n\nTwo skills answered the same question. `sk-code-frontend` already sent every open value to `sk-design-fundamentals`, so a frontend request crossed two hubs to pick a padding. The value guidance now sits where the code that uses it is written.\n\n&nbsp;\n=== frontend ===\n---\ntitle: \"sk-code-frontend v1.1.0.0, the surface decides visual values\"\ndescription: \"v1.1.0.0 adds three visual references and a starter token file, so the surface decides spacing, type, colour, elevation, hierarchy and motion values instead of sending them to another skill.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-code-frontend v1.1.0.0\"\n  - \"sk-code-frontend 1.1.0.0\"\n  - \"visual value references\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\nversion: 1.1.0.0\n---\n\n# v1.1.0.0, The Surface Decides Visual Values\n\nThe frontend surface now carries the value scales and visual review it used to borrow. An open value is decided here, from a scale, rather than handed to the design hub.\n\n> Spec folder: `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals` (Level 2)\n\n&nbsp;\n\n=== chart ===\n---\ntitle: \"sk-design-chart v0.23.7.0, the references describe only the chart work\"\ndescription: \"v0.23.7.0 removes research citations and phase history from the chart references. Each rule they backed stays, stated on its own.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-design-chart v0.23.7.0\"\n  - \"sk-design-chart 0.23.7.0\"\n  - \"research citations removed\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\nversion: 0.23.7.0\n---\n\n# v0.23.7.0, The References Describe Only the Chart Work\n\nThe catalog, colour system, template contract and the evilcharts origin note no longer cite research files or name the phase that made a decision. The decisions stay.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && head -25 .skilled/skills/sk-design/changelog/v3.0.0.0.md; echo \\\"=== frontend ===\\\"; head -20 .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/changelog/v1.1.0.0.md; echo \\\"=== chart ===\\\"; head -15 .skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.23.7.0.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873115183,"end":1793873115479}}}}
