{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873125257,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2b9e1e001gypJbfsyphrt4R","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2b8fb2001trXwO846rWJfxT","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f604118b188ff66","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -n \"120\\|180\\|260\\|500ms\\|duration\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md | head -25"},"output":"5:  - \"ui animation duration\"\n38:- **Value scales.** Spacing, type, colour and elevation scales remain in [web-visual-values.md](web-visual-values.md). The duration scale is [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n261:The values that drive these items, including the duration bands and the easing choices, are in Section 10.\n265:- **Rule:** Suppress transitions and animations for the duration of a theme swap.\n323:- **Rule:** Use `transform: translateZ(0)` sparingly as a fix for a measured problem, and toggle `will-change` on for the duration of an unperformant scroll animation and off afterwards.\n491:- **See also:** [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n546:- **Rule:** Choose a duration from the band that matches the interaction, and never let a user-initiated animation exceed 300ms.\n547:- **Why:** A fixed set of bands makes the interface feel consistent and stops each component from inventing its own sense of speed. When something feels slow, shorten the duration before touching the curve, because the curve shapes the ends while the duration sets the wait.\n549:- **Pitfall:** A unique duration per component makes the interface feel inconsistent even when each value looks smooth alone.\n551:- **See also:** [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n555:| Press and hover | 120 to 180ms |\n556:| Small state change such as a toggle, dropdown or tooltip | 180 to 260ms |\n557:| Layout transition such as a modal, drawer or accordion | up to 500ms |\n569:- **See also:** [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n590:- **See also:** [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n610:### M57. Reconciling the duration guidance\n615:- **Pitfall:** Taking the 200ms figure as a global ceiling makes a drawer feel rushed, and taking 500ms as a global ceiling makes a press feel dead.\n617:- **See also:** [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n622:| This ruleset | 300ms ceiling, 120 to 180ms press and hover, 180 to 260ms small state |\n623:| Layered bands | 100 to 150ms feedback, 200 to 300ms state change, 300 to 500ms layout transition |\n625:The 200ms figure is about direct feedback, meaning the response to a press or hover, where any perceptible lag reads as unresponsiveness. The 300ms ceiling is about user-initiated state changes, which are allowed slightly more room because something visibly changed. The 300 to 500ms band covers layout transitions such as a drawer or modal, which do not block a further input.\n631:- **Direct feedback** for press, hover or tap: 120 to 180ms. Never above 200ms.\n632:- **State change** for a toggle, dropdown, tooltip or tab: 180 to 260ms. Never above 300ms.\n633:- **Layout transition** for a modal, drawer or accordion: up to 500ms, and only when it is not blocking the next input.\n640:- [web-visual-values.md](web-visual-values.md) holds the spacing, type, colour and elevation scales, and [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands) holds the duration bands this file enforces.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"5:  - \"ui animation duration\"\n38:- **Value scales.** Spacing, type, colour and elevation scales remain in [web-visual-values.md](web-visual-values.md). The duration scale is [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n261:The values that drive these items, including the duration bands and the easing choices, are in Section 10.\n265:- **Rule:** Suppress transitions and animations for the duration of a theme swap.\n323:- **Rule:** Use `transform: translateZ(0)` sparingly as a fix for a measured problem, and toggle `will-change` on for the duration of an unperformant scroll animation and off afterwards.\n491:- **See also:** [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n546:- **Rule:** Choose a duration from the band that matches the interaction, and never let a user-initiated animation exceed 300ms.\n547:- **Why:** A fixed set of bands makes the interface feel consistent and stops each component from inventing its own sense of speed. When something feels slow, shorten the duration before touching the curve, because the curve shapes the ends while the duration sets the wait.\n549:- **Pitfall:** A unique duration per component makes the interface feel inconsistent even when each value looks smooth alone.\n551:- **See also:** [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n555:| Press and hover | 120 to 180ms |\n556:| Small state change such as a toggle, dropdown or tooltip | 180 to 260ms |\n557:| Layout transition such as a modal, drawer or accordion | up to 500ms |\n569:- **See also:** [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n590:- **See also:** [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n610:### M57. Reconciling the duration guidance\n615:- **Pitfall:** Taking the 200ms figure as a global ceiling makes a drawer feel rushed, and taking 500ms as a global ceiling makes a press feel dead.\n617:- **See also:** [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands).\n622:| This ruleset | 300ms ceiling, 120 to 180ms press and hover, 180 to 260ms small state |\n623:| Layered bands | 100 to 150ms feedback, 200 to 300ms state change, 300 to 500ms layout transition |\n625:The 200ms figure is about direct feedback, meaning the response to a press or hover, where any perceptible lag reads as unresponsiveness. The 300ms ceiling is about user-initiated state changes, which are allowed slightly more room because something visibly changed. The 300 to 500ms band covers layout transitions such as a drawer or modal, which do not block a further input.\n631:- **Direct feedback** for press, hover or tap: 120 to 180ms. Never above 200ms.\n632:- **State change** for a toggle, dropdown, tooltip or tab: 180 to 260ms. Never above 300ms.\n633:- **Layout transition** for a modal, drawer or accordion: up to 500ms, and only when it is not blocking the next input.\n640:- [web-visual-values.md](web-visual-values.md) holds the spacing, type, colour and elevation scales, and [V4](web-visual-values.md#v4-motion-duration-bands) holds the duration bands this file enforces.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -n \\\"120\\\\|180\\\\|260\\\\|500ms\\\\|duration\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md | head -25\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873124894,"end":1793873125257}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873125297,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2b9cb70020AkNGXwOX22NeW","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2b8fb2001trXwO846rWJfxT","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e7a9b2e31ef65f9","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re, pathlib\nroot=pathlib.Path('.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend')\nfiles=[root/'references/web-visual-values.md',root/'references/web-visual-hierarchy.md',root/'references/web-motion-and-interaction.md',root/'manual-testing-playbook/frontend-surface/visual-values.md']\nfor f in files:\n    text=f.read_text()\n    links=re.findall(r'\\]\\(([^)#]+)(?:#[^)]*)?\\)',text)\n    missing=[]\n    for l in links:\n        if l.startswith(('http','mailto:')): continue\n        p=(f.parent/l).resolve()\n        if not p.exists(): missing.append(l)\n    print(f.name, 'links', len(links), 'missing', sorted(set(missing)))\nEOF"},"output":"web-visual-values.md links 57 missing []\nweb-visual-hierarchy.md links 60 missing []\nweb-motion-and-interaction.md links 65 missing []\nvisual-values.md links 8 missing []\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"web-visual-values.md links 57 missing []\nweb-visual-hierarchy.md links 60 missing []\nweb-motion-and-interaction.md links 65 missing []\nvisual-values.md links 8 missing []\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport re, pathlib\\nroot=pathlib.Path('.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend')\\nfiles=[root/'references/web-visual-values.md',root/'references/web-visual-hierarchy.md',root/'references/web-motion-and-interaction.md',root/'manual-testing-playbook/frontend-surface/visual-values.md']\\nfor f in files:\\n    text=f.read_text()\\n    links=re.findall(r'\\\\]\\\\(([^)#]+)(?:#[^)]*)?\\\\)',text)\\n    missing=[]\\n    for l in links:\\n        if l.startswith(('http','mailto:')): continue\\n        p=(f.parent/l).resolve()\\n        if not p.exists(): missing.append(l)\\n    print(f.name, 'links', len(links), 'missing', sorted(set(missing)))\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873124535,"end":1793873125297}}}}
