{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873151129,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2c00430011WkkXZ9AGsg5Oz","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2bf95e001hUIpNbcUvDSNzt","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-82336929fadf073e","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -n \"role layer\\|retune\\|token file\\|tokens.css\\|copy it in\\|Copy\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md | head -30; echo \"=== section 9/10 headings ===\"; grep -n \"^## \\|^### V3[5-9]\\|^### V4\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md | tail -25"},"output":"32:- Choosing which grey carries which text role, or retuning a token file for a project.\n56:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the scale as custom properties.\n64:- **Why:** Same logic as the other scales: decide once, reuse everywhere. The token file maps them to `--opacity-1` through `--opacity-6` from `.05` to `.8`.\n68:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n109:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--text-xs` through `--text-7xl`.\n118:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--weight-normal` and `--weight-bold`.\n127:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--leading-tight` through `--leading-loose` and `--measure: 34em`.\n154:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the weight and text-size tokens.\n176:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the grey, primary and accent ramps.\n185:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) writes every ramp in HSL.\n194:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) shows a completed nine-shade primary ramp.\n203:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) raises saturation toward both ends.\n216:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) rotates hue across each ramp.\n225:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) ships cool greys and names the warm hue to swap in.\n234:- **See also:** [web-accessibility-patterns.md](web-accessibility-patterns.md) and [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n243:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the dark-mode role overrides.\n264:- **See also:** [web-visual-hierarchy.md](web-visual-hierarchy.md) and [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n300:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the base elevation values these treatments extend.\n322:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) holds the single-shadow default this scale replaces.\n338:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) holds the five-elevation set.\n347:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the black-alpha default.\n400:- **Pitfall:** A 4px inner radius inside a 4px outer radius with 8px padding produces two curves that visibly disagree. The token file ships a 4px neutral default, `0` for formal and `12px+` for playful.\n402:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--radius` and `--radius-full`.\n468:- **Rule:** Components reference semantic roles, never raw ramps. The role layer is what makes a dark-mode block work, because the dark override redefines only the roles. A component that points at `--text-secondary` follows automatically, while a component pointing at `--grey-700` does not:\n476:- **Why:** Copy the token file in and retune the hues. The file groups its custom properties by scale, from `--space-1` through `--space-16` and `--text-xs` through `--text-7xl` to the semantic roles. It is not a theme, a component library or a brand. It is the decisions, made once, with the hues chosen to be replaced. Re-deriving the scales from prose wastes the work already done and reintroduces the ad hoc values the system exists to eliminate.\n480:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the role layer and the dark-mode block.\n489:- **See also:** [web-accessibility-patterns.md](web-accessibility-patterns.md) and [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n498:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the measured ratios in comments.\n500:### V38. Retuning the token file for a project\n507:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) and [web-accessibility-patterns.md](web-accessibility-patterns.md).\n=== section 9/10 headings ===\n21:## 1. OVERVIEW\n43:## 2. SPACING, SIZING, OPACITY AND TIMING\n79:### V4. Motion duration bands\n96:## 3. TYPE SCALE AND TYPE DETAIL\n167:## 4. COLOUR RAMPS\n247:## 5. ELEVATION AND SHADOWS\n384:## 6. RADIUS, BORDERS AND COMPONENT SHAPE\n433:## 7. IMAGES AND MEDIA\n464:## 8. DESIGN TOKENS AND ROLES\n466:### V35. Reference roles, not raw ramps\n482:### V36. Decorative and functional borders\n491:### V37. Which grey carries which text\n500:### V38. Retuning the token file for a project\n511:## 9. HARD RULES\n513:### V39. ALWAYS\n529:### V40. NEVER\n545:### V41. ESCALATE IF\n561:## 10. REFERENCES AND RELATED RESOURCES\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"32:- Choosing which grey carries which text role, or retuning a token file for a project.\n56:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the scale as custom properties.\n64:- **Why:** Same logic as the other scales: decide once, reuse everywhere. The token file maps them to `--opacity-1` through `--opacity-6` from `.05` to `.8`.\n68:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n109:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--text-xs` through `--text-7xl`.\n118:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--weight-normal` and `--weight-bold`.\n127:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--leading-tight` through `--leading-loose` and `--measure: 34em`.\n154:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the weight and text-size tokens.\n176:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the grey, primary and accent ramps.\n185:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) writes every ramp in HSL.\n194:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) shows a completed nine-shade primary ramp.\n203:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) raises saturation toward both ends.\n216:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) rotates hue across each ramp.\n225:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) ships cool greys and names the warm hue to swap in.\n234:- **See also:** [web-accessibility-patterns.md](web-accessibility-patterns.md) and [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n243:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the dark-mode role overrides.\n264:- **See also:** [web-visual-hierarchy.md](web-visual-hierarchy.md) and [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n300:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the base elevation values these treatments extend.\n322:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) holds the single-shadow default this scale replaces.\n338:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) holds the five-elevation set.\n347:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the black-alpha default.\n400:- **Pitfall:** A 4px inner radius inside a 4px outer radius with 8px padding produces two curves that visibly disagree. The token file ships a 4px neutral default, `0` for formal and `12px+` for playful.\n402:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--radius` and `--radius-full`.\n468:- **Rule:** Components reference semantic roles, never raw ramps. The role layer is what makes a dark-mode block work, because the dark override redefines only the roles. A component that points at `--text-secondary` follows automatically, while a component pointing at `--grey-700` does not:\n476:- **Why:** Copy the token file in and retune the hues. The file groups its custom properties by scale, from `--space-1` through `--space-16` and `--text-xs` through `--text-7xl` to the semantic roles. It is not a theme, a component library or a brand. It is the decisions, made once, with the hues chosen to be replaced. Re-deriving the scales from prose wastes the work already done and reintroduces the ad hoc values the system exists to eliminate.\n480:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the role layer and the dark-mode block.\n489:- **See also:** [web-accessibility-patterns.md](web-accessibility-patterns.md) and [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n498:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the measured ratios in comments.\n500:### V38. Retuning the token file for a project\n507:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) and [web-accessibility-patterns.md](web-accessibility-patterns.md).\n=== section 9/10 headings ===\n21:## 1. OVERVIEW\n43:## 2. SPACING, SIZING, OPACITY AND TIMING\n79:### V4. Motion duration bands\n96:## 3. TYPE SCALE AND TYPE DETAIL\n167:## 4. COLOUR RAMPS\n247:## 5. ELEVATION AND SHADOWS\n384:## 6. RADIUS, BORDERS AND COMPONENT SHAPE\n433:## 7. IMAGES AND MEDIA\n464:## 8. DESIGN TOKENS AND ROLES\n466:### V35. Reference roles, not raw ramps\n482:### V36. Decorative and functional borders\n491:### V37. Which grey carries which text\n500:### V38. Retuning the token file for a project\n511:## 9. HARD RULES\n513:### V39. ALWAYS\n529:### V40. NEVER\n545:### V41. ESCALATE IF\n561:## 10. REFERENCES AND RELATED RESOURCES\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -n \\\"role layer\\\\|retune\\\\|token file\\\\|tokens.css\\\\|copy it in\\\\|Copy\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md | head -30; echo \\\"=== section 9/10 headings ===\\\"; grep -n 