{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873180956,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2c77dc001KoIl13hrDXo79c","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2c69730015xsC0ifN9S4AkT","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8315549ce393db62","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \"sk-code-frontend\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md | head -12; echo \"=== description keywords ===\"; python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('.skilled/skills/sk-code/description.json'));print(d['description']);print([k for k in d['keywords'] if 'visual' in k or 'padding' in k or 'spacing' in k])\""},"output":".skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:10:<!-- Keywords: sk-code, code, surface-aware, two-axis, opencode, typescript, python, shell, json, jsonc, github-actions, ci-workflow, sk-code-quality, sk-code-review, sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend, quality, code-review, verification, debug, implement, workflow-doctrine, mode-registry, workflowmode, packetkind, backendkind, surface-router, evidence-base, surface-packet -->\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:16:The **surface axis** has three read-only evidence packets the hub bundles alongside a workflow mode: sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend and sk-code-skilled.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:44:| **sk-code-frontend** | Stack-agnostic frontend evidence: web markup and CSS, web layout and accessibility, and Figma-to-code checks. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-frontend/` |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:50:- Frontend (`sk-code-frontend`): the stack-agnostic web practice and Figma-to-code surface, bundled from request vocabulary alone.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:60:- When a request or a frame leaves a visual value open (spacing, type, color, radius, shadow or motion), or a value sits off every token and scale, load `sk-code-frontend` and decide it from its visual-values reference.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:115:  sk-code-frontend/      # stack-agnostic web and Figma-to-code evidence packet (read-only)\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:127:The `evidence-base` backend serves the surface packets as read-only domain evidence (`sk-code-ci/`, `sk-code-frontend/`, `sk-code-skilled/`). The hub bundles them alongside the primary mode.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:170:- Surface evidence packets: `sk-code-ci/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-skilled/SKILL.md`.\n=== description keywords ===\nCoding standards, references, and assets for this framework's own system code. Provides surface-aware code-quality patterns, checklists, and verification recipes for OpenCode system code (JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Shell, JSON/JSONC, MCP server code, agents, commands, skills). Smart-routing internals detect the active stack and load matching standards; unsupported stacks ask for disambiguation. Its surface axis bundles the CI, frontend (web and Figma-to-code) and SKILLED evidence packets.\n[]\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:10:<!-- Keywords: sk-code, code, surface-aware, two-axis, opencode, typescript, python, shell, json, jsonc, github-actions, ci-workflow, sk-code-quality, sk-code-review, sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend, quality, code-review, verification, debug, implement, workflow-doctrine, mode-registry, workflowmode, packetkind, backendkind, surface-router, evidence-base, surface-packet -->\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:16:The **surface axis** has three read-only evidence packets the hub bundles alongside a workflow mode: sk-code-ci, sk-code-frontend and sk-code-skilled.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:44:| **sk-code-frontend** | Stack-agnostic frontend evidence: web markup and CSS, web layout and accessibility, and Figma-to-code checks. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-frontend/` |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:50:- Frontend (`sk-code-frontend`): the stack-agnostic web practice and Figma-to-code surface, bundled from request vocabulary alone.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:60:- When a request or a frame leaves a visual value open (spacing, type, color, radius, shadow or motion), or a value sits off every token and scale, load `sk-code-frontend` and decide it from its visual-values reference.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:115:  sk-code-frontend/      # stack-agnostic web and Figma-to-code evidence packet (read-only)\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:127:The `evidence-base` backend serves the surface packets as read-only domain evidence (`sk-code-ci/`, `sk-code-frontend/`, `sk-code-skilled/`). The hub bundles them alongside the primary mode.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md:170:- Surface evidence packets: `sk-code-ci/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-skilled/SKILL.md`.\n=== description keywords ===\nCoding standards, references, and assets for this framework's own system code. Provides surface-aware code-quality patterns, checklists, and verification recipes for OpenCode system code (JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Shell, JSON/JSONC, MCP server code, agents, commands, skills). Smart-routing internals detect the active stack and load matching standards; unsupported stacks ask for disambiguation. Its surface axis bundles the CI, frontend (web and Figma-to-code) and SKILLED evidence packets.\n[]\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \\\"sk-code-frontend\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md | head -12; echo \\\"=== description keywords ===\\\"; python3 -c \\\"import json;d=json.load(open('.skilled/skills/sk-code/description.json'));print(d['description']);print([k for k in d['keywords'] if 'visual' in k or 'padding' in k or 'spacing' in k])\\\"\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873180636,"end":1793873180956}}}}
