it through the browser rather than restating it.</p>\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/assets/style-reference/evilcharts/palette-sheet-categorical.html:131:  <p class=\"source\" data-chart-part=\"source\">Source: the palette file in this packet. This sheet reads it through the browser rather than restating it.</p>\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/assets/style-reference/evilcharts/origin.md:33:**Source:** the evilcharts component library, `src/app/globals.css`, its `:root` and `.dark`\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/assets/style-reference/evilcharts/palette-sheet-neutral.html:131:  <p class=\"source\" data-chart-part=\"source\">Source: the palette file in this packet. This sheet reads it through the browser rather than restating it.</p>\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \\\"Source:\\\\|SOURCE:\\\\|specs/\\\\|018-sk-design\\\\|013-shadcn\\\\|Phase\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references .skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/assets/style-reference/evilcharts 2>/dev/null | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873184592,"end":1793873185028}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873185031,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2c8859001BntpZanYboT2Jx","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2c7e39001eweEexJ3lKp6PP","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcb8072154aab84b","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \"research\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart --include=\"*.md\" | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.2.0.0.md:18:Ten recommendations from fidelity research were reviewed against the contract. Seven were applied and three were refused in writing because an item nobody decided is an item that comes back.\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.3.0.0.md:149:The phase was built around the research finding that `grouped-bars` sits on the wrong system, but the reading does not support it. All twenty catalog rows were read against the color definitions one by one, and no row moved. The two series of `grouped-bars` are ordered in time, `categorical` is defined for categories that are unordered and `neutral` is the documented default that wins a tie. The reading found instead that `progress-single` was correctly declared and behaving as though it were not. Every verdict is written down, including the seventeen that were never in doubt. The reason a wrong claim survived that long is that nobody had read both documents against each other.\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.23.7.0.md:3:description: \"v0.23.7.0 removes research citations and phase history from the chart references. Each rule they backed stays, stated on its own.\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.23.7.0.md:7:  - \"research citations removed\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.23.7.0.md:15:The catalog, colour system, template contract and the evilcharts origin note no longer cite research files or name the phase that made a decision. The decisions stay.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.2.0.0.md:18:Ten recommendations from fidelity research were reviewed against the contract. Seven were applied and three were refused in writing because an item nobody decided is an item that comes back.\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.3.0.0.md:149:The phase was built around the research finding that `grouped-bars` sits on the wrong system, but the reading does not support it. All twenty catalog rows were read against the color definitions one by one, and no row moved. The two series of `grouped-bars` are ordered in time, `categorical` is defined for categories that are unordered and `neutral` is the documented default that wins a tie. The reading found instead that `progress-single` was correctly declared and behaving as though it were not. Every verdict is written down, including the seventeen that were never in doubt. The reason a wrong claim survived that long is that nobody had read both documents against each other.\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.23.7.0.md:3:description: \"v0.23.7.0 removes research citations and phase history from the chart references. Each rule they backed stays, stated on its own.\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.23.7.0.md:7:  - \"research citations removed\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/changelog/v0.23.7.0.md:15:The catalog, colour system, template contract and the evilcharts origin note no longer cite research files or name the phase that made a decision. The decisions stay.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \\\"research\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart --include=\\\"*.md\\\" | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873184857,"end":1793873185031}}}}
