{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793873190411,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"id":"prt_1ab2c9e0b001mQ35ZPjPS7q6OG","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2c978c001oh3ght0LguD5zq","type":"step-start","snapshot":"25529385e68a1449d361de773993a1f56d02aa07"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873191793,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2ca28c001UawatmKp1V2Xs6","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2c978c001oh3ght0LguD5zq","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-93bc9b9dbb8a266f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && sed -n '380,420p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md"},"output":"\n- **Rule:** Ship an SVG favicon with an inline style tag that follows `prefers-color-scheme`.\n- **Why:** One file then serves both themes and the mark stays legible in a light or dark tab strip.\n- **When not to:** Ship a single static favicon when the mark must not change with the theme.\n- **Pitfall:** A dark favicon disappears in a dark tab strip.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [A10](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a10-contrast-color-scheme-and-transparency-preferences).\n\n### M36. Feedback beside its trigger\n\n- **Rule:** Display feedback relative to its trigger. A copy button shows an inline checkmark, and a form error highlights the offending input.\n- **Why:** Feedback far from its cause makes the user hunt for the connection.\n- **When not to:** Use a page-level status region when the result belongs to the whole page rather than one control.\n- **Pitfall:** A toast in the corner for a field error leaves the field looking valid.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [A17](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a17-error-summary-and-focus-on-submit).\n\n### M37. Empty states\n\n- **Rule:** Prompt the user to create the first item, optionally with templates.\n- **Why:** An empty surface is the one moment when the next action is not obvious, so it is the cheapest place to teach the product.\n- **When not to:** Show a plain message when the user cannot create the item, such as a read-only view.\n- **Pitfall:** An empty state that only says there are no results leaves the user with nothing to do.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [web-visual-hierarchy.md](web-visual-hierarchy.md).\n\n---\n\n## 9. THE TWELVE ANIMATION PRINCIPLES\n\nThe principles say what motion should express. Section 10 says which values express it.\n\n### M38. Squash and stretch\n\n- **Rule:** Fake mass with momentary deformation, kept inside the 0.95 to 1.05 range.\n- **Why:** Digital objects have no physics, so a small deformation is what tells the eye about weight, material and energy.\n- **When not to:** Skip deformation on a large surface where the distortion reads as a layout bug.\n- **Pitfall:** Too much squash and stretch turns professional software into a cartoon, which is why the bound exists.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [Section 10](#10-the-enforceable-motion-ruleset) for the physics item.\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n- **Rule:** Ship an SVG favicon with an inline style tag that follows `prefers-color-scheme`.\n- **Why:** One file then serves both themes and the mark stays legible in a light or dark tab strip.\n- **When not to:** Ship a single static favicon when the mark must not change with the theme.\n- **Pitfall:** A dark favicon disappears in a dark tab strip.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [A10](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a10-contrast-color-scheme-and-transparency-preferences).\n\n### M36. Feedback beside its trigger\n\n- **Rule:** Display feedback relative to its trigger. A copy button shows an inline checkmark, and a form error highlights the offending input.\n- **Why:** Feedback far from its cause makes the user hunt for the connection.\n- **When not to:** Use a page-level status region when the result belongs to the whole page rather than one control.\n- **Pitfall:** A toast in the corner for a field error leaves the field looking valid.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [A17](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a17-error-summary-and-focus-on-submit).\n\n### M37. Empty states\n\n- **Rule:** Prompt the user to create the first item, optionally with templates.\n- **Why:** An empty surface is the one moment when the next action is not obvious, so it is the cheapest place to teach the product.\n- **When not to:** Show a plain message when the user cannot create the item, such as a read-only view.\n- **Pitfall:** An empty state that only says there are no results leaves the user with nothing to do.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [web-visual-hierarchy.md](web-visual-hierarchy.md).\n\n---\n\n## 9. THE TWELVE ANIMATION PRINCIPLES\n\nThe principles say what motion should express. Section 10 says which values express it.\n\n### M38. Squash and stretch\n\n- **Rule:** Fake mass with momentary deformation, kept inside the 0.95 to 1.05 range.\n- **Why:** Digital objects have no physics, so a small deformation is what tells the eye about weight, material and energy.\n- **When not to:** Skip deformation on a large surface where the distortion reads as a layout bug.\n- **Pitfall:** Too much squash and stretch turns professional software into a cartoon, which is why the bound exists.\n- **Support:** Judgment, no version gate.\n- **See also:** [Section 10](#10-the-enforceable-motion-ruleset) for the physics item.\n\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && sed -n '380,420p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873191564,"end":1793873191793}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873191801,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2ca128002rrj0TlcHEayByT","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2c978c001oh3ght0LguD5zq","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad10960dcd29aee2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \"innerHTML\\|eval(\\|csrf\\|XSS\\|auth\\|secret\\|password\\|token\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-hierarchy.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md | head -25"},"output":".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:3:description: Spacing, type, colour, shadow, radius, motion and token values for web interfaces.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:9:  - \"design token roles\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:25:This file covers the value scales and construction methods for spacing, type, colour, elevation, radius, borders, images and token roles.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:30:- Building a colour ramp or a token set from scratch.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:32:- Choosing which grey carries which text role, or retuning a token file for a project.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:56:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the scale as custom properties.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:64:- **Why:** Same logic as the other scales: decide once, reuse everywhere. The token file maps them to `--opacity-1` through `--opacity-6` from `.05` to `.8`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:68:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:109:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--text-xs` through `--text-7xl`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:118:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--weight-normal` and `--weight-bold`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:127:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--leading-tight` through `--leading-loose` and `--measure: 34em`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:154:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the weight and text-size tokens.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:176:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the grey, primary and accent ramps.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:185:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) writes every ramp in HSL.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:194:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) shows a completed nine-shade primary ramp.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:203:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) raises saturation toward both ends.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:216:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) rotates hue across each ramp.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:225:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) ships cool greys and names the warm hue to swap in.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:231:- **When not to:** A decorative hairline that merely divides content has no contrast obligation. Text and non-text are two different tokens.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:234:- **See also:** [web-accessibility-patterns.md](web-accessibility-patterns.md) and [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:243:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the dark-mode role overrides.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:264:- **See also:** [web-visual-hierarchy.md](web-visual-hierarchy.md) and [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:300:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the base elevation values these treatments extend.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:322:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) holds the single-shadow default this scale replaces.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:338:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) holds the five-elevation set.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:3:description: Spacing, type, colour, shadow, radius, motion and token values for web interfaces.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:9:  - \"design token roles\"\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:25:This file covers the value scales and construction methods for spacing, type, colour, elevation, radius, borders, images and token roles.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:30:- Building a colour ramp or a token set from scratch.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:32:- Choosing which grey carries which text role, or retuning a token file for a project.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:56:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the scale as custom properties.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:64:- **Why:** Same logic as the other scales: decide once, reuse everywhere. The token file maps them to `--opacity-1` through `--opacity-6` from `.05` to `.8`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:68:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:109:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--text-xs` through `--text-7xl`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:118:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--weight-normal` and `--weight-bold`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:127:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries `--leading-tight` through `--leading-loose` and `--measure: 34em`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:154:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the weight and text-size tokens.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:176:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the grey, primary and accent ramps.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:185:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) writes every ramp in HSL.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:194:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) shows a completed nine-shade primary ramp.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:203:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) raises saturation toward both ends.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:216:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) rotates hue across each ramp.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:225:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) ships cool greys and names the warm hue to swap in.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:231:- **When not to:** A decorative hairline that merely divides content has no contrast obligation. Text and non-text are two different tokens.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:234:- **See also:** [web-accessibility-patterns.md](web-accessibility-patterns.md) and [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:243:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the dark-mode role overrides.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:264:- **See also:** [web-visual-hierarchy.md](web-visual-hierarchy.md) and [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css).\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:300:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) carries the base elevation values these treatments extend.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:322:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) holds the single-shadow default this scale replaces.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:338:- **See also:** [tokens.css](../assets/tokens.css) holds the five-elevation set.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \\\"innerHTML\\\\|eval(\\\\|csrf\\\\|XSS\\\\|auth\\\\|secret\\\\|password\\\\|token\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-hierarchy.md .sk