{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873220640,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2d134f001MaUHjyF7i7dN7y","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2ce5d6001ED5gcjBuueZb61","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-93c816ff84c4156c","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && sed -n '474,600p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-hierarchy.md"},"output":"## 6. THE REVIEW PASS\n\nAn audit over UI code rather than a rendered picture. Every finding names a file, a line, the criterion it violates and the fix.\n\nThis pass starts from the code and works forward to findings, whether or not anyone has complained. The diagnosis tables in Section 3 start from a complaint and work back to a cause. Use both on a substantial review, because the checklist catches what nobody noticed and the diagnosis table explains what somebody did.\n\n### Accessibility, critical\n\nFix before merge. Each row breaks the interface for someone.\n\n| Check | WCAG | What to look for |\n|---|---|---|\n| Images without alt | 1.1.1 | `<img>` with no `alt` attribute |\n| Icon-only buttons | 4.1.2 | `<button>` containing only an SVG or icon, with no accessible name. See [A2](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a2-accessible-name-order) |\n| Form inputs without labels | 1.3.1 | `<input>`, `<select>` or `<textarea>` with no associated `<label>` and no `aria-label` |\n| Non-semantic click handlers | 2.1.1 | `<div onClick>` or `<span onClick>` without `role`, `tabIndex` and `onKeyDown`. See [A3](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a3-roving-tabindex-and-active-descendant) |\n| Missing link destination | 2.1.1 | `<a>` with only `onClick` and no `href` |\n| HTML illustrations unlabelled | 1.1.1 | A composition of divs with no `aria-label`, so a screen reader announces the DOM tree |\n\n### Accessibility, serious\n\n| Check | WCAG | What to look for |\n|---|---|---|\n| Focus indicator removed | 2.4.7 | `outline-none` or `outline: none` with no visible focus replacement. Keep a visible focus indicator that survives forced-colors mode. See [A5](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a5-focus-visible-styling) and [A8](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a8-forced-colors) |\n| Missing keyboard handlers | 2.1.1 | Interactive elements with `onClick` but no `onKeyDown` or `onKeyUp`. See [A13](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a13-menu-button) |\n| Colour-only information | 1.4.1 | Status or error indicated by colour alone, with no icon or text |\n| Touch target too small | 2.5.5 | Clickable elements under 44 by 44px. Expand with padding or a negative-inset pseudo-element, not by growing the visual box |\n| Text contrast below minimum | 1.4.3 | Normal text under 4.5:1. The 3:1 allowance applies only to 24px regular or 18.66px bold |\n| Functional border contrast | 1.4.11 | A border that is the only thing identifying a control, under 3:1 against its background |\n| Tooltip on a disabled button | 4.1.2 | Disabled elements are not focusable, so the tooltip is unreachable. See [A14](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a14-tooltip) |\n| Interactive content in a hover tooltip | 2.1.1 | The content cannot be reached by keyboard. See [A14](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a14-tooltip) |\n\n### Accessibility, moderate\n\n| Check | WCAG | What to look for |\n|---|---|---|\n| Heading hierarchy | 1.3.1 | Skipped levels, such as `h1` straight to `h3` |\n| Positive tabIndex | 2.4.3 | `tabIndex` greater than 0, which disrupts natural tab order. See [A3](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a3-roving-tabindex-and-active-descendant) |\n| Role without required attributes | 4.1.2 | `role=\"button\"` with no `tabIndex=\"0\"` |\n| List keyboard navigation | 2.1.1 | A sequential list of focusable elements not navigable with arrow keys. See [A3](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a3-roving-tabindex-and-active-descendant) |\n\n### Visual and component checks\n\n**Layout and spacing**\n\n- Spacing values that are not on the spacing scale in [web-visual-values.md](web-visual-values.md).\n- Equal spacing inside and between groups, which makes grouping ambiguous.\n- Overflow and alignment problems, `z-index` conflicts.\n- Percentage widths on elements that should not scale.\n\n**Typography**\n\n- Mixed font families, weights or sizes with no system behind them.\n- Font sizes off the type scale, or `em` used for the type scale.\n- Line height not inversely tracking size, measure outside 45 to 75 characters.\n- Missing font fallbacks.\n- Font weight changing on hover or selected state, which shifts layout.\n\n**Colour and contrast**\n\n- Contrast below the minimums above.\n- Grey text on a coloured background.\n- Shades generated at runtime with `lighten()` or `darken()`.\n- Dark mode inconsistencies: a mechanically inverted ramp, accents that were not desaturated, text a shade too bright.\n\n**Components**\n\n- Missing button states: disabled, loading, hover, active, focus. The `:active` state needs a scale transform.\n- Missing form field states: error, success, disabled.\n- Inconsistent borders, shadows or icon sizing.\n- Shadows chosen by looks rather than by z-position, or two elevation systems mixed in one project.\n\n**Motion**\n\n- Motion timing and easing checks live in [web-motion-and-interaction.md](web-motion-and-interaction.md).\n\n### Report format\n\nGroup by severity, most severe first. Every finding carries a location, the offending code, the fix and the criterion where one applies.\n\n```text\nUI REVIEW: <file or scope>\n\nCRITICAL (n)\n  [A11Y] path/to/file.tsx line 24: Button has no accessible name\n    <button><CloseIcon /></button>\n    Fix: add aria-label=\"Close\"\n    WCAG: 4.1.2\n\nSERIOUS (n)\n  [VISUAL] path/to/file.css line 88: Off-scale spacing (17px)\n    padding: 17px;\n    Fix: use 16px (--space-4)\n\nMODERATE (n)\n  ...\n\nSUMMARY: n critical, n serious, n moderate\n```\n\nReport a count of zero explicitly rather than omitting the tier. A missing tier reads as \"not checked\".\n\n### Rules for the reviewer\n\n1. Read the files before assessing them. No finding from a filename or a guess.\n2. Give a line number and the actual snippet for every finding.\n3. Give the fix, not only the problem.\n4. Order by severity, critical accessibility first, always.\n5. Do not report a value as off-scale without checking the project's own token file first, because an established system outranks the defaults here.\n6. Offer to apply the fixes, and do not apply them unasked.\n\n---\n\n## 7. COMPLETION CHECKLIST AND QUALITY GATES\n\n### Task completion checklist\n\nA UI task is complete when:\n\n- [ ] Every spatial value, font size, weight, shadow, radius and duration came from a scale, or from an established system that supersedes it.\n- [ ] The content has a stated primary, secondary and tertiary tier, separated by weight and colour rather than size alone.\n- [ ] Exactly one primary action is styled as primary on the surface.\n- [ ] Group spacing exceeds within-group spacing everywhere grouping is meaningful.\n- [ ] Every text and control pair meets its contrast minimum (4.5:1 normal text, 3:1 large text and functional non-text).\n- [ ] Interactive elements carry their full state set, and focus is visible.\n- [ ] Motion durations sit in their band, similar elements share values and nothing animates that should not.\n- [ ] No hard rule in this file is violated, or each deviation is stated with its reason.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## 6. THE REVIEW PASS\n\nAn audit over UI code rather than a rendered picture. Every finding names a file, a line, the criterion it violates and the fix.\n\nThis pass starts from the code and works forward to findings, whether or not anyone has complained. The diagnosis tables in Section 3 start from a complaint and work back to a cause. Use both on a substantial review, because the checklist catches what nobody noticed and the diagnosis table explains what somebody did.\n\n### Accessibility, critical\n\nFix before merge. Each row breaks the interface for someone.\n\n| Check | WCAG | What to look for |\n|---|---|---|\n| Images without alt | 1.1.1 | `<img>` with no `alt` attribute |\n| Icon-only buttons | 4.1.2 | `<button>` containing only an SVG or icon, with no accessible name. See [A2](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a2-accessible-name-order) |\n| Form inputs without labels | 1.3.1 | `<input>`, `<select>` or `<textarea>` with no associated `<label>` and no `aria-label` |\n| Non-semantic click handlers | 2.1.1 | `<div onClick>` or `<span onClick>` without `role`, `tabIndex` and `onKeyDown`. See [A3](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a3-roving-tabindex-and-active-descendant) |\n| Missing link destination | 2.1.1 | `<a>` with only `onClick` and no `href` |\n| HTML illustrations unlabelled | 1.1.1 | A composition of divs with no `aria-label`, so a screen reader announces the DOM tree |\n\n### Accessibility, serious\n\n| Check | WCAG | What to look for |\n|---|---|---|\n| Focus indicator removed | 2.4.7 | `outline-none` or `outline: none` with no visible focus replacement. Keep a visible focus indicator that survives forced-colors mode. See [A5](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a5-focus-visible-styling) and [A8](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a8-forced-colors) |\n| Missing keyboard handlers | 2.1.1 | Interactive elements with `onClick` but no `onKeyDown` or `onKeyUp`. See [A13](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a13-menu-button) |\n| Colour-only information | 1.4.1 | Status or error indicated by colour alone, with no icon or text |\n| Touch target too small | 2.5.5 | Clickable elements under 44 by 44px. Expand with padding or a negative-inset pseudo-element, not by growing the visual box |\n| Text contrast below minimum | 1.4.3 | Normal text under 4.5:1. The 3:1 allowance applies only to 24px regular or 18.66px bold |\n| Functional border contrast | 1.4.11 | A border that is the only thing identifying a control, under 3:1 against its background |\n| Tooltip on a disabled button | 4.1.2 | Disabled elements are not focusable, so the tooltip is unreachable. See [A14](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a14-tooltip) |\n| Interactive content in a hover tooltip | 2.1.1 | The content cannot be reached by keyboard. See [A14](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a14-tooltip) |\n\n### Accessibility, moderate\n\n| Check | WCAG | What to look for |\n|---|---|---|\n| Heading hierarchy | 1.3.1 | Skipped levels, such as `h1` straight to `h3` |\n| Positive tabIndex | 2.4.3 | `tabIndex` greater than 0, which disrupts natural tab order. See [A3](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a3-roving-tabindex-and-active-descendant) |\n| Role without required attributes | 4.1.2 | `role=\"button\"` with no `tabIndex=\"0\"` |\n| List keyboard navigation | 2.1.1 | A sequential list of focusable elements not navigable with arrow keys. See [A3](web-accessibility-patterns.md#a3-roving-tabindex-and-active-descendant) |\n\n### Visual and component checks\n\n**Layout and spacing**\n\n- Spacing values that are not on the spacing scale in [web-visual-values.md](web-visual-values.md).\n- Equal spacing inside and between groups, which makes grouping ambiguous.\n- Overflow and alignment problems, `z-index` conflicts.\n- Percentage widths on elements that should not scale.\n\n**Typography**\n\n- Mixed font families, weights or sizes with no system behind them.\n- Font sizes off the type scale, or `em` used for the type scale.\n- Line height not inversely tracking size, measure outside 45 to 75 characters.\n- Missing font fallbacks.\n- Font weight changing on hover or selected state, which shifts layout.\n\n**Colour and contrast**\n\n- Contrast below the minimums above.\n- Grey text on a coloured background.\n- Shades generated at runtime with `lighten()` or `darken()`.\n- Dark mode inconsistencies: a mechanically inverted ramp, accents that were not desaturated, text a shade too bright.\n\n**Components**\n\n- Missing button states: disabled, loading, hover, active, focus. The `:active` state needs a scale transform.\n- Missing form field states: error, success, disabled.\n- Inconsistent borders, shadows or icon sizing.\n- Shadows chosen by looks rather than by z-position, or two elevation systems mixed in one project.\n\n**Motion**\n\n- Motion timing and easing checks live in [web-motion-and-interaction.md](web-motion-and-interaction.md).\n\n### Report format\n\nGroup by severity, most severe first. Every finding carries a location, the offending code, the fix and the criterion where one applies.\n\n```text\nUI REVIEW: <file or scope>\n\nCRITICAL (n)\n  [A11Y] path/to/file.tsx line 24: Button has no accessible name\n    <button><CloseIcon /></button>\n    Fix: add aria-label=\"Close\"\n    WCAG: 4.1.2\n\nSERIOUS (n)\n  [VISUAL] path/to/file.css line 88: Off-scale spacing (17px)\n    padding: 17px;\n    Fix: use 16px (--space-4)\n\nMODERATE (n)\n  ...\n\nSUMMARY: n critical, n serious, n moderate\n```\n\nReport a count of zero explicitly rather than omitting the tier. A missing tier reads as \"not checked\".\n\n### Rules for the reviewer\n\n1. Read the files before assessing them. No finding from a filename or a guess.\n2. Give a line number and the actual snippet for every finding.\n3. Give the fix, not only the problem.\n4. Order by severity, critical accessibility first, always.\n5. Do not report a value as off-scale without checking the project's own token file first, because an established system outranks the defaults here.\n6. Offer to apply the fixes, and do not apply them unasked.\n\n---\n\n## 7. COMPLETION CHECKLIST AND QUALITY GATES\n\n### Task completion checklist\n\nA UI task is complete when:\n\n- [ ] Every spatial value, font size, weight, shadow, radius and duration came from a scale, or from an established system that supersedes it.\n- [ ] The content has a stated primary, secondary and tertiary tier, separated by weight and colour rather than size alone.\n- [ ] Exactly one primary action is styled as primary on the surface.\n- [ ] Group spacing exceeds within-group spacing everywhere grouping is meaningful.\n- [ ] Every text and control pair meets its contrast minimum (4.5:1 normal text, 3:1 large text and functional non-text).\n- [ ] Interactive elements carry their full state set, and focus is visible.\n- [ ] Motion durations sit in their band, similar elements share values and nothing animates that should not.\n- [ ] No hard rule in this file is violated, or each deviation is stated with its reason.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && sed -n '474,600p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-hierarchy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873220431,"end":1793873220640}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1793873222086,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"id":"prt_1ab2d19c6001aQ1c4XwVI2P7aS","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2ce5d6001ED5gcjBuueZb61","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"d0b33eedb2284cb2e1178c9ed78dd1f7bc02c680","cost":0.002446242,"tokens":{"input":1519,"output":91,"reasoning":2550,"cache":{"read":211264,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793873223770,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"id":"prt_1ab2d205a001V31KS6FoNarI6o","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2d19d0001Qa9qQi11BmpZKF","type":"step-start","snapshot":"d0b33eedb2284cb2e1178c9ed78dd1f7bc02c680"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873224815,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2d21ed002WziB9TQh9DL0A3","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2d19d0001Qa9qQi11BmpZKF","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-852f2236f55cf008","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \"animate a shadow\\|Animating a shadow\\|shadow.*animat\\|animat.*shadow\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/*.md | head; echo \"=== old excerpt ===\"; git show 10474a9567:.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-fundamentals/references/depth-and-detail.md | sed -n '/Animating a shadow/,/Full button/p' | head -30"},"output":"=== old excerpt ===\n### Animating a shadow\n\nTransitioning `box-shadow` directly forces an expensive repaint on every frame. Put the target shadow on a pseudo-element and animate its `opacity` instead:\n\n```css\n.card { position: relative; box-shadow: var(--shadow-1); }\n.card::after {\n  content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; border-radius: inherit;\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-3); opacity: 0; transition: opacity 180ms ease;\n  pointer-events: none;\n}\n.card:hover::after { opacity: 1; }\n```\n\nThe duration belongs to the state-change band in [`motion-principles.md`](motion-principles.md) Section 5.\n\n### Full button anatomy\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== old excerpt ===\n### Animating a shadow\n\nTransitioning `box-shadow` directly forces an expensive repaint on every frame. Put the target shadow on a pseudo-element and animate its `opacity` instead:\n\n```css\n.card { position: relative; box-shadow: var(--shadow-1); }\n.card::after {\n  content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0; border-radius: inherit;\n  box-shadow: var(--shadow-3); opacity: 0; transition: opacity 180ms ease;\n  pointer-events: none;\n}\n.card:hover::after { opacity: 1; }\n```\n\nThe duration belongs to the state-change band in [`motion-principles.md`](motion-principles.md) Section 5.\n\n### Full button anatomy\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \\\"animate a shadow\\\\|Animating a shadow\\\\|shadow.*animat\\\\|animat.*shadow\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/*.md | head; echo \\\"=== old excerpt ===\\\"; git show 10474a9567:.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-fundamentals/references/depth-and-detail.md | sed -n '/Animating a shadow/,/Full button/p' | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873224173,"end":1793873224815}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1793873225736,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"id":"prt_1ab2d2808001WjgNQ2qiytqBnC","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2d19d0001Qa9qQi11BmpZKF","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"d0b33eedb2284cb2e1178c9ed78dd1f7bc02c680","cost":0.001477266,"tokens":{"input":4503,"output":163,"reasoning":110,"cache":{"read":212672,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1793873227289,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"id":"prt_1ab2d2e19001AC9nG96MRP8vz9","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2d2811001VcJXwg4FOtyvDd","type":"step-start","snapshot":"d0b33eedb2284cb2e1178c9ed78dd1f7bc02c680"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873227959,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2d2e780027OmwyjienmXCPr","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2d2811001VcJXwg4FOtyvDd","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8042be2008829f8f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -n \"box-shadow\\|pseudo-element\\|::after\\|paint\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md | head -20"},"output":".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md:123:- **Rule:** Make every target a thumb operates at least 44 by 44px and treat 32px as the absolute minimum for a dense pointer-driven interface. Expand a small target with padding or a negative-inset pseudo-element rather than by growing the visual box.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md:307:- **When not to:** Use a large blur once on a static decorative layer that never repaints.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md:308:- **Pitfall:** A blurred backdrop on a scrolling header repaints on every frame.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:268:- **Rule:** Decide the element's profile, then mimic how light would hit that shape. Light comes from above and people look slightly down at their screens, so the top edge of a raised element is visible and the bottom edge of an inset one is. Each element needs both the lit edge and the blocked light in a single comma-separated `box-shadow`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:269:- **Why:** Borrow the real-world cue and stop, because depth comes from mimicking one light source consistently, not from chasing photorealism. Raised and inset are the same trick. Two `box-shadow` declarations on one selector do not combine, and the second silently discards the first.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:279:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:286:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:292:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:306:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:328:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:357:  box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:455:- **Rule:** Contain user-uploaded content in fixed-size containers with `background-size: cover`, cropping the overflow. Prevent background bleed, where a user photo's edges match the UI background, with a subtle inset shadow such as `box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px hsla(0,0%,0%,.1)` rather than a border. For photography itself, use a photographer or good stock and never design against placeholders while planning to shoot something on a phone later.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md:123:- **Rule:** Make every target a thumb operates at least 44 by 44px and treat 32px as the absolute minimum for a dense pointer-driven interface. Expand a small target with padding or a negative-inset pseudo-element rather than by growing the visual box.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md:307:- **When not to:** Use a large blur once on a static decorative layer that never repaints.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md:308:- **Pitfall:** A blurred backdrop on a scrolling header repaints on every frame.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:268:- **Rule:** Decide the element's profile, then mimic how light would hit that shape. Light comes from above and people look slightly down at their screens, so the top edge of a raised element is visible and the bottom edge of an inset one is. Each element needs both the lit edge and the blocked light in a single comma-separated `box-shadow`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:269:- **Why:** Borrow the real-world cue and stop, because depth comes from mimicking one light source consistently, not from chasing photorealism. Raised and inset are the same trick. Two `box-shadow` declarations on one selector do not combine, and the second silently discards the first.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:279:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:286:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:292:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:306:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:328:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:357:  box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:455:- **Rule:** Contain user-uploaded content in fixed-size containers with `background-size: cover`, cropping the overflow. Prevent background bleed, where a user photo's edges match the UI background, with a subtle inset shadow such as `box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px hsla(0,0%,0%,.1)` rather than a border. For photography itself, use a photographer or good stock and never design against placeholders while planning to shoot something on a phone later.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -n \\\"box-shadow\\\\|pseudo-element\\\\|::after\\\\|paint\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873227384,"end":1793873227959}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873227974,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2d2f94001c2ua25X3psFA4f","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2d2811001VcJXwg4FOtyvDd","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-82cc2c9a02d2b9fc","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && git show 10474a9567:.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-fundamentals/references/interaction-craft.md | grep -n \"animate\\|will-change\\|paint\\|performance\" | head -20"},"output":"3:description: The implementation-level details that make an interface feel right — inputs, touch, focus, keyboard, performance and feedback — grouped as build-time checks.\n123:- Toggle `will-change` on for the duration of an unperformant scroll animation and off afterwards. A permanent `will-change` is its own leak.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:description: The implementation-level details that make an interface feel right — inputs, touch, focus, keyboard, performance and feedback — grouped as build-time checks.\n123:- Toggle `will-change` on for the duration of an unperformant scroll animation and off afterwards. A permanent `will-change` is its own leak.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && git show 10474a9567:.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-fundamentals/references/interaction-craft.md | grep -n \\\"animate\\\\|will-change\\\\|paint\\\\|performance\\\" | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873227668,"end":1793873227974}}}}
