{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873275801,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2dea85001Oil6O22aeaiHwN","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2dddf5001BY5V01yJgTsEAv","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-94b0c6fc1c80f0f2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && git show 10474a9567:.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-fundamentals/references/depth-and-detail.md | grep -n \"^### \" "},"output":"23:### Purpose\n27:### When to Use\n35:### Core Principle\n39:### Prerequisites\n114:### Three parallel systems, pick one\n129:### Shadow color, and the pure-black question\n139:### Animating a shadow\n155:### Full button anatomy\n193:### Baseline, not center\n201:### Letter-spacing\n208:### Line breaking\n214:### Underlines and synthesis\n220:### Numerals\n226:### Choosing typefaces without taste\n250:### Grids are overrated\n262:### Concentric radius\n278:### Semi-transparent borders\n284:### Break the default component shape\n298:### Text over photos\n309:### Everything has an intended size\n315:### User-uploaded content\n322:### Photos themselves\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"23:### Purpose\n27:### When to Use\n35:### Core Principle\n39:### Prerequisites\n114:### Three parallel systems, pick one\n129:### Shadow color, and the pure-black question\n139:### Animating a shadow\n155:### Full button anatomy\n193:### Baseline, not center\n201:### Letter-spacing\n208:### Line breaking\n214:### Underlines and synthesis\n220:### Numerals\n226:### Choosing typefaces without taste\n250:### Grids are overrated\n262:### Concentric radius\n278:### Semi-transparent borders\n284:### Break the default component shape\n298:### Text over photos\n309:### Everything has an intended size\n315:### User-uploaded content\n322:### Photos themselves\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && git show 10474a9567:.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-fundamentals/references/depth-and-detail.md | grep -n \\\"^### \\\" \"}"},"time":{"start":1793873275525,"end":1793873275801}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873275853,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2de95e0029hsZR5b4g1uIgg","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2dddf5001BY5V01yJgTsEAv","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0b90b26c6cff4ed","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \"shadcn\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart | grep -v changelog | head -10"},"output":".skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/color-system.md:263:The rule is the HTML corpus' projection of the frozen shadcn examples: line and area examples\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md:118:The visual pass moves the corpus to the compact register in the frozen shadcn examples: a title\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md:133:The values are measured from the frozen shadcn copy: the card header keeps title and description\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md:144:### The shadcn visual register\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md:146:The corpus keeps the shadcn choices that survive the standalone-file constraint. The frozen line\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md:149:shadcn ships: a vertical 0.8-to-0.1 gradient with 0.4 flat opacity for stacked areas\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/scripts/check-corpus.cjs:1832:    record('tooltip-card', 'error', file, `the HTML tooltip has no ${what}. The card follows the measured shadcn content spacing and indicator register`);\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/assets/style-reference/evilcharts/palettes.json:42:    \"note\": \"The chart register and the proof-sheet register, side by side. Not colours, and like the corner ladder they sit in their own object for that reason: they are the other half of the vocabulary a template reads, and they live here so the check that rejects a size off the scale reads a value rather than restating one. The chart roles are the compact card scale measured from the frozen shadcn copy, and the metric rung is the value a card leads with when its data has a meaningful baseline; in-figure text steps down a rung as a form gets denser, which is the scale working.\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/assets/style-reference/evilcharts/DESIGN.md:18:evilcharts is a chart component library built on shadcn's tokens. Its language is a near-white\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/color-system.md:263:The rule is the HTML corpus' projection of the frozen shadcn examples: line and area examples\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md:118:The visual pass moves the corpus to the compact register in the frozen shadcn examples: a title\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md:133:The values are measured from the frozen shadcn copy: the card header keeps title and description\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md:144:### The shadcn visual register\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md:146:The corpus keeps the shadcn choices that survive the standalone-file constraint. The frozen line\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/references/template-contract.md:149:shadcn ships: a vertical 0.8-to-0.1 gradient with 0.4 flat opacity for stacked areas\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/scripts/check-corpus.cjs:1832:    record('tooltip-card', 'error', file, `the HTML tooltip has no ${what}. The card follows the measured shadcn content spacing and indicator register`);\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/assets/style-reference/evilcharts/palettes.json:42:    \"note\": \"The chart register and the proof-sheet register, side by side. Not colours, and like the corner ladder they sit in their own object for that reason: they are the other half of the vocabulary a template reads, and they live here so the check that rejects a size off the scale reads a value rather than restating one. The chart roles are the compact card scale measured from the frozen shadcn copy, and the metric rung is the value a card leads with when its data has a meaningful baseline; in-figure text steps down a rung as a form gets denser, which is the scale working.\",\n.skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart/assets/style-reference/evilcharts/DESIGN.md:18:evilcharts is a chart component library built on shadcn's tokens. Its language is a near-white\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -rn \\\"shadcn\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-design/sk-design-chart | grep -v changelog | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873275230,"end":1793873275853}}}}
