{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873413232,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab2fe8d4001qYiVlj78zqdZ47","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab2fe15d001KmQtA6iABmTsdT","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-83f12ef586f85996","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - 021-deprecate-fundamentals\ndescription: Externalized review strategy for the deepseek fan-out lineage of the sk-design 021 change set review.\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - 021 Deprecate Fundamentals\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nReview of `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals`, the phased packet that retires\n`sk-design-fundamentals`, moves its screen value guidance into `sk-code-frontend`, and removes\nresearch citations from `sk-design-chart`. The reviewed change set is the worktree state against\nbaseline `10474a9567`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Reworking the retired guidance itself, beyond checking that no rule was lost.\n- Re-running repo gates that write outside this lineage: `validate.sh`, `generate-context.js`,\n  `compiled-route-sync`, mirror sync tools, and any git write.\n- Judging historical changelog entries, the dated benchmark run report, or style-library site\n  descriptions that mention research: the packet explicitly keeps them as records.\n- Treating the untracked `specs/` packet or recovery scratch logs as production code.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- `stopPolicy` is `max-iterations`: the lineage runs iterations 1 through 5, then synthesizes with\n  `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`. Convergence ratios are telemetry only.\n- Any confirmed active P0 forces the terminal verdict `FAIL`; a P1 without a P0 yields\n  `CONDITIONAL`; P2-only yields `PASS` with advisories.\n- A scope or evidence gate failure also blocks PASS and is recorded in the iteration.\n\n---\n\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\n| [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n\n---\n\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Swept: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\n\n---\n\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\nIteration 1: correctness. Confirm the retirement is complete on disk and in routing, then test\nwhether value and visual-review prompts still reach the new owner.\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/spec.md` and its three phase\n  children (`001-frontend-upgrade`, `002-retire-fundamentals`, `003-chart-research-cleanup`);\n  the worktree diff against `10474a9567`.\n- Behavior claims: the sk-design hub registers exactly three modes with no default; no live hub\n  file names the deleted folder; the five baseline value prompts and the new value, hierarchy and\n  motion prompts reach `sk-code-frontend`; the four chart files keep every rule without a research\n  citation; each phase validates under `--strict`.\n- Reuse and convention pointers: `.skilled/skills/sk-design/mode-registry.json` and\n  `hub-router.json` as the authored routing truth; `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs` as the\n  read-only replay front door; `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md` as stage two.\n- Review risks and gaps: the change set is doc- and routing-heavy, so correctness is mostly\n  contradiction and reach analysis; `specs/` is untracked in this worktree; generated metadata can\n  drift from its source; compiled manifests are hash-pinned.\n- Out of scope: any write outside\n  `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek`.\n\n---\n\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| [scope files in deep-review-config.json] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2] | [partial/complete] |\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n---\n\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n- Max iterations: 5\n- Convergence threshold: 0.1\n- Rolling STOP threshold: 0.08\n- No-progress threshold: 0.05\n- Coverage stabilization passes required: 1\n- Session lineage: sessionId=fanout-deepseek-1793872885543-931fzb, parentSessionId=null, generation=1, lineageMode=new\n- Findings registry: `deep-review-findings-registry.json`\n- Release-readiness states: in-progress | converged | release-blocking\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Severity threshold: P2\n- Review target type: spec-folder\n- Cross-reference checks: core=[spec_code, checklist_evidence], overlay=[skill_agent, agent_cross_runtime, feature_catalog_code, playbook_capability]\n- Started: 2026-11-05T10:09:34Z\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - 021-deprecate-fundamentals\\ndescription: Externalized review strategy for the deepseek fan-out lineage of the sk-design 021 change set review.\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Review Strategy - 021 Deprecate Fundamentals\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nReview of `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals`, the phased packet that retires\\n`sk-design-fundamentals`, moves its screen value guidance into `sk-code-frontend`, and removes\\nresearch citations from `sk-design-chart`. The reviewed change set is the worktree state against\\nbaseline `10474a9567`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- [ ] D1 Correctness, Logic errors, off-by-one, wrong return types, broken invariants\\n- [ ] D2 Security, Injection, auth bypass, secrets exposure, unsafe deserialization\\n- [ ] D3 Traceability, Spec/code alignment, checklist evidence, cross-reference integrity\\n- [ ] D4 Maintainability, Patterns, clarity, documentation quality, safe follow-on change cost\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Reworking the retired guidance itself, beyond checking that no rule was lost.\\n- Re-running repo gates that write outside this lineage: `validate.sh`, `generate-context.js`,\\n  `compiled-route-sync`, mirror sync tools, and any git write.\\n- Judging historical changelog entries, the dated benchmark run report, or style-library site\\n  descriptions that mention research: the packet explicitly keeps them as records.\\n- Treating the untracked `specs/` packet or recovery scratch logs as production code.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- `stopPolicy` is `max-iterations`: the lineage runs iterations 1 through 5, then synthesizes with\\n  `stopReason: maxIterationsReached`. Convergence ratios are telemetry only.\\n- Any confirmed active P0 forces the terminal verdict `FAIL`; a P1 without a P0 yields\\n  `CONDITIONAL`; P2-only yields `PASS` with advisories.\\n- A scope or evidence gate failure also blocks PASS and is recorded in the iteration.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\\n\\n| Dimension | Verdict | Iteration | Summary |\\n|-----------|---------|-----------|---------|\\n| [D1 Correctness] | [PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL] | [N] | [1-sentence result] |\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\\n\\n[Findings are tracked in `deep-review-findings-registry.json`. This section provides a running count summary updated after each iteration.]\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Swept: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated -- consolidated from iteration dead-end data]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\nIteration 1: correctness. Confirm the retirement is complete on disk and in routing, then test\\nwhether value and visual-review prompts still reach the new owner.\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/spec.md` and its three phase\\n  children (`001-frontend-upgrade`, `002-retire-fundamentals`, `003-chart-research-cleanup`);\\n  the worktree diff against `10474a9567`.\\n- Behavior claims: the sk-design hub registers exactly three modes with no default; no live hub\\n  file names the deleted folder; the five baseline value prompts and the new value, hierarchy and\\n  motion prompts reach `sk-code-frontend`; the four chart files keep every rule without a research\\n  citation; each phase validates under `--strict`.\\n- Reuse and convention pointers: `.skilled/skills/sk-design/mode-registry.json` and\\n  `hub-router.json` as the authored routing truth; `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs` as the\\n  read-only replay front door; `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/ROUTER.md` as stage two.\\n- Review risks and gaps: the change set is doc- and routing-heavy, so correctness is mostly\\n  contradiction and reach analysis; `specs/` is untracked in this worktree; generated metadata can\\n  drift from its source; compiled manifests are hash-pinned.\\n- Out of scope: any write outside\\n  `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n[Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\\n| [scope files in deep-review-config.json] | [D1, D3] | [N] | [0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2] | [partial/complete] |\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n- Max iterations: 5\\n- Convergence thre