ed there.'),\n('R3-P2-006','.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md','247','class-of-bug','The retired depth-and-detail shadow-animation technique is absent from web-visual-values.md and web-motion-and-interaction.md, so the phase lost a performance rule it was meant to carry.'),\n('R4-P2-007','.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md','361','instance-only','The new motion reference permits a client-side session-expiry redirect without saying the server must still refuse protected data, so a reader can treat a UX redirect as the authorization boundary.'),\n('R5-P2-008','.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/001-sk-code/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json','190','class-of-bug','The sk-code hub canary never exercises the new code-frontend-visual class, so the visual-review phrase failure is invisible to the compiled-route regression harness.'),\n]\nfor fid,path,lines,cls,claim in findings:\n    desc=re.sub(r'\\s+',' ',claim).strip().lower()[:80]\n    h=hashlib.sha256(f\"{path}\\x1f{lines}\\x1f{cls}\\x1f{desc}\".encode()).hexdigest()\n    print(fid,h)\nEOF"},"output":"R1-P1-001 23af1185fcbdcb2f7d1e2ca463ea69e5365665fd6f59a79425861022e3e9c2ad\nR1-P2-002 cfebd9dfda59726bed4e278b5b55d249cff71ccad406b33ab68715e5a93840bf\nR2-P2-003 4ef69bdd612f63ba681c05c8023620f4ae6af6645eb5976f7d0ce97bb9cc9eb9\nR2-P2-004 290c5a8d58a2fb8e0f6cca726e2fa064cc8b7cfc8ec2965c38b5167e1b602c45\nR3-P2-005 8671d8a8a1a7667da53361f26b2d34357f9bdde3fdbe03bc77a8574e1e9c8c22\nR3-P2-006 6f8eb7afe6e7c8a4a602bcced33091429e8ca128fbd3b5b97aed2f9ed413c148\nR4-P2-007 29940fe8d9d3c759840c38b9be0b94f9b7ab98e75e38ab716b9883c2753af2b7\nR5-P2-008 34b47e3cb9224bb9f8a35a51d3eba3fc156e626c36155345bab4762086ed91ab\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"R1-P1-001 23af1185fcbdcb2f7d1e2ca463ea69e5365665fd6f59a79425861022e3e9c2ad\nR1-P2-002 cfebd9dfda59726bed4e278b5b55d249cff71ccad406b33ab68715e5a93840bf\nR2-P2-003 4ef69bdd612f63ba681c05c8023620f4ae6af6645eb5976f7d0ce97bb9cc9eb9\nR2-P2-004 290c5a8d58a2fb8e0f6cca726e2fa064cc8b7cfc8ec2965c38b5167e1b602c45\nR3-P2-005 8671d8a8a1a7667da53361f26b2d34357f9bdde3fdbe03bc77a8574e1e9c8c22\nR3-P2-006 6f8eb7afe6e7c8a4a602bcced33091429e8ca128fbd3b5b97aed2f9ed413c148\nR4-P2-007 29940fe8d9d3c759840c38b9be0b94f9b7ab98e75e38ab716b9883c2753af2b7\nR5-P2-008 34b47e3cb9224bb9f8a35a51d3eba3fc156e626c36155345bab4762086ed91ab\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport hashlib,re\\nfindings=[\\n('R1-P1-001','.skilled/skills/sk-code/hub-router.json','90','cross-consumer','The sk-code hub documents \\\"design review findings\\\" and \\\"review this screen\\\" as frontend visual-intent phrases, but replaying \\\"design review findings\\\" and \\\"design review\\\" resolves to sk-code-review alone, so web-visual-hierarchy.md is not loaded.'),\\n('R1-P2-002','.skilled/skills/sk-design/graph-metadata.json','177-187','instance-only','sk-design graph-metadata.json keeps ten retired fundamentals phrases in derived.intent_signals while the phase summary says they were removed and the top-level intent_signals carries none of them.'),\\n('R2-P2-003','specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/002-retire-fundamentals/implementation-summary.md','75','instance-only','The phase 002 implementation summary lists mcp-figma/manual-testing-playbook/figma-to-code/node-to-token-markup.md as modified, but that file is byte-identical to baseline 10474a9567.'),\\n('R2-P2-004','specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/001-frontend-upgrade/acceptance-criteria.md','62','instance-only','Phase 001 AC-005 mixes a five-prompt baseline with an eight-prompt replay in one criterion, so its recorded evidence does not identify which prompt set proves the routing claim.'),\\n('R3-P2-005','.skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md','44','cross-consumer','The sk-code hub surface table and description.json still describe the frontend surface as web markup, layout, accessibility and Figma only, omitting the three visual references and tokens.css now shipped there.'),\\n('R3-P2-006','.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md','247','class-of-bug','The retired depth-and-detail shadow-animation technique is absent from web-visual-values.md and web-motion-and-interaction.md, so the phase lost a performance rule it was meant to carry.'),\\n('R4-P2-007','.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md','361','instance-only','The new motion reference permits a client-side session-expiry redirect without saying the server must still refuse protected data, so a reader can treat a UX redirect as the authorization boundary.'),\\n('R5-P2-008','.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/001-sk-code/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json','190','class-of-bug','The sk-code hub canary never exercises the new code-frontend-visual class, so the visual-review phrase failure is invisible to the compiled-route regression harness.'),\\n]\\nfor fid,path,lines,cls,claim in findings:\\n    desc=re.sub(r'\\\\s+',' ',claim).strip().lower()[:80]\\n    h=hashlib.sha256(f\\\"{path}\\\\x1f{lines}\\\\x1f{cls}\\\\x1f{desc}\\\".encode()).hexdigest()\\n    print(fid,h)\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873446398,"end":1793873448220}}}}
