{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873527784,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab31a889002cm4DOr7xbDe6vz","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab3193bb001iAPKCFz4KUGCWJ","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a93b62a911cd8bc","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Deep Review Iteration 2: Traceability\n\n## Dimension\n\nTraceability. Scope: do the packet's own acceptance criteria, implementation summaries and\nchangelogs match what is actually on disk, and does the recorded evidence identify a command that\ncan prove the claim?\n\n## Review Focus Addressed\n\nOperator focus, traceability half: the change set is measured against `spec.md`'s phase map and\nhandoff criteria, and each phase's recorded acceptance evidence is compared with the worktree. The\nrouting half of the focus was covered in iteration 1; the \"lost guidance\" and chart-citation\naccuracy parts are carried to iterations 3 and 5.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/spec.md:117-136` (phase map and handoff criteria)\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/001-frontend-upgrade/acceptance-criteria.md:54-77`\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/001-frontend-upgrade/implementation-summary.md:45-90`\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/002-retire-fundamentals/acceptance-criteria.md:54-77`\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/002-retire-fundamentals/implementation-summary.md:55-75`\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/003-chart-research-cleanup/acceptance-criteria.md:50-62`\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/003-chart-research-cleanup/implementation-summary.md:55-90`\n- the five new changelogs and the four chart references' rule groups\n\nCommand evidence used:\n\n- `compiled-route --hub sk-code` replays for the five baseline value prompts from the phase-1\n  brief (all five route `sk-code-frontend`)\n- `ls` on all five changelog files\n- version greps on `sk-code/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md`, `sk-design/SKILL.md` and\n  `sk-design-chart/SKILL.md`\n- row counts on `web-visual-hierarchy.md` (40 diagnosis rows, 21 review rows, 21 UX-law entries)\n- line counts on the three new references (566, 618, 642)\n- `git status --porcelain` compared row by row with each phase's \"Files Changed\" table\n- `node .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs` (5/5)\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new. R1-P1-001 remains active and keeps this iteration at CONDITIONAL under the active-finding\nmapping.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n3. **Phase 2's changed-file table names a file that never changed** -- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/002-retire-fundamentals/implementation-summary.md:75` -- The row says `.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/manual-testing-playbook/figma-to-code/node-to-token-markup.md` was modified to point at the frontend reference. The file is byte-identical to baseline `10474a9567` and contains no fundamentals or frontend reference at all.\n   Case: a reviewer or a future phase uses the table as the audit trail for the repoint, trusts\n   that this scenario was updated, and skips it. `git diff 10474a9567 --stat -- <path>` prints\n   nothing, while `grep -n 'fundamentals|web-visual-values'` on the file prints no line.\n   Finding class: instance-only\n   Scope proof: the same row-by-row comparison over all three implementation summaries found this\n   one false row; the other 45 rows name paths that are in `git status`.\n   Affected surface hints: [\"phase 2 implementation summary\", \"mcp-figma playbook audit\"]\n   Recommendation: drop the row, or update the scenario if the intended repoint is still needed.\n\n4. **Phase 1's routing criterion mixes a five-prompt baseline with an eight-prompt replay** -- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/001-frontend-upgrade/acceptance-criteria.md:62` -- AC-005 says \"Given the five baseline value prompts ... each one routes to sk-code-frontend\", but its verification cell says the replay routes \"all eight value, review and motion prompts\". The row records a `Met` status without naming which prompt set was replayed.\n   Case: a later reader repeats the gate with the five baseline prompts and cannot tell whether\n   the three extra prompts are a requirement, a sample, or the real contract. The phase summary\n   separately says \"all eight\", so the two documents disagree on the scope of the same evidence.\n   Finding class: instance-only\n   Scope proof: the three prompt counts appear only in this AC row and in the phase summary;\n   no list of the eight prompts is recorded in the packet.\n   Affected surface hints: [\"phase 1 acceptance criteria\", \"phase 1 implementation summary\", \"routing evidence\"]\n   Recommendation: name the eight prompts and their replay output in the AC, or narrow the\n   criterion to the five baseline prompts.\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | Phase map statuses match the worktree, the folder is deleted, the hub has three modes, the chart files have no research citation. The routing handoff criterion remains partial because R1-P1-001 shows a documented visual-review phrase outside the frontend surface. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | Ten of eleven phase-1 criteria, nine of ten phase-2 criteria and all five phase-3 criteria name a command that resolves on disk. AC-005's prompt count is ambiguous and the phase-2 file table carries one false row. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pass | The new `frontend-surface-visual-values` scenario declares `WEB_VISUAL_VALUES` and the two expected resources; `verify-router-sync.cjs` check 4 prints `PASS check 4` and the suite prints `5/5 checks passed`. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | No feature-catalog entry changes in this diff; the chart corpus and diagram feature catalogs are untouched. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | The five new changelogs exist; the canonical agent and four mirrors carry the new decide path (iteration 1 evidence). |\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- The phase summaries record `validate.sh --strict` results that this lineage is forbidden to\n  rerun. The review therefore checks the recorded evidence's specificity and cross-document\n  agreement, and does not claim the gate was re-observed. That is the same standard the packet's\n  own \"Known Limitations\" rows use.\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/` is untracked in this worktree, so git cannot show\n  an intra-packet delta. Baseline comparison is against `10474a9567` for the repo files and\n  against the packet's own text for the untracked docs.\n- The phase-2 file table's folder row shows as \"not changed\" in `git status` only because git\n  lists the deleted files individually; that is not a false claim.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- The five baseline value prompts named in the phase-1 brief all route to `sk-code-frontend`:\n  padding, type scale, palette, \"why does this screen look wrong\" and dropdown animation.\n- The four chart files keep the three rule groups the changelog names: the role split figures,\n  the radar/pie decision and the stacked-area one-row card.\n- All five new changelogs exist and carry the version they announce.\n- The three new references have the counts the acceptance criteria claim (566, 618, 642 lines;\n  40/21/21 hierarchy rows).\n- `verify-router-sync.cjs` passes all five legs, including the replay of the new visual-values\n  scenario.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **A wholesale false-files table in every phase.** Ruled out by row-by-row comparison; only one\n  row is false.\n- **A missing changelog or a version that disagrees with its changelog.** Ruled out by `ls` and\n  `grep` on all five files.\n- **A chart rule that lost its supporting figure.** Ruled out by reading the three rule groups\n  against the removed citations.\n\n## Next Focus\n\nDimension: maintainability. Check whether the canonical descriptions still match the new surface\ncontent, whether any retired rule failed to move, and whether the new files' own structure is\nsafe to change.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Deep Review Iteration 2: Traceability\\n\\n## Dimension\\n\\nTraceability. Scope: do the packet's own acceptance criteria, implementation summaries and\\nchangelogs match what is actually on disk, and does the recorded evidence identify a command that\\ncan prove the claim?\\n\\n## Review Focus Addressed\\n\\nOperator focus, traceability half: the change set is measured against `spec.md`'s phase map and\\nhandoff criteria, and each phase's recorded acceptance evidence is compared with the worktree. The\\nrouting half of the focus was covered in iteration 1; the \\\"lost guidance\\\" and chart-citation\\naccuracy parts are carried to iterations 3 and 5.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/spec.md:117-136` (phase map and handoff criteria)\\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/001-frontend-upgrade/acceptance-criteria.md:54-77`\\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/001-frontend-upgrade/implementation-summary.md:45-90`\\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/002-retire-fundamentals/acceptance-criteria.md:54-77`\\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/002-retire-fundamentals/implementation-summary.md:55-75`\\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/003-chart-research-cleanup/acceptance-criteria.md:50-62`\\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/003-chart-research-cleanup/implementation-summary.md:55-90`\\n- the five new changelogs and the four chart references' rule groups\\n\\nCommand evidence used:\\n\\n- `compiled-route --hub sk-code` replays for the five baseline value prompts from the phase-1\\n  brief (all five route `sk-code-frontend`)\\n- `ls` on all five changelog files\\n- version greps on `sk-code/SKILL.md`, `sk-code-frontend/SKILL.md`, `sk-design/SKILL.md` and\\n  `sk-design-chart/SKILL.md`\\n- row counts on `web-visual-hierarchy.md` (40 diagnosis rows, 21 review rows, 21 UX-law entries)\\n- line counts on the three new references (566, 618, 642)\\n- `git status --porcelain` compared row by row with each phase's \\\"Files Changed\\\" table\\n- `node .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/scripts/verify-router-sync.cjs` (5/5)\\n\\n## Findings by Severity\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new. R1-P1-001 remains active and keeps this iteration at CONDITIONAL under the active-finding\\nmapping.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n3. **Phase 2's changed-file table names a file that never changed** -- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/002-retire-fundamentals/implementation-summary.md:75` -- The row says `.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/manual-testing-playbook/figma-to-code/node-to-token-markup.md` was modified to point at the frontend reference. The file is byte-identical to baseline `10474a9567` and contains no fundamentals or frontend reference at all.\\n   Case: a reviewer or a future phase uses the table as the audit trail for the repoint, trusts\\n   that this scenario was updated, and skips it. `git diff 10474a9567 --stat -- <path>` prints\\n   nothing, while `grep -n 'fundamentals|web-visual-values'` on the file prints no line.\\n   Finding class: instance-only\\n   Scope proof: the same row-by-row comparison over all three implementation summaries found this\\n   one false row; the other 45 rows name paths that are in `git status`.\\n   Affected surface hints: [\\\"phase 2 implementation summary\\\", \\\"mcp-figma playbook audit\\\"]\\n   Recommendation: drop the row, or update the scenario if the intended repoint is still needed.\\n\\n4. **Phase 1's routing criterion mixes a five-prompt baseline with an eight-prompt replay** -- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/001-frontend-upgrade/acceptance-criteria.md:62` -- AC-005 says \\\"Given the five baseline value prompts ... each one routes to sk-code-frontend\\\", but its verification cell says the replay routes \\\"all eight value, review and motion prompts\\\". The row records a `Met` status without naming which prompt set was replayed.\\n   Case: a later reader repeats the gate with the five baseline prompts and cannot tell whether\\n   the three extra prompts are a requirement, a sample, or the real contract. The phase summary\\n   separately says \\\"all eight\\\", so the two documents disagree on the scope of the same evidence.\\n   Finding class: instance-only\\n   Scope proof: the three prompt counts appear only in this AC row and in the phase summary;\\n   no list of the eight prompts is recorded in the packet.\\n   Affected surface hints: [\\\"phase 1 acceptance criteria\\\", \\\"phase 1 implementation summary\\\", \\\"routing evidence\\\"]\\n   Recommendation: name the eight prompts and their replay output in the AC, or narrow the\\n   criterion to the five baseline prompts.\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | Phase map statuses match the worktree, the folder is deleted, the hub has three modes, the chart files have no research citation. The routing handoff criterion remains partial because R1-P1-001 shows a documented visual-review phrase outside the frontend surface. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | Ten of eleven phase-1 criteria, nine of ten phase-2 criteria and all five phase-3 criteria name a command that resolves on disk. AC-005's prompt count is ambiguous and the phase-2 file table carries one false row. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | pass | The new `frontend-surface-visual-values` scenario declares `WEB_VISUAL_VALUES` and the two expected resources; `verify-router-sync.cjs` check 4 prints `PASS check 4` and the suite prints `5/5 checks passed`. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | notApplicable | No feature-catalog entry changes in this diff; the chart corpus and diagram feature catalogs are untouched. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pass | The five new changelogs exist; the canonical agent and four mirrors carry the new decide path (iteration 1 evidence). |\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- The phase summaries record `validate.sh --strict` results that this lineage is forbidden to\\n  rerun. The review therefore checks the recorded evidence's specificity and cross-document\\n  agreement, and does not claim the gate was re-observed. That is the same standard the packet's\\n  own \\\"Known Limitations\\\" rows use.\\n- `specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/` is untracked in this worktree, so git cannot show\\n  an intra-packet delta. Baseline comparison is against `10474a9567` for the repo files and\\n  against the packet's own text for the untracked docs.\\n- The phase-2 file table's folder row shows as \\\"not changed\\\" in `git status` only because git\\n  lists the deleted files individually; that is not a false claim.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- The five baseline value prompts named in the phase-1 brief all route to `sk-code-frontend`:\\n  padding, type scale, palette, \\\"why does this screen look wrong\\\" and dropdown animation.\\n- The four chart files keep the three rule groups the changelog names: the role split figures,\\n  the radar/pie decision and the stacked-area one-row card.\\n- All five new changelogs exist and carry the version they announce.\\n- The three new references have the counts the acceptance criteria claim (566, 618, 642 lines;\\n  40/21/21 hierarchy rows).\\n- `verify-router-sync.cjs` passes all five legs, including the replay of the new visual-values\\n  scenario.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **A wholesale false-files table in every phase.** Ruled out by row-by-row comparison; only one\\n  row is false.\\n- **A missing changelog or a version that disagrees with its changelog.** Ruled out by `ls` and\\n  `grep` on all five files.\\n- **A chart rule that lost its supporting figure.** Ruled out by reading the three rule groups\\n  against the removed citations.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\nDimension: maintainability. Check whether the canonical descriptions still match the new surface\\ncontent, whether any retired rule failed to move, and whether the new files' own structure is\\nsafe to change.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873520777,"end":1793873527784}}}}
