{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873558622,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab323af5001RN4sf0YCt43IJR","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab322a20001h0DS1hECXTD0By","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a06af652e2439452","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -n \"box-shadow\\|transition.*opacity\\|repaint\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md | sed -n '1,20p'"},"output":".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:268:- **Rule:** Decide the element's profile, then mimic how light would hit that shape. Light comes from above and people look slightly down at their screens, so the top edge of a raised element is visible and the bottom edge of an inset one is. Each element needs both the lit edge and the blocked light in a single comma-separated `box-shadow`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:269:- **Why:** Borrow the real-world cue and stop, because depth comes from mimicking one light source consistently, not from chasing photorealism. Raised and inset are the same trick. Two `box-shadow` declarations on one selector do not combine, and the second silently discards the first.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:279:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:286:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:292:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:306:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:328:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:357:  box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:455:- **Rule:** Contain user-uploaded content in fixed-size containers with `background-size: cover`, cropping the overflow. Prevent background bleed, where a user photo's edges match the UI background, with a subtle inset shadow such as `box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px hsla(0,0%,0%,.1)` rather than a border. For photography itself, use a photographer or good stock and never design against placeholders while planning to shoot something on a phone later.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md:307:- **When not to:** Use a large blur once on a static decorative layer that never repaints.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md:308:- **Pitfall:** A blurred backdrop on a scrolling header repaints on every frame.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:268:- **Rule:** Decide the element's profile, then mimic how light would hit that shape. Light comes from above and people look slightly down at their screens, so the top edge of a raised element is visible and the bottom edge of an inset one is. Each element needs both the lit edge and the blocked light in a single comma-separated `box-shadow`.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:269:- **Why:** Borrow the real-world cue and stop, because depth comes from mimicking one light source consistently, not from chasing photorealism. Raised and inset are the same trick. Two `box-shadow` declarations on one selector do not combine, and the second silently discards the first.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:279:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:286:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:292:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:306:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:328:box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:357:  box-shadow:\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md:455:- **Rule:** Contain user-uploaded content in fixed-size containers with `background-size: cover`, cropping the overflow. Prevent background bleed, where a user photo's edges match the UI background, with a subtle inset shadow such as `box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px hsla(0,0%,0%,.1)` rather than a border. For photography itself, use a photographer or good stock and never design against placeholders while planning to shoot something on a phone later.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md:307:- **When not to:** Use a large blur once on a static decorative layer that never repaints.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md:308:- **Pitfall:** A blurred backdrop on a scrolling header repaints on every frame.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -n \\\"box-shadow\\\\|transition.*opacity\\\\|repaint\\\" .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-visual-values.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-frontend/references/web-motion-and-interaction.md | sed -n '1,20p'\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873558261,"end":1793873558622}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873558625,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab3239bf002003J3slbOJGp0W","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab322a20001h0DS1hECXTD0By","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b913964fd87da37a","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -n '\"description\"\\|\"lastUpdated\"' .skilled/skills/sk-code/description.json; sed -n '40,52p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md; sed -n '112,118p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md"},"output":"3:  \"description\": \"Coding standards, references, and assets for this framework's own system code. Provides surface-aware code-quality patterns, checklists, and verification recipes for OpenCode system code (JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Shell, JSON/JSONC, MCP server code, agents, commands, skills). Smart-routing internals detect the active stack and load matching standards; unsupported stacks ask for disambiguation. Its surface axis bundles the CI, frontend (web and Figma-to-code) and SKILLED evidence packets.\",\n40:  \"lastUpdated\": \"2026-10-10T00:00:00Z\"\n\n| Surface | Carries | Packet |\n|---------|---------|--------|\n| **sk-code-ci** | GitHub Actions evidence: trigger, filter, permission, timeout, concurrency and caching rules, the protected set, the intentional message-contract exception and the scaffold templates, with the repository-specific values read from a CI profile. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-ci/` |\n| **sk-code-frontend** | Stack-agnostic frontend evidence: web markup and CSS, web layout and accessibility, and Figma-to-code checks. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-frontend/` |\n| **sk-code-skilled** | System-code evidence: TypeScript/Python/shell/config standards, hooks, alignment verification, authoring checklists. Bundles the implement → debug → verify workflow doctrine (read-only evidence) for the Skilled surface, and the acting agent applies it. | `sk-code/sk-code-skilled/` |\n\n**Surface list.** The hub has exactly three surfaces:\n- SKILLED (`sk-code-skilled`): the native surface for this framework's own code.\n- CI (`sk-code-ci`): the GitHub Actions workflow standards surface.\n- Frontend (`sk-code-frontend`): the stack-agnostic web practice and Figma-to-code surface, bundled from request vocabulary alone.\n\nThe hub also has two workflow modes: quality (`sk-code-quality`) and review (`sk-code-review`).\n  sk-code-quality/       # quality mode packet     (workflow)\n  sk-code-review/        # review mode packet      (workflow)\n  sk-code-ci/            # GitHub Actions workflow standards packet (read-only evidence; rules, protected set and scaffold templates)\n  sk-code-frontend/      # stack-agnostic web and Figma-to-code evidence packet (read-only)\n  sk-code-skilled/      # skilled surface packet (read-only evidence; carries the workflow doctrine)\n  shared/                # shared surface-detection router, cross-mode helpers, and the implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine (references/workflow-*.md)\n```\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:  \"description\": \"Coding standards, references, and assets for this framework's own system code. Provides surface-aware code-quality patterns, checklists, and verification recipes for OpenCode system code (JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, Shell, JSON/JSONC, MCP server code, agents, commands, skills). Smart-routing internals detect the active stack and load matching standards; unsupported stacks ask for disambiguation. Its surface axis bundles the CI, frontend (web and Figma-to-code) and SKILLED evidence packets.\",\n40:  \"lastUpdated\": \"2026-10-10T00:00:00Z\"\n\n| Surface | Carries | Packet |\n|---------|---------|--------|\n| **sk-code-ci** | GitHub Actions evidence: trigger, filter, permission, timeout, concurrency and caching rules, the protected set, the intentional message-contract exception and the scaffold templates, with the repository-specific values read from a CI profile. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-ci/` |\n| **sk-code-frontend** | Stack-agnostic frontend evidence: web markup and CSS, web layout and accessibility, and Figma-to-code checks. Read-only. | `sk-code/sk-code-frontend/` |\n| **sk-code-skilled** | System-code evidence: TypeScript/Python/shell/config standards, hooks, alignment verification, authoring checklists. Bundles the implement → debug → verify workflow doctrine (read-only evidence) for the Skilled surface, and the acting agent applies it. | `sk-code/sk-code-skilled/` |\n\n**Surface list.** The hub has exactly three surfaces:\n- SKILLED (`sk-code-skilled`): the native surface for this framework's own code.\n- CI (`sk-code-ci`): the GitHub Actions workflow standards surface.\n- Frontend (`sk-code-frontend`): the stack-agnostic web practice and Figma-to-code surface, bundled from request vocabulary alone.\n\nThe hub also has two workflow modes: quality (`sk-code-quality`) and review (`sk-code-review`).\n  sk-code-quality/       # quality mode packet     (workflow)\n  sk-code-review/        # review mode packet      (workflow)\n  sk-code-ci/            # GitHub Actions workflow standards packet (read-only evidence; rules, protected set and scaffold templates)\n  sk-code-frontend/      # stack-agnostic web and Figma-to-code evidence packet (read-only)\n  sk-code-skilled/      # skilled surface packet (read-only evidence; carries the workflow doctrine)\n  shared/                # shared surface-detection router, cross-mode helpers, and the implement/debug/verify workflow doctrine (references/workflow-*.md)\n```\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals && grep -n '\\\"description\\\"\\\\|\\\"lastUpdated\\\"' .skilled/skills/sk-code/description.json; sed -n '40,52p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md; sed -n '112,118p' .skilled/skills/sk-code/SKILL.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873557951,"end":1793873558625}}}}
