{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1793873753943,"sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","part":{"partID":"prt_1ab353199001Y8fHYklsZRsNwF","sessionID":"ses_e54d7f46fffe0ZLISbmnuV6zfy","messageID":"msg_1ab352538001lGBvvxwLL46Fuu","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b25e9b8b320faa70","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading the compiled-route decision for exact prompts exposed a route the prose claimed but the\n  contract did not produce (iterations 1 and 5).\n- `git show 10474a9567:<path>` against the current tree mapped every retired reference heading to\n  its new V/H/M item and found the one missing section (iteration 3).\n- Comparing every changed-file row against `git status` isolated the single false summary row\n  (iteration 2).\n- Running the reducer after each gateway append kept the registry, dashboard and strategy in step\n  with the five iteration records.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Treating a documented keyword as reachable. The hub vocabulary listed the phrase; the tie-break\n  sent it to a different mode (iteration 1, confirmed in iteration 5).\n- Treating the packet's changed-file table as an audit trail before checking it (iteration 2).\n- Assuming the consolidated references carried every retired section; one performance technique\n  had no successor (iteration 3).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -59,15 +59,26 @@\n \n <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading the compiled-route decision for exact prompts exposed a route the prose claimed but the\n+  contract did not produce (iterations 1 and 5).\n+- `git show 10474a9567:<path>` against the current tree mapped every retired reference heading to\n+  its new V/H/M item and found the one missing section (iteration 3).\n+- Comparing every changed-file row against `git status` isolated the single false summary row\n+  (iteration 2).\n+- Running the reducer after each gateway append kept the registry, dashboard and strategy in step\n+  with the five iteration records.\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Treating a documented keyword as reachable. The hub vocabulary listed the phrase; the tie-break\n+  sent it to a different mode (iteration 1, confirmed in iteration 5).\n+- Treating the packet's changed-file table as an audit trail before checking it (iteration 2).\n+- Assuming the consolidated references carried every retired section; one performance technique\n+  had no successor (iteration 3).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":13,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Reading the compiled-route decision for exact prompts exposed a route the prose claimed but the\\n  contract did not produce (iterations 1 and 5).\\n- `git show 10474a9567:<path>` against the current tree mapped every retired reference heading to\\n  its new V/H/M item and found the one missing section (iteration 3).\\n- Comparing every changed-file row against `git status` isolated the single false summary row\\n  (iteration 2).\\n- Running the reducer after each gateway append kept the registry, dashboard and strategy in step\\n  with the five iteration records.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Treating a documented keyword as reachable. The hub vocabulary listed the phrase; the tie-break\\n  sent it to a different mode (iteration 1, confirmed in iteration 5).\\n- Treating the packet's changed-file table as an audit trail before checking it (iteration 2).\\n- Assuming the consolidated references carried every retired section; one performance technique\\n  had no successor (iteration 3).\", \"oldString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\", \"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/316-deprecate-design-fundamentals/specs/sk-design/021-deprecate-fundamentals/review/lineages/deepseek/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1793873752473,"end":1793873753943}}}}
